e of their surroundings and quickly fade into the walls ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T11:40:12-08:00","id":1366361,"title":"","content":"How can a ghost return from the underworld?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T02:05:12-08:00","id":1366716,"title":"","content":"I have no idea how is it portrayed in the new edition but is eating ghosts, like, evil?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","name":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T02:33:46-08:00","id":1366717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1366716#post1366716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea how is it portrayed in the new edition but is eating ghosts, like, evil?</div> </div> </div> </div>You loose Synergy per Rank of the Ghost that was eaten. Furthermore it is compared to cannibalism. (Page 95, Loosing Synergy)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T02:37:34-08:00","id":1366719,"title":"","content":"Oh, that makes sense. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","name":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T02:40:41-08:00","id":1366720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1366361#post1366361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can a ghost return from the underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pick the lock with a meaningful and heart-stirring ritual celebration of life.<br /> Gather enough overwhelming, explosive force to smash the gate open.<br /> Drink from the Rivers of the Underworld and become a geist, sacrificing some measure of your humanity for alien Essence.<br /> Search the shores of the Rivers for a Deathmask and become a reaper, obtaining freedom to leave in exchange for a promise to capture others.<br /> <br /> If you have lost your Anchors, any of these methods except the reaper one is taking a gamble, because you're going to bleed Essence fast up there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1366716#post1366716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea how is it portrayed in the new edition but is eating ghosts, like, evil?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts think thoughts and feel feelings. Ghosts are people and, consequentially, eating them is bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T02:57:27-08:00","id":1366724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1366720#post1366720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gather enough overwhelming, explosive force to smash the gate open.<br /> Drink from the Rivers of the Underworld and become a geist, sacrificing some measure of your humanity for alien Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know where I can read more about the details?<br /> On smashing the gate open?<br /> Why can a Ghost with Rank 3 leave!? What usually prevents other ghosts from doing the same. etc.<br /> <br /> Could also a Demon from Inferno \u201csomehow\u201d help with that? (Asmodeus)<br /> I know they can\u2019t leave themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T03:10:12-08:00","id":1366725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1366724#post1366724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you know where I can read more about the details?<br /> On smashing the gate open?<br /> Why can a Ghost with Rank 3 leave!? What usually prevents other ghosts from doing the same. etc.<br /> <br /> Could also a Demon from Inferno \u201csomehow\u201d help with that? (Asmodeus)<br /> I know they can\u2019t leave themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can read about crossing back through Avernian Gates to the living world on Geist Second Edition, p. 200. There's not much detail to smashing the gate open, just: if you can manage an improbable amount of physical damage to the gate, you can smash through.<br /> Geists hold Keys to death, the same Keys that Sin-Eaters use to unlock their Haunts. The Keys can also be used to unlock Avernian Gates.<br /> It's plausible that infernal powers could get a ghost out of the Underworld, if you're able to invoke the right demon. The limits of demonic investments are pretty flexible and ambiguously defined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T05:55:32-08:00","id":1366749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1366725#post1366725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's plausible that infernal powers could get a ghost out of the Underworld, if you're able to invoke the right demon. The limits of demonic investments are pretty flexible and ambiguously defined.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ghost worshiped the demon in life by torturing and killing people. So the if the ghost can\u2019t return without changing who he was, this might be the best option, I guess. In the story the ghost wants to finish what he started.<br /> <br /> \u2014<br /> <br /> 1) If I want to give him the numen \u201cHost Jump\u201d, I think he needs to be Rank 4, because he needs to be able to create new anchors!? Or does he need to be Rank 5, because one Influence is always \u201cAnchors\u201d (I guess this means his personal type of anchor)!? <br /> <br /> 2) I am also not sure, what kind of Influence would be suitable for this. Maybe a certain type of characters that he can claim. (He will use people for a longer period of time to commit his new crimes.) <br /> <br /> 3) At the moment I think, that I need the players (or one of them) to become sin-eaters at one point in the story. Because nothing is preventing the ghost from coming back later, if not all of his essence and corpus is empty at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T11:01:45-08:00","id":1366811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1366720#post1366720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have lost your Anchors, any of these methods except the reaper one is taking a gamble, because you're going to bleed Essence fast up there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Becoming a geist is also less of a gamble for this reason, but the specific limitations of being a geist mean you're probably going to want to make a Bargain if you intend to have someone intelligible to help you with whatever unfinished business was worth drinking fire, bones, scorpions, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1366749#post1366749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) If I want to give him the numen \u201cHost Jump\u201d, I think he needs to be Rank 4, because he needs to be able to create new anchors!? Or does he need to be Rank 5, because one Influence is always \u201cAnchors\u201d (I guess this means his personal type of anchor)!?</div> </div> </div> </div>Plasm turns whatever it's covering Open for a chapter and forms whenever any ghost Manifests.<br /> <br /> Basically any ghost that has reached higher than Rank 2 is not going to have Influence: Anchors above a rating of 2, because that Rank is either temporary or comes with a reorientation of their Influence around Keys.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) I am also not sure, what kind of Influence would be suitable for this. Maybe a certain type of characters that he can claim. (He will use people for a longer period of time to commit his new crimes.) </div> </div> </div>Becoming a ghost's Anchor after the fact of their formation is usually a deliberate act of Ceremony that can only be done by the living or the Bound.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) At the moment I think, that I need the players (or one of them) to become sin-eaters at one point in the story. Because nothing is preventing the ghost from coming back later, if not all of his essence and corpus is empty at the same time. </div> </div> </div>If he's not a Reaper or a geist and he gets discorporated without an Anchor, he's going back to the Underworld and will have the same difficulties he had getting back the first time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T14:31:20-08:00","id":1366862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1366811#post1366811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plasm turns whatever it's covering Open for a chapter and forms whenever any ghost Manifests.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what Rank does a Ghost require to use \u201cHost Jump\u201d?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1366811#post1366811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically any ghost that has reached higher than Rank 2 is not going to have Influence: Anchors above a rating of 2, because that Rank is either temporary or comes with a reorientation of their Influence around Keys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure what you mean. Why does the rating of anchors needs to become higher? <br /> Geists and Reapers are Rank 3 and don\u2019t need anchors, and don\u2019t suffer from essence bleed without them. Therefore I presume that\u2019s true for every Ghost of Rank 3 or higher.<br /> <br /> And what do you mean by \u201creorientation\u201d? (I didn\u2019t finish the book by now. Still reading.) Does every Ghost at Rank 3 get keys? Even Reapers?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1366811#post1366811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Becoming a ghost's Anchor after the fact of their formation is usually a deliberate act of Ceremony that can only be done by the living or the Bound.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the victim needs to get the open condition by a Ghost using Plasm? Is that the only way to get possessed or claimed?<br /> (Can every Ghost of Rank 3 or higher use Plasm? And where can I find what you mentioned about Anchors?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1366811#post1366811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If he's not a Reaper or a geist and he gets discorporated without an Anchor, he's going back to the Underworld and will have the same difficulties he had getting back the first time.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Ghost is Rank 3 or higher, I would guess that he is identical in that way to Geists and Reapers. Sadly the rules, that I have read so far, only seem to cover Geist and Reapers and not other Ghosts with a higher Rank. <br /> (Anyway that guy would do anything to \u201cfinish\u201d his job. So he would come back, sooner or later. Even as a Reaper, if that\u2019s what it takes.)<br /> <br /> \u2014\u2014<br /> <br /> I am also still looking for a suitable Influence for that ghost!??<br /> <br /> ====<br /> <br /> Sorry for asking a lot of questions..<br /> I have still a lot of difficulties to understand the rules for ghosts and other ephemeral entities. \ud83e\udd17","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":1825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","user":"Elythia","date":". 02-10-2020, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T14:54:41-08:00","id":1366866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1366862#post1366862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what Rank does a Ghost require to use \u201cHost Jump\u201d?</div> </div> </div> </div>1.<br /> <br /> It may not necessarily have the rest of the toolkit needed for it to be practically usable without ritual assistance, but the only requirement for a ghost to have and use Host Jump is the Possess Manifestation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am not sure what you mean. Why does the rating of anchors needs to become higher? </div> </div> </div>This was a literal response to your supposition that a ghost would need to be high-Rank because of Influence: Anchors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Geists and Reapers are Rank 3 and don\u2019t need anchors, and don\u2019t suffer from essence bleed without them. Therefore I presume that\u2019s true for every Ghost of Rank 3 or higher. </div> </div> </div>The only hypothetical examples of Rank 3+ ghosts that aren't geists, Reapers, Kerberoi, or weird one-off exceptional phenomena are Rank 2 Doppelgangers who have consumed their duplicates. There is no reason to presume high Rank makes you immune to Essence bleed just because the main things that are immune to Essence bleed are high-Rank with strings attached.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what do you mean by \u201creorientation\u201d? (I didn\u2019t finish the book by now. Still reading.) Does every Ghost at Rank 3 get keys? Even Reapers? </div> </div> </div>A geist changes out all of its Influence dots for its Rank in Influence [Innate Key] and a Reaper adds specific dots of Influence based on the Deathmask it's using to the ghost's own stats (multiple examples of which suggest that most Reapers gain Influences from or along the thematic lines of Keys); the Reaper's extra dots go away when they remove the mask. None of these allow for the broad-scope Influence over &quot;things that are this ghost's Anchors&quot; to be raised to the level of a Create or Mass Create Influence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the victim needs to get the open condition by using plasm? Is that the only way to get possessed or claimed? </div> </div> </div>It is a more broadly accessible way for ghosts to affect things besides their Anchors than a powerful Ceremony that they can't use themselves, and Anchors are highly limited in number without that assistance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Ghost is Rank 3 or higher, I would guess that he is identical in that way to Geists and Reapers. Sadly the rules, that I have read so far, only seem to cover Geist and Reapers and not other Ghosts with a higher Rank. </div> </div> </div>See &quot;reorientation.&quot; Being part of the apparatus by which the Underworld makes beachheads in the land of the living comes with a higher Rank, but the reverse is not inherently true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T02:42:19-08:00","id":1366935,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your answers Satchel, even though I have difficulties to follow all of your thoughts.. \ud83e\udd14<br /> I am looking for help to make my story work. Please keep that in mind while answering. \ud83e\udd17<br /> <br /> 1) a) What Rank does a Ghost need to use \u201cHost Jump\u201d -without help- to \u201cclaim\u201c a victim?<br /> b) What does he need to do? (Is there more than one way?) <br /> <br /> 2) Why can\u2019t a Ghost use \u201cInfluence - Create\u201d to make a person an anchor? (Page in the book?)<br /> <br /> 3) Why doesn\u2019t a Ghost need an anchor, if it\u2019s not the Rank? (They don\u2019t even need anchors without the Bargain.)<br /> <br /> 4) What would you recommend for the story, if you don\u2019t want to change the personality of the Ghost too much?<br /> (He needs to be able to leave the Underworld, have or make time to find a host, and be able to do a \u201eHost Jump\u201c and \u201eClaim\u201c his victims.)<br /> <br /> He might get the support of Asmodeus. This would be be a unique way to increase his Rank, leave the Underworld etc. if there is no other solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":1825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","user":"Elythia","date":". 02-11-2020, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T03:59:01-08:00","id":1366942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1366935#post1366935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Why can\u2019t a Ghost use \u201cInfluence - Create\u201d to make a person an anchor? (Page in the book?)</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW: They can.<br /> RAI: It probably varies. Influences and Anchors are just messy because ghosts were originally meant to have &quot;Anchors&quot; as an Influence (implying that only that Influence would be used to actually create Anchors) but for the longest time the only example ghost had only a thematic Influence. Then Geist 2e came along and started assigning <i>specific Anchors</i> as Influences.<br /> It's such a fucking mess. There's no internal bible used by the writers for CofD so everyone needs to base their writings on the released books, except they are often vague or subtly change from game to game or just aren't available for a specific writer which just snowballs into even more and more inconsistencies because different writers have different interpretations. And then the players are supposed to interpret those varying intentions and phrasings and examples into a singular rules system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-11-2020, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T04:54:50-08:00","id":1366947,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I didn't mean to mix &quot;Ghost&quot; and &quot;Geist&quot; up. In German, the word for ghost is &quot;Geist&quot;... \ud83d\ude06<br /> 3) I was wondering what might cause a \u201eGeist\u201c to not need anchors anymore. I assumed it was the Rank because I couldn't find anything else so far. But Satchel seemed to have another theory. \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> But in the end, I simply want to know the options that I have to tell the story. \ud83e\udd17","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T07:31:38-08:00","id":1366970,"title":"","content":"I meant to quote your second point. That's what I replied to. Gonna edit that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T08:13:36-08:00","id":1366979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1366970#post1366970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant to quote your second point. That's what I replied to. Gonna edit that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, now it makes perfect sense.\ud83d\ude04<br /> I also found a helpful sentence in the books: &quot;Finally, a high-Rank ghost can use a Create Influence to mark a target as an Anchor.&quot; <br /> <br /> I think I will open a separate post since this seems to be more complex than I had hoped. \ud83d\ude43","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T08:28:04-08:00","id":1366984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1366935#post1366935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) a) What Rank does a Ghost need to use \u201cHost Jump\u201d -without help- to \u201cclaim\u201c a victim?</div> </div> </div> </div>2, with the caveat that most ghosts liable to run a Possess/Host Jump combination are more likely to be geists or Reapers, since Claim requires both Possess and Fetter, ghosts only get so many Manifestation effects for free, and every aspect of this set of effects is very expensive Essence-wise (which means being immune to Essence bleed helps a lot).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> b) What does he need to do? (Is there more than one way?) </div> </div> </div>With Plasm or Influence 3, a ghost can temporarily create the Open Condition on a subject without the underlying Anchor Condition; with Influence 3 or repeated Possession, a ghost can step the Open Condition up to Controlled, whereupon the subject can be Claimed, which halts the countdown on any of the supporting Conditions until/unless Claimed is resolved. As mentioned, this is an expensive process.<br /> <br /> A geist with a stock of corpses dead of its innate Key effectively has several no-strings-attached Anchors in the same way that most ghosts treat their own remains as an Anchor, which in turn allows it to Strengthen that facet of death into an Open Condition that can be leveraged for Manifestations like normal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Why can\u2019t a Ghost use \u201cInfluence - Create\u201d to make a person an anchor? (Page in the book?) </div> </div> </div>They can, but the problem is that the vast majority of the ways a ghost can reach the Rank necessary to have a Create Influence of any kind don't allow them to assign dots to Influence: Anchors.<br /> <br /> Practically every geist of a Rank higher than 3 can use the Influence of their innate Key to mark a person as an &quot;Anchor,&quot; but the way that works is through geists being &quot;Anchored&quot; to a form of death rather than anything relating to them on a personal level. Meanwhile, Reapers have the stats of a Rank 2 ghost when they haven't got the mask on, and putting the mask on adds dots in Influences they probably don't already have, which is unlikely to put them at Influence 4 in anything.<br /> <br /> Influence: Anchors is mostly important to low-Rank ghosts because it allows them to affect all their Anchors with that Influence even if they aren't the same type of thing otherwise. It's no more essential to the Manifestation system than it would be for angels to have Influence: Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Why doesn\u2019t a <s>Ghost</s>Geist need an anchor, if it\u2019s not the Rank? (They don\u2019t even need anchors without the Bargain.) </div> </div> </div>Because they drank from the Rivers and got Broken in such a fashion that they specifically don't have their one-to-three-average personal Anchors anymore \u2014 the narrative role their Anchors played for them is now handled by their Remembrances and the metaphysical role their Anchors played for them is now handled by their innate Keys.<br /> <br /> Geists on their own and Reapers working to plan are ludonarratively set up to spread death in the living world, albeit in different ways; their freedom to leave the Underworld and safely venture beyond any Anchors they have is there in part to allow Reapers to be subtle threats and in part to allow geists to not be hemmed in geographically by their Keys the way ghosts are by their Anchors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) What would you recommend for the story, if you don\u2019t want to change the personality of the Ghost too much?<br /> (He needs to be able to leave the Underworld, have or make time to find a host, and be able to do a \u201eHost Jump\u201c and \u201eClaim\u201c his victims.) </div> </div> </div>Make him a geist whose innate Key is the Key of Blood (or whatever other Key is appropriate to his methods) and give him a Remembrance relating to the demon; it's already textual that necromancers can jump straight to geisthood when they die and &quot;finish what I started&quot; is a pretty definite goal to work towards.<br /> <br /> Why are Claim and Host Jump necessary for this concept?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T09:11:25-08:00","id":1366999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1366935#post1366935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Why doesn\u2019t a [geist] need an anchor, if it\u2019s not the Rank? (They don\u2019t even need anchors without the Bargain.)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1366984#post1366984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they drank from the Rivers and got Broken in such a fashion that they specifically don't have their one-to-three-average personal Anchors anymore \u2014 the narrative role their Anchors played for them is now handled by their Remembrances and the metaphysical role their Anchors played for them is now handled by their innate Keys.<br /> <br /> Geists on their own and Reapers working to plan are ludonarratively set up to spread death in the living world, albeit in different ways; their freedom to leave the Underworld and safely venture beyond any Anchors they have is there in part to allow Reapers to be subtle threats and in part to allow geists to not be hemmed in geographically by their Keys the way ghosts are by their Anchors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here we have a potentially jarring gameplay and story dissonance. Narratively speaking a ghost becomes a Geist by drinking from one of the Rivers of the Underworld until they are changed and gain a Rank. Mechanically speaking a ghost becomes a Geist by reaching Rank 3.<br /> The dissonance comes from the possibility for ghosts to drink from a River without reaching Rank 3 (and thus not becoming a Geist), as well for ghosts to reach Rank 3 through means other than drinking from a River (thus becoming Geister despite not having gone through the process that is supposed to turn them into Geister).<br /> <br /> Narratively speaking, the need for Anchors doesn't necessarily correspond to the ghost's Rank, but mechanically speaking it definitely is tied because Rank is used to determine if a ghost is a Geist or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T10:53:02-08:00","id":1367035,"title":"","content":"As mentioned before, this seems to be more complicated than expected.<br /> Therefore I created a separate topic for it:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1367034-creating-a-ghost-similar-to-the-one-in-what-the-night-knows-by-dean-koontz\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1367034-creating-a-ghost-similar-to-the-one-in-what-the-night-knows-by-dean-koontz\"> Creating a Ghost similar to the one in \"What the night knows\" by Dean Koontz - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1367034-creating-a-ghost-similar-to-the-one-in-what-the-night-knows-by-dean-koontz\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1367034-creating-a-ghost-similar-to-the-one-in-what-the-night-knows-by-dean-koontz </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Goal I want to create a Ghost, similar to the one in the story &amp;quot;What the night knows&amp;quot; by Dean Koontz. My group is playing a similar story right now. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> (I also provided more background information etc. there.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T16:01:12-08:00","id":1368814,"title":"","content":"How would I build Talion from Shadow of War? And then what would I have to change to make him in the epilogue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T08:16:24-08:00","id":1368933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HunterInTheNight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1368814#post1368814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would I build Talion from Shadow of War? And then what would I have to change to make him in the epilogue?</div> </div> </div> </div>Choose Vengeful, with Marionette, Rage, and Curse. Keys included Stigmata and Cold-Wind, but later included Beast, Disease, and Pyre-Flame. Might also take the Dread Geist merit to emphasize the history and power behind Celebrimbor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T09:30:37-08:00","id":1369142,"title":"","content":"I just never saw stigmata in his skills.<br /> And I'm not sure, but would Memoria, Oracle, and/or shroud work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T11:29:33-08:00","id":1369162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HunterInTheNight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1369142#post1369142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just never saw stigmata in his skills.<br /> And I'm not sure, but would Memoria, Oracle, and/or shroud work?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would! Especially if it works like psychometry. And shroud would work to represent his ability to stay sneaky stealthy in bushes!<br /> As for Stigmata, remember the means by which he died? Ritual sacrifice after witnessing the deaths of both his wife and son.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T09:07:47-08:00","id":1370067,"title":"","content":"My Geist PDF (Kickstarter) still includes p. XX, instead of a real page reference. Is the final version already out, and if so where can I find it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T09:49:28-08:00","id":1370076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1370067#post1370067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Geist PDF (Kickstarter) still includes p. XX, instead of a real page reference. Is the final version already out</div> </div> </div> </div>p.XX means the answer is &quot;no.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and if so where can I find it? </div> </div> </div>Per <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/geist-the-sin-eaters-2nd-edition/posts/2755683\" target=\"_blank\">the most recent update</a> on the Kickstarter page:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll note there are a handful of stragglers that'll take a nudge or two, and a few labels that we've still got to sort, but 99% of backers will be able to read Geist: The Sin-Eaters Second Edition by February 29th, which is Leap Day (so celebrate like you do only every 4 years!) </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T01:53:23-08:00","id":1370271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1370076#post1370076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">p.XX means the answer is &amp;quot;no.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Per <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/geist-the-sin-eaters-2nd-edition/posts/2755683&amp;quot;]the</a> most recent update[/URL] on the Kickstarter page:<br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! \ud83d\ude42","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T15:54:11-08:00","id":1370464,"title":"","content":"A very simple question guys and girls: do you think that GtS suits well as a &quot;solo game&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T19:44:27-08:00","id":1370489,"title":"","content":"Based on idea that Krewes are assumed to be build by many characters - I doubt it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T20:31:26-08:00","id":1370498,"title":"","content":"The dramatic failure for <i>Lay the Curse</i> (p106) includes &quot;the Sin-Eater suffers the effects of the Curse until the end of the scene.&quot;<br /> <br /> How does that work, if the &quot;effects&quot; are applied as reflexive actions <i>after</i> the Curse is laid (until charges are spent)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25989-primal-zed","name":"Primal Zed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25989_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T06:01:43-08:00","id":1370539,"title":"","content":"The ST gets to use the charges against the Sin-Eater until either the charges run out or the scene ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T01:22:45-08:00","id":1372233,"title":"","content":"I was wondering if angels and spirits can work as antagonists to Sin-eaters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T03:39:02-08:00","id":1372243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1372233#post1372233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering if angels and spirits can work as antagonists to Sin-eaters.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can for blue book characters so mechanically speaking they should for Sin-Eaters as well. Just be mindful of how it diverges from GtSE's otherwise quite strong focus on ghosts and the Underworld, and that it might break the players' expectations of the game in a bad way. I would recommend working it into the Remembrance of one or several of the PC's Geists to build a natural connection between the antagonist(s) and the PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T14:22:27-07:00","id":1374229,"title":"","content":"Some of the 3-dot Haunt enhancements give more charges:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Free:</b> The Curse Condition has two charges per Plasm spent on Lay the Curse. </div> </div> </div>Is this additive to the charges gained from Lay the Curse (for a total of 3 charges per plasm spent) or does it replace charges gained from Lay the Curse (for a total of 2 charges per plasm spent)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25989-primal-zed","name":"Primal Zed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25989_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T14:33:27-07:00","id":1374230,"title":"","content":"My assumption has been replace, not additive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T15:11:23-07:00","id":1374237,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Curse Condition <b>has</b> two charges [..]&quot;<br /> <br /> It <b>sets</b> it to two charges per Plasm; not adds two additional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T02:25:42-07:00","id":1374523,"title":"","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> I'm working (just to kill time, sadly) on a geist made of smoke. It died in a fire (maybe accidental), however not the fire, but heat and smoke killed it. Do you have any idea about a good ban and bane?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T20:07:06-07:00","id":1375743,"title":"","content":"Do final breaking points involved in a character's death impact their ghost-Integrity (thus not impacting Rank) or their pre-death Integrity (thus impacting Rank)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Starting Rank: Most ghosts are created at Rank 1 (if they died with an Integrity of 6 or lower) or Rank 2 (if they died with an Integrity of 7-9). </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fixed at Death: A ghost\u2019s Integrity is a holdover from her living self, set at the level she had before death, <b>barring</b> any final breaking point </div> </div> </div>A character with 7 Integrity kills themselves. As part of that final act, they suffer a breaking point, which they fail. Is the result:<br /> <br /> 1) A Rank 2 Ghost with 6 Integrity<br /> 2) A Rank 2 Ghost with 7 Integrity<br /> 3) A Rank 1 Ghost with 6 Integrity<br /> 4) A Rank 1 Ghost with 7 Integrity","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T21:02:58-07:00","id":1375746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1375743#post1375743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do final breaking points involved in a character's death impact their ghost-Integrity (thus not impacting Rank) or their pre-death Integrity (thus impacting Rank)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it'd have to be pre-death, because ghost-Integrity has its own breaking points to deal with and the roll for that involves a different stat that living characters with Integrity don't have.<br /> <br /> Considering the likely causes of a &quot;final breaking point&quot; for a character in the immediate process of dying, I feel it's germane to point out that &quot;this is the ghost of someone who died in a traumatic way and didn't take it well&quot; fits much better with Rank 1 ghosts than Rank 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","ti