er/26065-noahjam325-gmail-com","name":"[email\u00a0protected]","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T06:11:40-07:00","id":1392177,"title":"","content":"I am reading \u201eDeath is Not the End\u201c (A Geist: The Sin-Eaters Second Edition Anthology). In one of those stories a ghost and also a Reaper disappears in front of a Sin-Eater, just to be back moments later. (In my opinion a Ghost is always visible to a Sin-Eater, even in twilight.)<br /> <br /> Question: Is that possible? If yes, how?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T06:29:56-07:00","id":1392181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1392177#post1392177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am reading \u201eDeath is Not the End\u201c (A Geist: The Sin-Eaters Second Edition Anthology). In one of those stories a ghost and also a Reaper disappears in front of a Sin-Eater, just to be back moments later. (In my opinion a Ghost is always visible to a Sin-Eater, even in twilight.)<br /> <br /> Question: Is that possible? If yes, how?</div> </div> </div> </div>A powerful illusion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T08:30:25-07:00","id":1394565,"title":"","content":"I literally started reading Geist's ruilebook today, so this question might seem something I obviously overlooked. Can Geists speak? Like vocalise and understand English? Can a Sin-Eater communicate with their Geist when its unleashed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26181-malksam","name":"MalkSam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T16:07:35-07:00","id":1394648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalkSam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1394565#post1394565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I literally started reading Geist's ruilebook today, so this question might seem something I obviously overlooked. Can Geists speak? Like vocalise and understand English? Can a Sin-Eater communicate with their Geist when its unleashed?</div> </div> </div> </div>It s not clear to me too, but the mental faculty and skills of the geist are not diminished by the drink of the river waters.<br /> That said, their mindset is completely alien to human mind.<br /> So i think they can talk, but &quot;in a strange way&quot;, sometime mysterious and sometimes inchoerent (to the sin eater).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T21:31:23-07:00","id":1395230,"title":"","content":"They can certainly communicate, but it varies on the Geist specifically for how they go about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T21:48:25-07:00","id":1395234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1394648#post1394648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It s not clear to me too, but the mental faculty and skills of the geist are not diminished by the drink of the river waters.<br /> That said, their mindset is completely alien to human mind.<br /> So i think they can talk, but &amp;quot;in a strange way&amp;quot;, sometime mysterious and sometimes inchoerent (to the sin eater).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not completely. The rivers of the underworld may have twisted them, but the reason people even take the Bargain is because that alien thing has something undeniably human about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T22:11:52-07:00","id":1395239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalkSam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1394565#post1394565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I literally started reading Geist's ruilebook today, so this question might seem something I obviously overlooked. Can Geists speak? Like vocalise and understand English? Can a Sin-Eater communicate with their Geist when its unleashed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Their &quot;Broken&quot; quality means they roll a chance die for any Social action that doesn't have to do with terror and intimidation. Make of that what you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T00:24:44-07:00","id":1395260,"title":"","content":"So is there anything really mechanically stopping a Geist from just telling their Bound who they are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26181-malksam","name":"MalkSam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T01:34:00-07:00","id":1395267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalkSam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1395260#post1395260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is there anything really mechanically stopping a Geist from just telling their Bound who they are?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean who the geist was in life, it simply doesn t remember","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T07:09:25-07:00","id":1395339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalkSam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1395260#post1395260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is there anything really mechanically stopping a Geist from just telling their Bound who they are?</div> </div> </div> </div>They cannot meaningfully communicate or be communicated with in a complex manner and &quot;who they are&quot; is frequently going to be a complete stranger to their Bound in the first place. It's a metaphysically scarred super-ghost whose primary means of being stopped from acting out on its own is a roll heavily dependent upon its host's core-level relation to it and/or placating bribes. Remembrance tableaus are the most coherent clues you're likely to get from it in the normal course of play.<br /> <br /> They had to drink fire/scorpions/acid/raw hatred to become what they are, their voice isn't in the best of shape for self-introductions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T23:14:02-07:00","id":1395532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalkSam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1395260#post1395260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is there anything really mechanically stopping a Geist from just telling their Bound who they are?</div> </div> </div> </div>I started yesterday to read the geist fiction anthology by the way.<br /> It seems that geists can speak in complete phrases, in fact one of the Bound uses her own Geist to question herself using the Oracle haunt.<br /> That said, as Satchel said they are not great talkers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T07:02:41-07:00","id":1395589,"title":"","content":"What would a rank 1-2 Chthonian look like? Can/will Chthonian's communicate with anything other than their own kind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T00:20:33-07:00","id":1395777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1395589#post1395589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would a rank 1-2 Chthonian look like? Can/will Chthonian's communicate with anything other than their own kind?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think probably they would resemble a strange ocean deep creatures mix.<br /> For the comunication, probably their mind is too alien to speak with humans, maybe they can utter some word like kill or blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T00:23:56-07:00","id":1395779,"title":"","content":"The stygian treasure haunt enhancement has as an option &quot;anyone using the item can speak with the ghosts&quot;<br /> Considering that another option is hearing them, does this mean that ghosts in twilight cannot hear the living?<br /> Does any creature in twilight have the same problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T10:01:58-07:00","id":1396896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1395339#post1395339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They cannot meaningfully communicate or be communicated with in a complex manner and &quot;who they are&quot; is frequently going to be a complete stranger to their Bound in the first place. It's a metaphysically scarred super-ghost whose primary means of being stopped from acting out on its own is a roll heavily dependent upon its host's core-level relation to it and/or placating bribes. Remembrance tableaus are the most coherent clues you're likely to get from it in the normal course of play.<br /> <br /> They had to drink fire/scorpions/acid/raw hatred to become what they are, their voice isn't in the best of shape for self-introductions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My perception of it is as synergy grows and since the bound and their geist share a mind and a spiritual link, the bound can better communicate with his geist and even hallucinate some snippet of sentences that they gleans from their Geist. The bound may think they heard their geist poorly articulate a &quot;Behind you&quot; but any other observer would have heard the geist growl in a deep raspy voice","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T07:22:27-07:00","id":1397726,"title":"","content":"Just a curiosity, rules allow me to put all my three dots in a single haunt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T07:50:26-07:00","id":1397730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1397726#post1397726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a curiosity, rules allow me to put all my three dots in a single haunt?</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as that Haunt is one of your Burden's affinity Haunts, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T13:15:21-07:00","id":1397801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1395779#post1395779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The stygian treasure haunt enhancement has as an option &quot;anyone using the item can speak with the ghosts&quot;<br /> Considering that another option is hearing them, does this mean that ghosts in twilight cannot hear the living?<br /> Does any creature in twilight have the same problem?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not it means non medium cannot hear or speak with ghost, ghosts can hear the living just fine, that's the tragedy of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T16:23:28-07:00","id":1397840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1397801#post1397801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not it means non medium cannot hear or speak with ghost, ghosts can hear the living just fine, that's the tragedy of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why putting both the &quot;anyone using the item can speak with the ghosts&quot; and &quot;anyone using the item can hear the ghosts&quot;?<br /> If ghosts can already hear the living everyone can already speak with them, even if they cannot hear the replies.<br /> Maybe the hear the ghost option works with sounds made by the ghosts and the speak with ghosts option works only with words?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T02:31:35-07:00","id":1397933,"title":"","content":"Because this option is intended for the living, not for ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T03:33:40-07:00","id":1397938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1397933#post1397933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because this option is intended for the living, not for ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question is, why are those two different options if they effectively do the exact same thing? If ghosts naturally can hear you and you use the option to hear them, you can already communicate freely.<br /> What is the purpose of having &quot;speak to the dead&quot; as an option? Either it allows ghosts to hear you (which they already can) or it allows you to communicate back and forth with them, which you can already do with the previous option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T10:32:40-07:00","id":1398013,"title":"","content":"Ooooh i totally missed the point, huh, yeah it's strange<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T12:11:07-07:00","id":1398037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1398013#post1398013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooooh i totally missed the point, huh, yeah it's strange</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and then i ve found this quote on the core book<br /> &quot;To ghosts, material light sources are dimmed and sounds distorted as though underwater.&quot;.<br /> So i was wondering if ghosts are in fact able to hear clearly the livings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T00:07:24-07:00","id":1398724,"title":"","content":"I feel really dumb asking this, but here goes. As I read it, the dice pool to use a haunt is the sin-eaters Synergy + number of dots in the haunt. It feels like an attribute should be involved (similar to discipline use in Vampire). Otherwise a new SE will roll 2 dice and probably not activate a haunt. Is this correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24354-corbie","name":"Corbie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24354_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T00:57:32-07:00","id":1398731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corbie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1398724#post1398724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel really dumb asking this, but here goes. As I read it, the dice pool to use a haunt is the sin-eaters Synergy + number of dots in the haunt. It feels like an attribute should be involved (similar to discipline use in Vampire). Otherwise a new SE will roll 2 dice and probably not activate a haunt. Is this correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>But you have the option to open the haunt with a key, adding the correspondent attribute to the roll, and you start with at least two unlockable keys","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T13:02:26-07:00","id":1398857,"title":"","content":"Ooooh. I'd forgotten. On a first skim and still in that &quot;must learn vocabulary so I understand concepts&quot; stage. TY. I forgot you can use a key. Does that work even if the key isn't the right resonance? (Though they ought to be considering they reflect the build, right?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24354-corbie","name":"Corbie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24354_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T14:48:18-07:00","id":1398878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corbie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1398857#post1398857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooooh. I'd forgotten. On a first skim and still in that &amp;quot;must learn vocabulary so I understand concepts&amp;quot; stage. TY. I forgot you can use a key. Does that work even if the key isn't the right resonance? (Though they ought to be considering they reflect the build, right?)</div> </div> </div> </div>If i remember it rightly of you open a key without the resonance you simply gain the doomed condition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T14:56:40-07:00","id":1398880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1398878#post1398878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If i remember it rightly of you open a key without the resonance you simply gain the doomed condition</div> </div> </div> </div>The Doomed Condition for a Key happens if you don't either spend a Willpower to buy it off in the moment or roll an exceptional success to unlock the Haunt. If a use of a Haunt is resonant with the Key being used to unlock it, the roll is an exceptional success with three successes instead of five.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T15:49:48-07:00","id":1399928,"title":"","content":"Thanks for answering my question, everyone. I have another. What happens' to the Bound's body (the initial Bargain) if, say, it burned to a crisp in a fire or blew apart in an explosion? Does the Geist/Bargain reassemble the Sin-Eater? Is a 'reasonable facsimile' made?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24354-corbie","name":"Corbie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24354_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T22:50:28-07:00","id":1400244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corbie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1399928#post1399928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for answering my question, everyone. I have another. What happens' to the Bound's body (the initial Bargain) if, say, it burned to a crisp in a fire or blew apart in an explosion? Does the Geist/Bargain reassemble the Sin-Eater? Is a 'reasonable facsimile' made?</div> </div> </div> </div>They should be healed right up. Though, I admittedly dont know if they get blown to pieces. But I do know that if the body is fully intact, it should heal upon making the Bargain (if not instantly, then later through the use of Plasm)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T13:04:39-07:00","id":1401544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corbie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1399928#post1399928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for answering my question, everyone. I have another. What happens' to the Bound's body (the initial Bargain) if, say, it burned to a crisp in a fire or blew apart in an explosion? Does the Geist/Bargain reassemble the Sin-Eater? Is a 'reasonable facsimile' made?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm wrong, but from way I remember the Bargain don't heal the body, it just keep the death at bay, granting to the wounded body the time to heal by itself or to receive medical treatment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T06:49:59-07:00","id":1402405,"title":"","content":"This should be an easy question, but I'm running a Geist as a NPC in a campaign without having the book. How does a ghost become a Geist and about how long would that take? And how much do they remember of their life before they died?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T07:54:41-07:00","id":1402410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1402405#post1402405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This should be an easy question, but I'm running a Geist as a NPC in a campaign without having the book. How does a ghost become a Geist and about how long would that take? And how much do they remember of their life before they died?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Geist is created when a Ghost has &quot;drunk deep from the rivers of the Underworld.&quot; I've seen this interpreted a few different ways. The easiest being that they literally drank from the rivers of the Underworld, shedding everything that tied them to their humanity.<br /> <br /> The other I've seen is that a Ghost spends so much time in the Underworld their former self is shed over many different experiences over a long period of time.<br /> <br /> My impression is that both are valid. The basic idea is that a ghost becomes a Geist when they absorb power from the Underworld and lose their former self in the process. All that is left of their former life are seemingly unconnected flashes of memory called 'Remembrances.' Imagine a creature that has emotional memories, but can't comprehend why it even cares about them. They become unrecognizable from whomever they were and have effectively lost whatever made them human.<br /> <br /> As far as time; it varies. It kind be in an instant from drinking so much from the rivers you're old self is gone immediately, or it can be over many years, decades, or even centuries of drinking little by little, losing a piece of yourself with each taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26065-noahjam325-gmail-com","name":"[email\u00a0protected]","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T09:32:14-07:00","id":1402417,"title":"","content":"The only two ways described in GtS-E 2e (that I can remember) is the following:<br /> Drinking from a River. Drinking from one (no matter the amount, really) deals one aggravated damage per turn for for [10 - Integrity] turns. Doing this increases Rank by 1.<br /> The merger of two Doppelg\u00e4nger (two ghosts of the same individual; can be created through different shenanigans like near death experiences or magic). When they come into contact they automatically start eating each other. The survivor increases Rank by 1.<br /> When it happens, it happens. No time need passing other than the time required to drink a sip or eating your clone.<br /> <br /> Technically just increasing Rank doesn't necessarily mean the ghost turns into a Geist; it's specifically when you reach Rank 3 you become a Geist. I believe drinking from the Rivers is the only intended way to become a Geist, and that only Rank 2 ghosts would do so, and that Doppelg\u00e4nger only eat each other when at Rank 1 because it makes zero sense they get transformed into a heavily Underworld-connected entity without even visiting the Underworld. This disconnect in rules and fluff is a pet peeve that irritates me to no end, but for your NPC you could just make sure it's Rank 2 when it drinks from a River.<br /> <br /> And just a final side note: GMC rules update (and later CofD core book) stated that ghosts can only increase Rank while in the Underworld, but doesn't say anything about how that happens. Some took it to mean it happens over time, but GtS-E 2e clarifies that vague statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T14:43:34-07:00","id":1402867,"title":"","content":"Quick question!<br /> <br /> Can you use abjuration to dispel a possession condition? And if yes, what happens to the abjured ghost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T14:55:27-07:00","id":1402868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1402867#post1402867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use abjuration to dispel a possession condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Suppress, not dispel. Suppressing Manifestation Conditions is the primary use for abjuration.<br /> Unfortunately Bound/Sin-Eaters might not be able to do abjurations depending on how strict interpretation you have. At least, the rules for it are incomplete because Bound lack traits that are important modifiers for the roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1402867#post1402867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if yes, what happens to the abjured ghost?</div> </div> </div> </div>It stops possessing whoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T15:11:07-07:00","id":1402872,"title":"","content":"I don't understand. Why you say sin-eaters cannot perform abjuration? It is also reported into the core rulebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 07-14-2020, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T15:39:48-07:00","id":1402875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1402872#post1402872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand. Why you say sin-eaters cannot perform abjuration? It is also reported into the core rulebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>The text in CofD quite clearly states abjuration comes from the soul, and even if it's only flowery language, the rules simply do not account for Bound because the dice pool is supposed to be modified depending on Integrity (as well as Virtue and Vice).<br /> <br /> When double checking in GtSE, I see that there is a slightly edited version included under &quot;Common Actions&quot;. That one should probably work considering which book it's in and the fact that there's no mention of souls or mortal traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T15:32:44-07:00","id":1409027,"title":"","content":"I want to double check that my reading of the Rage is correct. Does Rage deal bashing or lethal damage?<br /> <br /> Your unarmed attacks gain a weapon damage rating<br /> equal to Plasm spent on Vent the Rage. Ghosts suffer<br /> lethal damage from these attacks.<br /> <br /> I *think* it's lethal because the core rules mention that every weapon does lethal damage, and there's specific rules for unarmed attacks that lay it out different. The Rage condition states that Ghosts suffer lethal damage from these attacks because Ghosts normally don't suffer damage from physical attacks not because unarmed attacks typically cause bashing.<br /> <br /> Does that sound correct?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25490-hrusk","name":"Hrusk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T15:48:54-07:00","id":1409030,"title":"","content":"Yes, my understanding is also that the Rage deals lethal damage. Not just to ghosts, but also to ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T07:22:40-07:00","id":1414390,"title":"","content":"What happens when a ghost with the Dead Meat merit wears a Deathmask? Does their meat body change to match the Reaper's form? If so, are they still ignored by most people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T17:36:49-07:00","id":1414846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1414390#post1414390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when a ghost with the Dead Meat merit wears a Deathmask? Does their meat body change to match the Reaper's form? If so, are they still ignored by most people?</div> </div> </div> </div>When donning a death mask, they almost turn into a new character. I imagine it could be different for each ghost. Maybe for 1 ghost it suppresses the merit, for another it molds their new form along side it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26065-noahjam325-gmail-com","name":"[email\u00a0protected]","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T14:48:51-08:00","id":1428513,"title":"","content":"If a Bound feeds their geist a Memento created from the Ghost Binding Ceremony, does that count as ectophagia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T06:02:41-08:00","id":1428590,"title":"","content":"I'd say so, at the very least it's a synergy breaking point with a penalty equal to ectophagia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T15:31:31-08:00","id":1429249,"title":"","content":"If a ghost is Trapped in the Walls of the Underworld, the core book says they lose one Essence per day and one Integrity if they cannot pay. For 3 Essence, they can restore an Integrity point. But at that point they should have 3 days worth of tithes. However, the core book does not mention anything about getting them out of the walls. Does it mean they need to restore themselves to full Integrity (or wherever they were before being absorbed) and pay a point of Essence before they are freed ? Are they going to be absorbed regardless and this just delays the inevitable ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T19:22:00-08:00","id":1429280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1429249#post1429249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a ghost is Trapped in the Walls of the Underworld, the core book says they lose one Essence per day and one Integrity if they cannot pay. For 3 Essence, they can restore an Integrity point. But at that point they should have 3 days worth of tithes. However, the core book does not mention anything about getting them out of the walls. Does it mean they need to restore themselves to full Integrity (or wherever they were before being absorbed) and pay a point of Essence before they are freed ? Are they going to be absorbed regardless and this just delays the inevitable ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Paying one Essence per day is what stops a ghost from getting Trapped in the Walls, at which point they have no Essence left to spend and the Underworld goes for their Integrity and autonomy. The rule is called &quot;Last Chance&quot; for a reason.<br /> <br /> Plasm and living memory can stall out a ghost's final consumption to set their affairs in order through external assistance, but once you've been incorporated into the geography, you're in dire straits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T17:00:16-08:00","id":1429436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1429280#post1429280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paying one Essence per day is what stops a ghost from getting Trapped in the Walls, at which point they have no Essence left to spend and the Underworld goes for their Integrity and autonomy. The rule is called &quot;Last Chance&quot; for a reason.<br /> <br /> Plasm and living memory can stall out a ghost's final consumption to set their affairs in order through external assistance, but once you've been incorporated into the geography, you're in dire straits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So basically its a race against time. They need someone to either research a way to set them free or complete their Anchors as proxies, all while providing them with a steady supply of Essence. Cool, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-30T13:36:27-08:00","id":1430493,"title":"","content":"Hi!<br /> This is a silly question about aesthetics. <br /> When a Sin-eater don the Caul, do you think we can visualize the outcome just like a Marvel's symbiote?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-30T17:25:21-08:00","id":1430514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1430493#post1430493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi!<br /> This is a silly question about aesthetics. <br /> When a Sin-eater don the Caul, do you think we can visualize the outcome just like a Marvel's symbiote?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it depends from the actual form of the bounded geist.<br /> Probably in some cases it could resemble a symbiote","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T23:06:21-08:00","id":1431123,"title":"","content":"About the Tomb Condition. It says it resolves in this case:<br /> <br /> &quot;The object comes into contact with the Ban of the creating Sin-Eater\u2019s geist.&quot;<br /> <br /> Was this supposed to be the Bane, not the Ban? Or is this actually right? Because a Ban seems like a weird choice for me here, concerning objects, at least. Sure, Bans can be things that make some sense to interact with objects, but what about Bans like acting a certain way toward the ghost in question? <br /> <br /> Like, how would you say a gun recreated from The Tomb came in contact with a Bane with a condition such as &quot;Having someone bow down to the ghost&quot; or &quot;Giving it something&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12306-andrew-kaninchen","name":"Andrew Kaninchen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T08:29:25-08:00","id":1431171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andrew Kaninchen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1431123#post1431123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was this supposed to be the Bane, not the Ban?</div> </div> </div> </div>Strong odds, considering every other Haunt Condition and the other effects of a Bound geist's bane on its powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-07T11:51:03-08:00","id":1431411,"title":"","content":"So I'm running a little side-game in a longer, larger campaign (Chronicle?) and while the overarching story has been centered around Vampires, this one's going to be Geist. We're all relatively experienced with Chronicles of Darkness, but this is our first time playing Geist. In addition to whatever first-timer tips anyone wants to throw my way, one of my players ended up with 5 dots in Memoria. Does anyone have any experience with this in-game? It seems like a lot, and I don't mind him having it (I trust him as a player), but I wanna make sure I &quot;get it right&quot; since it's so much of his sheet's weight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T14:19:51-08:00","id":1431501,"title":"","content":"Memoria requires that you be at the location of a meaningful event *or* have a ghost\u2019s anchor. Because some Anchors are portable, and Sin-Eaters can very easily recognize them, it\u2019s likely that such a character will want to carry around an Anchor with a \u201cuseful\u201d scene.<br /> [Note: the third dot let\u2019s you \u201cbottle\u201d any memory and take it with you, but only characters who drink from the bottle gain the Memoria condition... but as this isn\u2019t the Sin-Eaters condition, it isn\u2019t entirely clear if they can add Actors who didn\u2019t drink from the bottle or not.]<br /> <br /> With 4 dots, the Sin-Eater can /force/ any character to participate in that memory scene /as an instant action/. The text specifically cites mortals and ghosts, and that the contesting roll is Resolve+Synergy, implying Bound and other templates can also be drawn in; and does not state any exclusions. At 5 dots, the character can furthermore change how characters in that scene acted, to completely alter the outcome (but should keep it to a coherent scene; it can\u2019t pull of the same transformations as, say, Dream Weaving [CtL]). These illusions are \u2018real\u2019 to the actors, potentially applying damage or conditions - although lethal damage and breaking points can cause them to snap out of it.<br /> <br /> So, what I think you should expect is this character pulling out an anchor, binding people to a scene, and dictating their actions - particularly as a way to resolve combat or remove obstructions. This is probably the most \u201cbroken\u201d way this power can be used, even with a good faith reading of the rules.<br /> <br /> My advice is to work out the specific details of any memory that character carries around in an Anchor - and thus deciding on its use and limits. I recommend doing this collaboratively with the player, well beforehand.<br /> You may want to consider having a carried anchor for this purpose costing merit points: memento might be a good starting point (maybe with a discount, especially if it doesn\u2019t grant a Key); Retainer or Familiar (the ghost tethered to that Anchor) might also work.<br /> You will also need to rule on whether a bottled memoria can let them draw in actors or not. As I mentioned above, the text doesn\u2019t make this very clear. If it can, they have to activate and spend all the relevant essence beforehand (and you have to rule on what limits that has during downtime, and how much plasm they can get back to use on scene) but skips over the complication of a ghost hanging around them all the time, able to easily manifest and do it\u2019s own thing (and thus the costs for a retainer/ally).<br /> <br /> Specificity will be your friend here. I don\u2019t think you should try /preventing/ the PC from using it in this way, but you should probably avoid having an auto-win button. I don\u2019t think it\u2019s reasonable to restrict them to only the Memoria they encounter during the Story, with how the Haunt is written; but if you do consider that route, go out of your way to include them early on, and definitely to use them at numerous dramatic points.<br /> <br /> Also, keep in mind when a Clash of Wills would apply to this (only when 2 supernatural powers can\u2019t happen at the same time). Grant powers that would Clash to the opposition only sparingly - and make sure they get other uses relevant to the Story, beyond just resisting this power. Have an enemy bind the other PCs in their own Memoria, for example, or have one goon bound by Dominate, or a Fae use an elaborate Tale Spinning as part of their plot (although that might not be at thing in 2E).<br /> <br /> In general, I think you can \u201cget it right\u201d by buying in to this power: let them use it to auto-win a minor encounter or two, only directly counter it with awesome powers relevant to the plot, and go out of your way for them to come across Memoria during the story (at least one early on, and probably a few more at dramatic points). But, do work out very specific details (including how many actors can be bound, how many turns it lasts, what actions occur \u201cby default\u201d, and how far these can be twisted) - collaborate with your player on this as much as you\u2019re comfortable with; write drafts of these out on notecards that can be referenced or something. Providing a handout in the style of a movie script would be really awesome, actually. Then make sure those specific details are useful but limiting throughout various encounters.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hope this helps; Good Luck,<br /> ~ Seraph Kitty","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 01-08-2021, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T15:19:25-08:00","id":1431507,"title":"","content":"This is AMAZING! Thank you so much!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T17:26:17-08:00","id":1431522,"title":"","content":"Gonna just follow up with some notes to keep in mind:<br /> <br /> Mystery Play builds on D\u00e9nouement and Break the Cycle puts the ability to go off-script in the hands of the target. That means, among other things, that even within the specific confines of having a portable Anchor with a memory you know at least three details of, you're still spending Plasm based on the size of the scene you're making visible to everyone, then spending more Plasm to conscript no more than five people to play parts in the scene, and if you want to mess with an Actor that the scene didn't mess with then you have to spend yet more Plasm and hope they can manage to fail one roll and succeed the other.<br /> <br /> All of this pretty much guarantees the Haunt will need to be Unlocked, which means the character will either lose Willpower, limit their applications of this trick to circumstances resonant with their Keys, or deal with the gameplay loop the Doomed Condition(s) bring into play.<br /> <br /> Before getting into concerns about Clashes, remember that many of the Echoes the Memories grants access to end in the subject's death, that this is a very blatant explanation for the Haunt being on the Vengeful's list of affinities, and that taking lethal damage or suffering breaking points (or crisis points) prompts rolls to break out of the Actor Condition. The Memoria is a highly conditional power most useful for detective work and leveraging the past in specific ways; if you need to scare off living people or wreck a person, it can serve that purpose too, but there are more efficient means of doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T08:09:00-08:00","id":1431573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1431501#post1431501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Memoria requires that you be at the location of a meaningful event *or* have a ghost\u2019s anchor. Because some Anchors are portable, and Sin-Eaters can very easily recognize them, it\u2019s likely that such a character will want to carry around an Anchor with a \u201cuseful\u201d scene.<br /> [Note: the third dot let\u2019s you \u201cbottle\u201d any memory and take it with you, but only characters who drink from the bottle gain the Memoria condition... but as this isn\u2019t the Sin-Eaters condition, it isn\u2019t entirely clear if they can add Actors who 