 Hope this helps; Good Luck,<br /> ~ Seraph Kitty</div> </div> </div> </div>About memory in a bottle, the book states that it allows to &quot;store&quot; the Memoria condition, then the person who drinks it receives the same Memoria condition with the same charges.<br /> As the Haunts rules states that you can add Enhancement once the Haunt condition had been already activated, it seems to me that if a Sin eater with Memoriam 4 drinks the bottle, he can then add Actors.<br /> What it s not clear to me is if the bottles must be used only one time by drinking all of its content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T11:42:30-08:00","id":1431596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1431573#post1431573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What it s not clear to me is if the bottles must be used only one time by drinking all of its content.</div> </div> </div> </div>Odds are no, given that the Enhancement has a fixed cost, a permanent effect, and specific conditions for the memory being &quot;lost forever&quot; that are distinct from normal consumption (and remember that Plasm is not a pleasant substance to consume).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-12T04:59:21-08:00","id":1431951,"title":"","content":"Is the ocean of fragments supposed to represent the deepest part of the underworld or just one of the deeper parts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-12T05:32:51-08:00","id":1431956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1431951#post1431951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the ocean of fragments supposed to represent the deepest part of the underworld or just one of the deeper parts?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is the very bottom. All Rivers ends in the Ocean of Fragments and there are no ways to get deeper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T09:09:45-08:00","id":1432088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1431956#post1431956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is the very bottom. All Rivers ends in the Ocean of Fragments and there are no ways to get deeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot about that. I've recently started reading 2E geist so that's been an oddity.<br /> <br /> I was also thinking about bringing back my 1e geist character but it seems like death masks are taboo now. What's with that change? The character was a death mask collector in 1E.<br /> <br /> Edit- I forgot to ask if you attack someone using the marrionette such as a gun or a combat knife. Does it still count as an improvised weapon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 01-13-2021, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T10:21:43-08:00","id":1432093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1432088#post1432088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forgot about that. I've recently started reading 2E geist so that's been an oddity.<br /> <br /> I was also thinking about bringing back my 1e geist character but it seems like death masks are taboo now. What's with that change? The character was a death mask collector in 1E.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not completely up to 1e but I'm quite certain Deathmasks are very different between the two editions. Attitudes regarding Deathmasks should naturally change to reflect that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T10:47:05-08:00","id":1432094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1432093#post1432093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not completely up to 1e but I'm quite certain Deathmasks are very different between the two editions. Attitudes regarding Deathmasks should naturally change to reflect that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. deathmasks were the same. The old system had a tiered system with each memento doing something different. Deathmasks were a geist's deathmask and they gave you a skill bonus in addition to a key. They were weaker then memorabilia. Honestly, why did momentos get nerfed so hard? They used to be a lot stronger then they were in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T11:34:05-08:00","id":1432100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1432094#post1432094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. deathmasks were the same. The old system had a tiered system with each memento doing something different. Deathmasks were a geist's deathmask and they gave you a skill bonus in addition to a key. They were weaker then memorabilia. Honestly, why did momentos get nerfed so hard? They used to be a lot stronger then they were in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Were first edition Deathmasks also the source of one of the main antagonists to Sin-Eaters? That's the main thing about 2e Deathmasks. That they also function as Mementos is secondary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T11:46:19-08:00","id":1432101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1432094#post1432094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. deathmasks were the same. The old system had a tiered system with each memento doing something different. Deathmasks were a geist's deathmask and they gave you a skill bonus in addition to a key. They were weaker then memorabilia. Honestly, why did momentos get nerfed so hard? They used to be a lot stronger then they were in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keystones got replaced by Remembrance Traits, Haunts have a lower base dicepool than Manifestations did, Keys are now optional as well as impossible to simply buy as innate qualities, Reapers exist and geists have alternatives to the Bargain if they just want to exploit their greater mobility, and every Memento is now a way to get Plasm, make your Haunts work better, be more persuasive to other Sin-Eaters, and serves as a largely indestructible supernatural relic you can build a cult around.<br /> <br /> A Deathmask's defining features are that someone destroyed a geist to make it and a ghost who wears it assumes a monstrous form hellbent on damning the dead to consumption and misery. Mementos in general just got a buff from flattening the power curve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T12:10:30-08:00","id":1432104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1432101#post1432101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keystones got replaced by Remembrance Traits, Haunts have a lower base dicepool than Manifestations did, Keys are now optional as well as impossible to simply buy as innate qualities, Reapers exist and geists have alternatives to the Bargain if they just want to exploit their greater mobility, and every Memento is now a way to get Plasm, make your Haunts work better, be more persuasive to other Sin-Eaters, and serves as a largely indestructible supernatural relic you can build a cult around.<br /> <br /> A Deathmask's defining features are that someone destroyed a geist to make it and a ghost who wears it assumes a monstrous form hellbent on damning the dead to consumption and misery. Mementos in general just got a buff from flattening the power curve.</div> </div> </div> </div>To some extent yes, but I do remember that memorabilia used to be a +5 equipment modifier and death masks used to give additional abilities and skills. I know that deathmasks give ghosts the ability to become reapers but it kind of sucks that my character concept is probably going to cause a lot of hostilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T23:45:02-08:00","id":1432169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1432104#post1432104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To some extent yes, but I do remember that memorabilia used to be a +5 equipment modifier and death masks used to give additional abilities and skills. I know that deathmasks give ghosts the ability to become reapers but it kind of sucks that my character concept is probably going to cause a lot of hostilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>It must be said that the book states that Deathmasks don t give social bonus, but also that they MIGHT give social penalty.<br /> It depends probably on the story of how you obtained the masks, and if your character legend is appropriate probably he can still carry them without causing hostility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T19:34:08-08:00","id":1432274,"title":"","content":"So, this is related to a character concept I have. I\u2019m tempted to have a character start with 1 dot of Marionette and Tomb and work up from there, and to eventually use it on vehicles for various reasons. However, given he has a Volkswagen Beetle at the start, I\u2019m not sure what size that would fall under and thus how high in Marionette/Tomb they\u2019d need to be to affect/create such things. Would a Volkswagen Beetle be around size 9 or 10?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T19:52:33-08:00","id":1432275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1432274#post1432274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this is related to a character concept I have. I\u2019m tempted to have a character start with 1 dot of Marionette and Tomb and work up from there, and to eventually use it on vehicles for various reasons. However, given he has a Volkswagen Beetle at the start, I\u2019m not sure what size that would fall under and thus how high in Marionette/Tomb they\u2019d need to be to affect/create such things. Would a Volkswagen Beetle be around size 9 or 10?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cross-referencing Wikipedia with Deviant's expanded version of the Size chart, a Beetle is a &quot;compact car&quot; and therefore probably Size 8.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T20:49:29-08:00","id":1432279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1432274#post1432274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this is related to a character concept I have. I\u2019m tempted to have a character start with 1 dot of Marionette and Tomb and work up from there, and to eventually use it on vehicles for various reasons. However, given he has a Volkswagen Beetle at the start, I\u2019m not sure what size that would fall under and thus how high in Marionette/Tomb they\u2019d need to be to affect/create such things. Would a Volkswagen Beetle be around size 9 or 10?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would take marionette 3 to do that. You'd probably want to do that at CC and work your way towards Marionette 4 though. Servant at Marionette 4 is quite powerful and capable of making it so that you don't have to keep your focus on your car any more and much more versatile. Assume it's Size 8, you'd need to spend 2 plasm to affect it plus another 2 plasm to give the servant condition. If you want it to last 24 hours though it'd take another 4 plasm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T21:26:42-08:00","id":1432280,"title":"","content":"Trying to make sure I'm parsing the Krewe vs. Krewe rules correctly:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Attempting to destroy another krewe is a krewe action with an open-ended Complexity (and therefore no set amount of Tasks and no guarantee of success, heavily complicated or otherwise), with success being predicated on accumulating Effort from success or exceptional success on the action's rolls equal to the enemy krewe's Congregation rating (each point inflicting a point of lethal damage), which inflicts the Coup d'Etat Condition.<br /> \u2022 Conflicts between krewes are contested actions, with the victor earning the Effort (and thereby inflicting lethal damage on the opposition's Congregation, in the case of war with the aim of destruction).<br /> \u2022 A lower-Esotery krewe in conflict with a higher-Esotery krewe (i.e. one that has already committed one krewe action to acting against another krewe) can commit a second krewe action to apply a penalty equal to half its Power to all the higher-Esotery krewe's other Tasks as long as the smaller krewe doesn't start another action.<br /> <br /> Put differently:<br /> \u2022 A krewe action to destroy another krewe has no Complexity to set Tasks from (though presumably the krewe's Task limit still applies and an otherwise-identical krewe action can be declared from the krewe's pool of actions to continue the process), so its ultimate success is up in the air compared to other krewe actions.<br /> \u2022 Krewes acting against each other make a contested roll to see which of them gains the Effort for the action (and applies damage, in war), with their krewe actions and Task limits applying a soft restriction on how far they can push themselves in this pursuit.<br /> \u2022 A weaker krewe may effectively fully commit its resources to conflict with a larger krewe by dedicating one krewe action to the contested roll and another to inflict a penalty on all their other actions as long as the smaller krewe doesn't do anything else, having put most of their resources into interfering with the larger group's other actions as they attack it. (&quot;The rest of the higher-Esotery krewe's Tasks&quot; here meaning &quot;any other rolls the krewe makes to generate Effort,&quot; not &quot;any other rolls to generate Effort on the ongoing krewe action of destroying the krewe.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Does that seem accurate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T22:32:49-08:00","id":1432282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1432275#post1432275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cross-referencing Wikipedia with Deviant's expanded version of the Size chart, a Beetle is a &quot;compact car&quot; and therefore probably Size 8.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks dude. I forgot Deviant spelled that out more thorough - should look into that for other games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1432279#post1432279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would take marionette 3 to do that. You'd probably want to do that at CC and work your way towards Marionette 4 though. Servant at Marionette 4 is quite powerful and capable of making it so that you don't have to keep your focus on your car any more and much more versatile. Assume it's Size 8, you'd need to spend 2 plasm to affect it plus another 2 plasm to give the servant condition. If you want it to last 24 hours though it'd take another 4 plasm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should have specified that I wanted to <i>eventually</i> get to doing that, not doing so at character creation. Still, I appreciate you taking the time to elaborate on all that. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-16T01:07:24-08:00","id":1432385,"title":"","content":"By the way it is worded, isn't the Stillness Key a very easy limitless suply of Plasm via Free Plasm/accepting the Doom? You just have to unlock any Haunt with it, say something so the Doom resolves and the condition ends and boom, plasm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12306-andrew-kaninchen","name":"Andrew Kaninchen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-16T07:43:46-08:00","id":1432403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andrew Kaninchen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1432385#post1432385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way it is worded, isn't the Stillness Key a very easy limitless suply of Plasm via Free Plasm/accepting the Doom? You just have to unlock any Haunt with it, say something so the Doom resolves and the condition ends and boom, plasm.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;boom, plasm&quot; happens before you say something and ends any Haunts you <i>invoked the power of the Underworld</i> to benefit, which is usually not something you want happening in a scene where you're using a Haunt to accomplish anything.<br /> <br /> The basic social contract of &quot;don't waste your fellow players' time putting the camera on your character doing this for literally no reason&quot; applies. The Doomed Condition is a dramatic tool to justify story complications. See also the general fair-play consideration of &quot;if you have the Shaken or Spooked Condition(s), you should probably play that state of mind a bit and resolve them instead of having breaking points/the Boneyard/other jarring circumstance not affect narratively despite having mechanically affected you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-16T08:15:35-08:00","id":1432406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andrew Kaninchen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1432385#post1432385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way it is worded, isn't the Stillness Key a very easy limitless suply of Plasm via Free Plasm/accepting the Doom? You just have to unlock any Haunt with it, say something so the Doom resolves and the condition ends and boom, plasm.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Stillness key has one of the less punishing key effects upon getting hit with the Doom, in that all it does is cancel your haunt. However, used without a haunt and your character will be mute until the next game session. Meaning that for the entire chapter you can't resolve the doom, can't speak and I believe you can't use the key until it resolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 01-16-2021, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-16T09:43:52-08:00","id":1432414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1432280#post1432280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to make sure I'm parsing the Krewe vs. Krewe rules correctly:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Attempting to destroy another krewe is a krewe action with an open-ended Complexity (and therefore no set amount of Tasks and no guarantee of success, heavily complicated or otherwise), with success being predicated on accumulating Effort from success or exceptional success on the action's rolls equal to the enemy krewe's Congregation rating (each point inflicting a point of lethal damage), which inflicts the Coup d'Etat Condition.<br /> \u2022 Conflicts between krewes are contested actions, with the victor earning the Effort (and thereby inflicting lethal damage on the opposition's Congregation, in the case of war with the aim of destruction).<br /> \u2022 A lower-Esotery krewe in conflict with a higher-Esotery krewe (i.e. one that has already committed one krewe action to acting against another krewe) can commit a second krewe action to apply a penalty equal to half its Power to all the higher-Esotery krewe's other Tasks as long as the smaller krewe doesn't start another action.<br /> <br /> Put differently:<br /> \u2022 A krewe action to destroy another krewe has no Complexity to set Tasks from (though presumably the krewe's Task limit still applies and an otherwise-identical krewe action can be declared from the krewe's pool of actions to continue the process), so its ultimate success is up in the air compared to other krewe actions.<br /> \u2022 Krewes acting against each other make a contested roll to see which of them gains the Effort for the action (and applies damage, in war), with their krewe actions and Task limits applying a soft restriction on how far they can push themselves in this pursuit.<br /> \u2022 A weaker krewe may effectively fully commit its resources to conflict with a larger krewe by dedicating one krewe action to the contested roll and another to inflict a penalty on all their other actions as long as the smaller krewe doesn't do anything else, having put most of their resources into interfering with the larger group's other actions as they attack it. (&quot;The rest of the higher-Esotery krewe's Tasks&quot; here meaning &quot;any other rolls the krewe makes to generate Effort,&quot; not &quot;any other rolls to generate Effort on the ongoing krewe action of destroying the krewe.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Does that seem accurate?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are also other conditions that can generate as a side effect of a war especially a weaker krewe but yes in general that is correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-16T18:26:14-08:00","id":1432452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andrew Kaninchen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1432385#post1432385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way it is worded, isn't the Stillness Key a very easy limitless suply of Plasm via Free Plasm/accepting the Doom? You just have to unlock any Haunt with it, say something so the Doom resolves and the condition ends and boom, plasm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. This was discovered the same day the Kickstarter manuscript was released to backers so it's quite shocking it still hasn't been fixed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1432403#post1432403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;boom, plasm&quot; happens before you say something and ends any Haunts you <i>invoked the power of the Underworld</i> to benefit, which is usually not something you want happening in a scene where you're using a Haunt to accomplish anything.<br /> <br /> The basic social contract of &quot;don't waste your fellow players' time putting the camera on your character doing this for literally no reason&quot; applies. The Doomed Condition is a dramatic tool to justify story complications. See also the general fair-play consideration of &quot;if you have the Shaken or Spooked Condition(s), you should probably play that state of mind a bit and resolve them instead of having breaking points/the Boneyard/other jarring circumstance not affect narratively despite having mechanically affected you.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, if you gain an advantage for a drawback you can completely ignore it's just bad design. The fact that the Key of Stillness is the <i>only</i> Key that has a different resolution for using it without a Haunt is basically an admission of that fact. And it's hardly a time waster when you can just go &quot;Ah, at the end of this scene I just activate this Haunt with this Key repeatedly to refill my Plasm pool&quot; and then just roll until you've filled up. It's trivially easy to exploit this loophole. The whole &quot;invoking the power of the Underworld&quot; thing definitely should be dramatic, but it's turned comical by the fact that you can actually benefit from ignoring it.<br /> <br /> You mention Shaken and Spooked, but in order to gain the benefits of those Conditions (namely, the beat for resolving them) you need to actively engage with the drawback. They're carrots for the player to roleplay according to what they represent. You can elect to ignore them (and I don't shame players for doing so as long as they don't act too much out of character) but then you simply don't get the bonus from them. The key (hehe) difference is that the Key of Stillness' Doomed Condition gives you the carrot while making the drawback wholly optional (and ignoring the drawback is how you get a beat on top of the free Plasm). Combined with the fact that you can freely choose to receive this Condition (as opposed to Shaken and Spooked) means you've got an at-will Plasm refill with basically no character or player investment necessary aside from a few quick rolls. The one limit is that you might not want to do it if you're busy using the Key or your action economy for other stuff, but if you keep yourself topped up between those times you should rarely be able to empty your Plasm pool during those times.<br /> <br /> Hell, if you only need to activate a Haunt for a turn or two for whatever reason, using the Key of Stillness appropriately would also lead to you gaining all the benefits (extra dice, free Plasm, beat for resolving the Condition) for the minor drawback of not wanting to speak for a few seconds. So even when you don't actively pursue the obvious loophole that never should've existed in the first place you can still benefit from it when all other Keys would force an actual drawback (or at the very least put you at risk, in the case of the Key of Chance).<br /> <br /> Now, my group does have a social contract regarding wildly unbalanced rules or rules that have wildly unintentional consequences: After we see something like that we bring it up in the group and discuss how to patch it away.<br /> And to preempt anyone saying &quot;you don't need to house rule away the OP thing as long as you honour the game and simply don't use it&quot;: That's just an unspoken house rule to the same effect, except much fuzzier and it doesn't resolve any borderline cases as mentioned above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-16T20:39:17-08:00","id":1432459,"title":"","content":"\u2026Anyway.<br /> <br /> Are Krewe Beats and Synergy Beats counted separately from regular Beats for the purposes of the one-Beat-per-category-per-scene limit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T00:05:56-08:00","id":1432467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1432452#post1432452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. This was discovered the same day the Kickstarter manuscript was released to backers so it's quite shocking it still hasn't been fixed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, if you gain an advantage for a drawback you can completely ignore it's just bad design. The fact that the Key of Stillness is the <i>only</i> Key that has a different resolution for using it without a Haunt is basically an admission of that fact. And it's hardly a time waster when you can just go &amp;quot;Ah, at the end of this scene I just activate this Haunt with this Key repeatedly to refill my Plasm pool&amp;quot; and then just roll until you've filled up. It's trivially easy to exploit this loophole. The whole &amp;quot;invoking the power of the Underworld&amp;quot; thing definitely should be dramatic, but it's turned comical by the fact that you can actually benefit from ignoring it.<br /> <br /> You mention Shaken and Spooked, but in order to gain the benefits of those Conditions (namely, the beat for resolving them) you need to actively engage with the drawback. They're carrots for the player to roleplay according to what they represent. You can elect to ignore them (and I don't shame players for doing so as long as they don't act too much out of character) but then you simply don't get the bonus from them. The key (hehe) difference is that the Key of Stillness' Doomed Condition gives you the carrot while making the drawback wholly optional (and ignoring the drawback is how you get a beat on top of the free Plasm). Combined with the fact that you can freely choose to receive this Condition (as opposed to Shaken and Spooked) means you've got an at-will Plasm refill with basically no character or player investment necessary aside from a few quick rolls. The one limit is that you might not want to do it if you're busy using the Key or your action economy for other stuff, but if you keep yourself topped up between those times you should rarely be able to empty your Plasm pool during those times.<br /> <br /> Hell, if you only need to activate a Haunt for a turn or two for whatever reason, using the Key of Stillness appropriately would also lead to you gaining all the benefits (extra dice, free Plasm, beat for resolving the Condition) for the minor drawback of not wanting to speak for a few seconds. So even when you don't actively pursue the obvious loophole that never should've existed in the first place you can still benefit from it when all other Keys would force an actual drawback (or at the very least put you at risk, in the case of the Key of Chance).<br /> <br /> Now, my group does have a social contract regarding wildly unbalanced rules or rules that have wildly unintentional consequences: After we see something like that we bring it up in the group and discuss how to patch it away.<br /> And to preempt anyone saying &amp;quot;you don't need to house rule away the OP thing as long as you honour the game and simply don't use it&amp;quot;: That's just an unspoken house rule to the same effect, except much fuzzier and it doesn't resolve any borderline cases as mentioned above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that is pretty much exactly how I feel about the whole thing. I asked here mainly to know if I hadn't missed anything that would make it less of an easily exploitable thing, but seeing as there isn't, I'll try to think of something alongside my st and other players. Probably change the Doom altogether. I enjoy the roleplay of being forced not to speak or there will be a penalty, so I'll try to go from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12306-andrew-kaninchen","name":"Andrew Kaninchen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-17T08:16:26-08:00","id":1432507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andrew Kaninchen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1432467#post1432467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that is pretty much exactly how I feel about the whole thing. I asked here mainly to know if I hadn't missed anything that would make it less of an easily exploitable thing, but seeing as there isn't, I'll try to think of something alongside my st and other players. Probably change the Doom altogether. I enjoy the roleplay of being forced not to speak or there will be a penalty, so I'll try to go from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2022 As described, but lose one Willpower per instance of the Doom resolved by speaking.<br /> \u2022 As described, but the Doom resolves at the end of the scene <i>after</i> the one where the Haunt Condition resolves, as with deliberately Unleashing your geist and the Weakened Bond Condition.<br /> \u2022 As described, but this corresponds to a Social roll that relies on spoken language, which automatically fails, as with the Key of Beasts and animal-related rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T17:59:23-08:00","id":1432983,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve gotten into an argument with someone on Discord regarding how Supernatural Membership is supposed to work. As they have surmised, the merit can be read in two ways:<br /> <br /> You can create characters whose collective total dots in Supernatural Merits are Supernatural Membership, multiplied by two.<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> You can create characters who each have up to Supernatural Membership, multiplied by two, in Supernatural Merit dots.<br /> <br /> I am firmly in the latter reading, they are firmly in the former category. I feel that going by the former is a gross oversimplification that negates most of the usefulness of the merit - at one dot at most your Krewe has a single NPC with Unseen Sense, and at five dots you have, at most, five human Krewe members who can do anything of note with the merit. Of course this doesn\u2019t count player characters who are playing as psychics, but it still feels like hamstringing NPCs for the sake of simplification.<br /> <br /> As our respective arguments aren\u2019t doing anything to convince the other, outside arbitrator about this would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 01-21-2021, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T19:18:02-08:00","id":1432995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1432983#post1432983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve gotten into an argument with someone on Discord regarding how Supernatural Membership is supposed to work. As they have surmised, the merit can be read in two ways:<br /> <br /> You can create characters whose collective total dots in Supernatural Merits are Supernatural Membership, multiplied by two.<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> You can create characters who each have up to Supernatural Membership, multiplied by two, in Supernatural Merit dots.<br /> <br /> I am firmly in the latter reading, they are firmly in the former category. I feel that going by the former is a gross oversimplification that negates most of the usefulness of the merit - at one dot at most your Krewe has a single NPC with Unseen Sense, and at five dots you have, at most, five human Krewe members who can do anything of note with the merit. Of course this doesn\u2019t count player characters who are playing as psychics, but it still feels like hamstringing NPCs for the sake of simplification.<br /> <br /> As our respective arguments aren\u2019t doing anything to convince the other, outside arbitrator about this would be appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the latter.<br /> <br /> A krewe's typical membership numbers don't even approach multiple hundreds at most (or even a single hundred, for the vast majority of krewes) \u2014 headcount trends to ten times the krewe's Resistance, and most krewes don't have the Esotery to support Attributes rated above 9.<br /> <br /> Having a krewe whose membership has &quot;various living members with exceptional abilities&quot; defined as a collective total rating in Supernatural Merits would have barely more living characters with abilities than it had Sin-Eaters, and given that the Merit specifically doesn't count player characters or Geist's expanded form of the Retainer Merit, that's a bit thinly-spread for a Merit built to represent &quot;your krewe has multiple mediums, psychics, and other minor talents among its membership.&quot;<br /> <br /> The scaling is for <i>how Supernatural</i> your krewe's Membership is, not for how Supernatural <i>your krewe's Membership</i> is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T14:11:56-08:00","id":1433098,"title":"","content":"Given the Rank note on page 91 of the corebook, should the range of the Liminal Aura be understood as 10 x Rank yards rather than 10 x Synergy yards?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T21:01:33-08:00","id":1433456,"title":"","content":"Questions regarding the Tomb Haunt.<br /> So I get that if you are just restoring an item to how it was at some point in the past, you are just fixing up the object you physically have there with you.<br /> However, if are creating a replica from a piece of an item/person, does that piece become part of the newly created replica?<br /> What about when you use a picture as a link for the replica instead?<br /> Or what about when you use a symbolic link such as the guys leather jacket being used to make a replica of his beloved car example they give in the book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11980-emparawr","name":"Emparawr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11980_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T21:59:45-08:00","id":1433462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emparawr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433456#post1433456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, if are creating a replica from a piece of an item/person, does that piece become part of the newly created replica?<br /> What about when you use a picture as a link for the replica instead?<br /> Or what about when you use a symbolic link such as the guys leather jacket being used to make a replica of his beloved car example they give in the book?</div> </div> </div> </div>The text seems quite clear: &quot;The piece or symbolic representation of the object becomes a precise replica of the original at whatever point in its history the Sin-Eater desires.&quot;<br /> <br /> Presumably the reference material persists beyond the resolution of the Haunt, but what happens to it while it's being used is that it turns into the replica.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-26T22:22:35-08:00","id":1433577,"title":"","content":"Just making sure but If I get tossed out a large story building I can string the marionette on myself and stop myself from falling right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-26T23:50:33-08:00","id":1433581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433577#post1433577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just making sure but If I get tossed out a large story building I can string the marionette on myself and stop myself from falling right?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, for much the same reason it doesn't let you fly. There's two other Haunts to use if you want to cover yourself in Plasm and defy gravity under your own power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T08:06:20-08:00","id":1433617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433581#post1433581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, for much the same reason it doesn't let you fly. There's two other Haunts to use if you want to cover yourself in Plasm and defy gravity under your own power.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? It lets you levitate a gun. You should be able to levitate people and SUVs at 3.<br /> <br /> Edit- This leads to a follow up question. If you can take a gun out of someone's holster and fire with it. How fast do things levitate with the marionette.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 01-27-2021, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T10:02:46-08:00","id":1433628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433617#post1433617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so? It lets you levitate a gun. You should be able to levitate people and SUVs at 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because there's a distinction between &quot;people&quot; and &quot;yourself.&quot; It's an instant action to use and it's a telekinesis/remote control power besides. You're not going to be able to apply it reactively in any circumstance where falling isn't taking an appreciable amount of time even if the power were as simple as &quot;thing levitates.&quot;<br /> <br /> Caul 3 lets you fly at your normal Speed for a minimum of 3 Plasm and is based around physically reshaping your body to grant you aerial mobility.<br /> <br /> Shroud 2 lets you hover and fly at half your normal Speed for a minimum of 3 Plasm and is based around surrounding you with your geist and becoming more ghostly.<br /> <br /> Marionette 3 lets you telekinetically move a Size 5 target at a Speed between 3 and 50 (and having Synergy 3 puts that number at at least the full Speed of a character with average Strength and Dexterity) for a minimum of 1 Plasm and is based around connecting you to the target with Plasmic puppet strings.<br /> <br /> One of these things is not like the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T11:47:16-08:00","id":1433637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433628#post1433628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because there's a distinction between &quot;people&quot; and &quot;yourself.&quot; It's an instant action to use and it's a telekinesis/remote control power besides. You're not going to be able to apply it reactively in any circumstance where falling isn't taking an appreciable amount of time even if the power were as simple as &quot;thing levitates.&quot;<br /> <br /> Caul 3 lets you fly at your normal Speed for a minimum of 3 Plasm and is based around physically reshaping your body to grant you aerial mobility.<br /> <br /> Shroud 2 lets you hover and fly at half your normal Speed for a minimum of 3 Plasm and is based around surrounding you with your geist and becoming more ghostly.<br /> <br /> Marionette 3 lets you telekinetically move a Size 5 target at a Speed between 3 and 50 (and having Synergy 3 puts that number at at least the full Speed of a character with average Strength and Dexterity) for a minimum of 1 Plasm and is based around connecting you to the target with Plasmic puppet strings.<br /> <br /> One of these things is not like the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing stops you from targeting yourself with the marionette and you still have to concentrate to do preform the action. It's not reflexive like the caul or shroud. It also doesn't have any of the other effects shroud or caul have. You're just controlling yourself long enough to get out of harm. It probably feels unnatural and might require a roll to keep concentrating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T12:11:47-08:00","id":1433642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433637#post1433637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing stops you from targeting yourself with the marionette</div> </div> </div> </div>Again: Puppet strings. Pulling. From you. On something else.<br /> <br /> The power ends if you break line of sight with the thing you're controlling and deprives an active target of their own action whenever you control it. It's very clearly described in terms of a power that is used on things that aren't yourself.<br /> <br /> This isn't the Forces Arcanum \u2014 you don't have a broad ability to mess with gravity, you have Plasmic tendrils that let you move something without touching it and make it do stuff it can normally do. The &quot;levitation&quot; is an incidental effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T12:28:40-08:00","id":1433644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433642#post1433642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again: Puppet strings. Pulling. From you. On something else.<br /> <br /> The power ends if you break line of sight with the thing you're controlling and deprives an active target of their own action whenever you control it. It's very clearly described in terms of a power that is used on things that aren't yourself.<br /> <br /> This isn't the Forces Arcanum \u2014 you don't have a broad ability to mess with gravity, you have Plasmic tendrils that let you move something without touching it and make it do stuff it can normally do. The &quot;levitation&quot; is an incidental effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can look at yourself and nothing in the ruling precludes you from targeting yourself. I don't see why a creative use of the power is such an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T13:30:56-08:00","id":1433650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433644#post1433644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can look at yourself and nothing in the ruling precludes you from targeting yourself. I don't see why a creative use of the power is such an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the way the Marionette explicitly works makes using it for self-levitation functionally a Troll Physics bootstrapping method, which is pretty far outside the descriptive language that represents the Haunt in question.<br /> <br /> There are two other powers with a better claim on &quot;make yourself fly&quot; that cost more to accomplish the effect than Marionette 3 does. Avoiding getting tossed out of a building is accomplished through mundane rolls or other powers, not by tangling yourself up in phantom limbs.<br /> <br /> If you've already decided you're going to run it that way on the sole basis of &quot;doesn't say&quot; then there's no point in continuing the discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T14:36:29-08:00","id":1433657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433650#post1433650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the way the Marionette explicitly works makes using it for self-levitation functionally a Troll Physics bootstrapping method, which is pretty far outside the descriptive language that represents the Haunt in question.<br /> <br /> There are two other powers with a better claim on &quot;make yourself fly&quot; that cost more to accomplish the effect than Marionette 3 does. Avoiding getting tossed out of a building is accomplished through mundane rolls or other powers, not by tangling yourself up in phantom limbs.<br /> <br /> If you've already decided you're going to run it that way on the sole basis of &quot;doesn't say&quot; then there's no point in continuing the discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it really matter if you target your body or your clothes to make yourself levitate? Outside possibly needing to target multiple things costing more plasm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T23:11:54-08:00","id":1433685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433657#post1433657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it really matter if you target your body or your clothes to make yourself levitate? Outside possibly needing to target multiple things costing more plasm.</div> </div> </div> </div>My opinion is, let s think about Marionette strings like invisible long arms.<br /> Now, with an arm you can lift a doll, make it dance and also &quot;fly&quot;.<br /> But what happens if you try to use your arms to lift yourself?<br /> A creative use of the power COULD (not sure) be to select a valid target during the fall to anchor yourself to it with the strings and stop the fall.<br /> Even in this case you should target a fixed thing with a size that doesn t exceed your limits, and strong enough to support your weight (the only thing i can think about that fits is an helicopter)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 01-28-2021, 02:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T00:52:54-08:00","id":1433686,"title":"","content":"Using Marionette on yourself means you're pulling on yourself. Not with your physical strength or anything, but it's still shaky. If it was physical, then it would be impossible because you'd literally be unable to have any leverage. Since it works mystically it's kinda impossible to say either way, but both ways are possible.<br /> Since that line of reasoning isn't conclusive, I think it's better to choose the option that is most thematically appropriate given the context.<br /> Two examples for what I mean: In Mage this would totally be possible according to the wide utility of the Arcana, but it Changeling it wouldn't because &quot;puppeteering&quot; yourself is not actually puppeteering in a literal/narrative sense even if you apply the same physical forces so that would be excluded from the Contract.<br /> I don't know Geist that well, but given that the focus of Marionette is largely to manipulate things on a distance I'm definitely leaning towards disallowing use on the self (as well as your clothes when used in this way since you still have the same &quot;leverage&quot; as when attempting it on the self).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 01-28-2021, 03:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T11:25:45-08:00","id":1433728,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, it turns out you cannot use the Marionette to fly unless you can already fly, at which point, using the Marionette to do it for you seems a little silly. From page 109:<br /> &quot;The Sin-Eater can command a puppet to do whatever it could do normally \u2014 if she controls a car, she can make it drive, and if she puppeteers a bird, she can make it fly.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T12:06:53-08:00","id":1433732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433728#post1433728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, it turns out you cannot use the Marionette to fly unless you can already fly, at which point, using the Marionette to do it for you seems a little silly. From page 109:<br /> &quot;The Sin-Eater can command a puppet to do whatever it could do normally \u2014 if she controls a car, she can make it drive, and if she puppeteers a bird, she can make it fly.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That entirely contradicts the ability to make a gun levitate and shoot or SUVs fly. As per the description of both Swarm, the second dot power, and Phantom Strength. It would also make it incredibly useless to control objects if you could only say make a TV turn on instead of being able to fling one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T12:44:32-08:00","id":1433736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433732#post1433732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That entirely contradicts the ability to make a gun levitate and shoot or SUVs fly. As per the description of both Swarm, the second dot power, and Phantom Strength. It would also make it incredibly useless to control objects if you could only say make a TV turn on instead of being able to fling one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The power literally has rules for throwing stuff in the same sidebar containing the quote I pulled. I also suspect most, if not all references to levitation in the Haunt is just throwing things, possibly including pulling the gun from its holster.<br /> <br /> But, to be fair, that sidebar <i>also</i> describes the speed at which objects can be moved telekinetically, so one can argue that this makes flight possible. I think that is for individual tables/Bound/Keys to decide. However, the underlying Conditions make it pretty clear to me that the Bound using the Marionette cannot reasonably target themself, since they would be... using their possession power on themself. And that is beyond stupid, and obviously not intentional.<br /> <br /> If you really want to fly using the Marionette so badly, just get a large carpet and stand on it, or something. Like, this doesn't have to be hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T12:59:34-08:00","id":1433738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433736#post1433736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The power literally has rules for throwing stuff in the same sidebar containing the quote I pulled. I also suspect most, if not all references to levitation in the Haunt is just throwing things, possibly including pulling the gun from its holster.<br /> <br /> But, to be fair, that sidebar <i>also</i> describes the speed at which objects can be moved telekinetically, so one can argue that this makes flight possible. I think that is for individual tables/Bound/Keys to decide. However, the underlying Conditions make it pretty clear to me that the Bound using the Marionette cannot reasonably target themself, since they would be... using their possession power on themself. And that is beyond stupid, and obviously not intentional.<br /> <br /> If you really want to fly using the Marionette so badly, just get a large carpet and stand on it, or something. Like, this doesn't have to be hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, I can target my clothes with it instead of my body. It's clear that the marionette is supposed to be telekinetic control though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T13:28:19-08:00","id":1433740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433738#post1433738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, I can target my clothes with it instead of my body. It's clear that the marionette is supposed to be telekinetic control though.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've very clearly made up your mind by now and gotten multiple &quot;run it that way if you like&quot; responses as caveats to the multiple people telling you that they don't think the power of telekinetic control generalizes to telekinetic flight in this game. You're not going to be convinced and you're not convincing anyone else. Further discussion in this vein serves no purpose.<br /> <br /> <br /> Given that the only mechanical difference between Tyranny and Synergy is the fixed intervention dicepool, is it reasonable to assume that Tyrannous characters still derive the emotional awareness and controlled crisis point responses of different Relationship levels at higher Tyranny ratings (and through the temporary benefits of the Bonding Condition), albeit in a darker/more one-way fashion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T14:30:53-08:00","id":1433746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433740#post1433740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the only mechanical difference between Tyranny and Synergy is the fixed intervention dicepool, is it reasonable to assume that Tyrannous characters still derive the emotional awareness and controlled crisis point responses of different Relationship levels at higher Tyranny ratings (and through the temporary benefits of the Bonding Condition), albeit in a darker/more one-way fashion?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not. It seems awfully fitting that greater Tyranny allows you to command your geist to specific action in lieu of interceding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T11:59:01-08:00","id":1433815,"title":"","content":"I could not find an answer in the book nor searching the forum. In the core Geist book, it states that a Ceremony costs 2 XP. However, many of the ceremonies are 1-5 dots. Is that 2 XP per dot, or 2 XP for ANY ceremony? Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1907-waywardson74","name":"Waywardson74","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T14:43:44-08:00","id":1433839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433736#post1433736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The power literally has rules for throwing stuff in the same sidebar containing the quote I pulled. I also suspect most, if not all references to levitation in the Haunt is just throwing things, possibly including pulling the gun from its holster.<br /> <br /> But, to be fair, that sidebar <i>also</i> describes the speed at which objects can be moved telekinetically, so one can argue that this makes flight possible. I think that is for individual tables/Bound/Keys to decide. However, the underlying Conditions make it pretty clear to me that the Bound using the Marionette cannot reasonably target themself, since they would be... using their possession power on themself. And that is beyond stupid, and obviously not intentional.<br /> <br /> If you really want to fly using the Marionette so badly, just get a large carpet and stand on it, or something. Like, this doesn't have to be hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, I imagine it\u2019d work very well if you were paralyzed in some way and needed to move your own body... though Sin Eaters can\u2019t be poisoned, and drugs that would affect the body like that would probably affect the mind too.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t remember, would a drug work to that effect on a Sin Eater?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T15:53:35-08:00","id":1433850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Waywardson74</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433815#post1433815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could not find an answer in the book nor searching the forum. In the core Geist book, it states that a Ceremony costs 2 XP. However, many of the ceremonies are 1-5 dots. Is that 2 XP per dot, or 2 XP for ANY ceremony? Thank you!</div> </div> </div> </div>2xp per dot would be an HUGE expense, so i suppose it s a flat 2xp per ceremony","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T16:18:44-08:00","id":1433851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Waywardson74</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433815#post1433815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could not find an answer in the book nor searching the forum. In the core Geist book, it states that a Ceremony costs 2 XP. However, many of the ceremonies are 1-5 dots. Is that 2 XP per dot, or 2 XP for ANY ceremony? Thank you!</div> </div> </div> </div>The chart on page 77 says 2 in the &quot;Cost per dot&quot; column and the Krewe Advancement chart on page 80 also says 2 per dot. It's 2 per dot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433850#post1433850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2xp per dot would be an HUGE expense, so i suppose it s a flat 2xp per ceremony</div> </div> </div> </div>It costs the same to buy it for the krewe as for an individual, you can spend Krewe Experiences on some of the cost of buying it for the krewe, and buying it for the krewe means everyone with enough Mystery Cult Initiation gets it for free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 01-29-2021, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T17:47:32-08:00","id":1433858,"title":"","content":"In our game a geist got the Wavering condition. The book said it required the sin eater to spend a point of willpower to roll &quot;any dice pool, including Synergy&quot; but the PDF doesn't have the comma. So it's just spending a willpower to use your powers.<br /> <br /> Which is it supposed to be?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13508-necrobotany","name":"necrobotany","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T17:50:38-08:00","id":1433859,"title":"","content":"It's pretty clear it's 2 XP per dot, but I agree that it's unreasonably expensive for characters. A five dot Ceremony costs 10 XP! You can also exchange starting Merit dots for Ceremonies, seemingly on a dot for dot basis. Considering that and that werewolf Rites (the closest equivalent that I can think of right now) are one XP per dot, I'd heavily recommend houseruling the XP cost to one XP per dot. At least for Bound characters, giving them a bit of an XP break for being more attuned with Ceremonies due to their ties to deathly energies and all that stuff. It might be more reasonable for Krewes, but I don't have enough experience (hehe) with the Krewe XP economy to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T19:05:35-08:00","id":1433866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>necrobotany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433858#post1433858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In our game a geist got the Wavering condition. The book said it required the sin eater to spend a point of willpower to roll &quot;any dice pool, including Synergy&quot; but the PDF doesn't have the comma. So it's just spending a willpower to use your powers.<br /> <br /> Which is it supposed to be?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter. Worth noting that the list of rolls that include Synergy also includes Intercession attempts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T21:22:54-08:00","id":1433879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433859#post1433859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty clear it's 2 XP per dot, but I agree that it's unreasonably expensive for characters. A five dot Ceremony costs 10 XP! You can also exchange starting Merit dots for Ceremonies, seemingly on a dot for dot basis. Considering that and that werewolf Rites (the closest equivalent that I can think of right now) are one XP per dot, I'd heavily recommend houseruling the XP cost to one XP per dot. At least for Bound characters, giving them a bit of an XP break for being more attuned with Ceremonies due to their ties to deathly energies and all that stuff. It might be more reasonable for Krewes, but I don't have enough experience (hehe) with the Krewe XP economy to say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rites have their character creation exchange rate hard-capped at five dots' worth, can only be rolled for by werewolves and certain types of Wolf-Blooded, are resolved as extended actions that automatically dramatically fail if interrupted and lose three dice on subsequent rolls with a regular failure, and are bound up in packs' relation to the Shadow and their territory.<br /> <br /> Ceremonies are resolved as instant actions with a time prerequisite, can be rolled for by anybody, have a much less onerous consequences for failure and interruption, and every Sin-Eater in a krewe starts with free access to fifteen dots' worth of Ceremonies (with another five gated behind raising their krewe's Esotery and spending 2 Experiences to strengthen their Initiation). The published four- and five-dot Ceremonies let you call up ghosts from anywhere, create lasting instances of the Anchor Condition, and forge new Mementos or Avernian Gates, and even weaker Ceremonies can manage things like staving off Essence Bleed or applying Bans to a location or duplicating a spell that mages need multiple dots in an Arcanum to accomplish. Krewes connect them to their Esotery and attendant mythology; unaffiliated Sin-Eaters and other characters pick them up piecemeal or to suit their particular aims.<br /> <br /> Werewolves with rites are part of a global society of supernatural beings, connected to another world where sources of information and supernatural power tend to persist. Occult knowledge being lost is not as big a concern as it being held by beings that demand payment and/or service for it.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters with krewes have only started being a consistent phenomenon in the last century or so, having previously been the product of temporal flashpoints in history and geography, and primarily interact with another world that combines the two most malicious features of two <i>other</i> otherworlds in addition to being run through with hazards that destroy those immortal conscious beings that interact with them. Lost knowledge is a real issue, particularly when the most probable sources of it are either right bastards or incapable of communicating it immediately (if not both at once).<br /> <br /> Ceremonies are more primarily a thing that krewes have than Sin-Eaters in particular, as evidenced by the whole sidebar about how they don't have any specific tie to the Bound and are just parts of how the world works. It tracks for learning them to be more expensive individually than collectively in a game where collective action is the root of an entire endgame. Sin-Eaters who aren't deep into a death cult don't have a big bag of tricks unless they've done the legwork for it, because the specific tweaks to reality that their nature relies on are innate to their template; mortals and ghosts and mediums likewise don't pick up this knowledge without some pretty deep investment.<br /> <br /> It's the second-cheapest cost in the game and it can be divided across the entire table if you're playing into the side of the game where it matters most. This is a game where your main powerstat has its own Experience type and four sources of free dots. You can afford to spend ten Experiences to learn how to crack open a fresh gate to the Underworld for the rest of the chronicle if you don't want to reach the pinnacle of a powerful religion of the living dead first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 01-30-2021, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-30T12:54:04-08:00","id":1433947,"title":"","content":"Can bound be in Krewes with sin-eaters? Outside of obviously conflicting ideology does a compromise in belief prevent it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-30T14:11:12-08:00","id":1433955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433947#post1433947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can bound be in Krewes with sin-eaters? Outside of obviously conflicting ideology does a compromise in belief prevent it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bound are called so because of their bond to their resident Geist that resurrected them through the Bargain. Sin-Eaters are just a subset of the Bound that are ideologically predisposed to helping ghosts. It's kinda like asking if werewolves can be in packs with the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> But can Sin-Eaters and Bound that aren't considered Sin-Eaters be part of the same krewe? Totally, as long as the doctrines aren't too pro or anti &quot;Sin-Eating&quot; philosophies/activities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-30T15:08:25-08:00","id":1433962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433955#post1433955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Bound are called so because of their bond to their resident Geist that resurrected them through the Bargain. Sin-Eaters are just a subset of the Bound that are ideologically predisposed to helping ghosts. It's kinda like asking if werewolves can be in packs with the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> But can Sin-Eaters and Bound that aren't considered Sin-Eaters be part of the same krewe? Totally, as long as the doctrines aren't too pro or anti &quot;Sin-Eating&quot; philosophies/activities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just wondering whether it was more like the pure and the forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T20:40:06-08:00","id":1434663,"title":"","content":"Can the Bound end Haunt Conditions they created at will? There are some that strongly indicate it - like the Caul Condition, which actually <i>resolves </i>once &quot;the geist is dismissed from their body either willingly or unwillingly&quot; - but I can't find anything that indicates it is possible to simply <i>end the condition because I said so. </i>Maybe I'm missing something, as I have before, so worth the try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12306-andrew-kaninchen","name":"Andrew Kaninchen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T21:32:00-08:00","id":1434664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1433962#post1433962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just wondering whether it was more like the pure and the forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. The Pure wage an ideological war against the Forsaken collectively, and perform a scarring ritual that scours off their auspice and makes them metaphysically distinct from Forsaken werewolves. There is no collective organization or ideology of non-Sin-Eater Bound, nor any intrinsic metaphysical difference. &quot;Sin-Eater&quot; is just a cultural designation, and not one with a clearly agreed upon definition. It's just a word for &quot;I think we Bound have a responsibility to use our powers to better the lot of others, and you don't seem to agree.&quot;<br /> <br /> You could have a case where people argue if a particular Bound is really a Sin-Eater or not. Whether a werewolf is Pure or not is generally an easy call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 02-06-2021, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-06T17:58:08-08:00","id":1434718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andrew Kaninchen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1434663#post1434663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the Bound end Haunt Conditions they created at will? There are some that strongly indicate it - like the Caul Condition, which actually <i>resolves </i>once &quot;the geist is dismissed from their body either willingly or unwillingly&quot; - but I can't find anything that indicates it is possible to simply <i>end the condition because I said so. </i>Maybe I'm missing something, as I have before, so worth the try.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Each condition has its own method of ending. For example, Memoria states that it ends when all charges are spent. Rage ends at the end of the scene. Dirge ends when the Sin-Eater stops singing. Ultimately, I would say it's a matter of interpretation by the Storyteller. <br /> <br /> For me, these are conditions created by the player, unless it would benefit the story, or otherwise be a challenge, I would allow them to end it at will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1907-waywardson74","name":"Waywardson74","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-07T02:04:35-08:00","id":1434740,"title":"","content":"I'm working on a sin-eater character, and his geist died by poisoning. Do you have any good idea about a bane for a poison's victim geist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-07T06:48:42-08:00","id":1434749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1434740#post1434740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm working on a sin-eater character, and his geist died by poisoning. Do you have any good idea about a bane for a poison's victim geist?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Whatever poison killed them&quot; is the first thing that comes to mind. Classics include arsenic, cyanide, and strychnine, but the list of substances that will make a human body stop working is quite long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T12:46:37-08:00","id":1436063,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Boneyard Questions</u></b><br /> <br /> The boneyard ends when you leave the area. Does that mean you have to be INSIDE the area of your boneyard? Or can you stand just outside the space, like pressing a hand on the outside wall? How about ominously standing across the street?<br /> <br /> Are you subject to the penalties of the boneyard while inside it? Such as taking penalties to escape, suffering environmental hazards, or having to obey your own laws?<br /> <br /> Do you count as a faux Kerebos for breaking a Boneyard law?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 02-19-2021, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T19:02:37-08:00","id":1436123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1436063#post1436063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Boneyard Questions</u></b><br /> <br /> The boneyard ends when you leave the area. Does that mean you have to be INSIDE the area of your boneyard? Or can you stand just outside the space, like pressing a hand on the outside wall? How about ominously standing across the street?<br /> <br /> Are you subject to the penalties of the boneyard while inside it? Such as taking penalties to escape, suffering environmental hazards, or having to obey your own laws?<br /> <br /> Do you count as a faux Kerebos for breaking a Boneyard law?</div> </div> </div> </div>To my understanding, they must be inside it. But even then if you really mean standing just outside it, I would leave to storyteller discretion. They are not subject to the penalties, and I think even Laws. Not sure how to answer the last part","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T03:24:03-08:00","id":1436173,"title":"","content":"Hello friends, I'm about to play a crossover as sin-eater. I also have the feeling that soon or later the master will send us into the underworld, but humans, vampires and werewolves can really travel in the underworld just like sin-eaters do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T04:45:51-08:00","id":1436179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1436173#post1436173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello friends, I'm about to play a crossover as sin-eater. I also have the feeling that soon or later the master will send us into the underworld, but humans, vampires and werewolves can really travel in the underworld just like sin-eaters do?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can, but they cannot normally se avernian gates, so they must locate them by various alternative ways.<br /> Also sin eaters have easy ways to open the portals, while other creatures must find the necessary keys.<br /> In the underworld sin eaters can use their innate Keys to navigate, other creatures must use the classical ways.<br /> Add to it that the underworld is empty of nourishing food and blood...<br /> They CAN but what an hellish trip","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T06:22:43-08:00","id":1436193,"title":"","content":"Well, I suppose we can carry some supplies with us, I'm right?<br /> And also, ghosts can eat food from the living world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T09:15:47-08:00","id":1436552,"title":"","content":"This is a bit unclear in 2E (at least, I\u2019m not finding the section dealing with it), but other Realms (like the Shadow) and the Underworld in 1E stated that living things and physical items are converted to ephemera once they cross into the Underworld. Equipment mostly works, but gets unreliable. <br /> IIRC from Book of the Dead (1E), physical food brought into the underworld can nourish the living - and anyone intentionally delving definitely brought those supplies - but that it didn\u2019t provide Essence to ghosts. There seemed to be a difference between objects converted into ephemera and inherently ghostly objects that provided essence; I\u2019m not sure if that carried over to 2E.<br /> <br /> I would rule in my games that mortal food/items cannot sustain ghosts (can\u2019t give Essence), but does retain most of its properties (like taste and utility) - often making it more valuable to ghosts. Being able to truly taste a favored meal, or receiving an instrument they\u2019ll never be tempted to consume for survival being rare moments of hope that would deeply indebt them, and possibly lead to discovering how they Resolve. But YMMV.<br /> Usually the Living have more direct ways of nourishing ghosts, particularly non-Bound who are able to interact with them. Just remembering them or leaving minor offerings can bestow a point of Essence or two, and would probably be even easier in the Underworld. <br /> I think that, after being converted to ephemera, I would rule objects can\u2019t be destroyed in a way that creates Castoffs, though. That feels like a process that should happen in the mortal world... but that\u2019s just my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 02-22-2021, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T00:37:01-08:00","id":1437437,"title":"","content":"Do you think it s possible to use Haunts remotely with the Boneyard enhancement Eyes in the Paintings?<br /> Marionette in particular, the condition resolves when the target exits the sin eater line of sight, but does sensory enhancement (the Boneyard, binoculars) counts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T15:51:10-08:00","id":1437544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1437437#post1437437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think it s possible to use Haunts remotely with the Boneyard enhancement Eyes in the Paintings?<br /> Marionette in particular, the condition resolves when the target exits the sin eater line of sight, but does sensory enhancement (the Boneyard, binoculars) counts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rules as written, it should but ask your ST about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"us