other Bound can see it.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad, I was too lazy to check the corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T20:55:21-07:00","id":1466602,"title":"","content":"Do Geists get Willpower from sleeping?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T11:59:03-08:00","id":1470062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1466602#post1466602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Geists get Willpower from sleeping?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean Sin Eaters or the Geists themselves that they have? Because I don\u2019t remember Geists having their own Willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T15:04:23-08:00","id":1470078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1466602#post1466602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Geists get Willpower from sleeping?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bound geists share Willpower with their Sin-Eater. As for Sin-Eaters, per the FAQ in the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Do characters regain Willpower from sleeping?</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As described in the Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook, humans regain Willpower when they get a good night\u2019s rest, and so do most monsters.<br /> <br /> Not everyone does, though. Complicating that, not every core book says whether a monster does or not, nor draws the line clearly between a given monster type and humans.<br /> <br /> The general rule is: \u201cIs sleeping truly restful for this creature? Does it help connect them to themself and affirm their identity, or does it erode it?\u201d Even a sleep filled with nightmares can be inherently fulfilling, allowing a character to see their fears clearly in a way they can\u2019t in the waking world.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-24T05:59:33-08:00","id":1471191,"title":"","content":"Hello guys!<br /> <br /> When a sin-eater meet a tryant boud, do you think he can feel the tyranny?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-24T12:18:21-08:00","id":1471205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1471191#post1471191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello guys!<br /> <br /> When a sin-eater meet a tryant boud, do you think he can feel the tyranny?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's a universal sense, but you can probably tell from observing the way a Bound treats their Geist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T02:59:25-08:00","id":1471320,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone, I'm going to join a geist game soon and the corebook so far seems pretty straigthforward compared to the other splats, the only things I don't get is what a geist rank effectively does in game terms and what does it mean when it says that the geist treat its key as influence, does it add a dice bonus or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 12-27-2021, 06:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T05:19:58-08:00","id":1471325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1471320#post1471320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone, I'm going to join a geist game soon and the corebook so far seems pretty straigthforward compared to the other splats, the only things I don't get is what a geist rank effectively does in game terms and what does it mean when it says that the geist treat its key as influence, does it add a dice bonus or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Bound geist's Sin-Eater treats their effective Rank as the lower of their geist's Rank and their Synergy, which allows them to treat their touch as a bane against a ghost they outrank by at least 2 Ranks; an Unleashed geist is treated as having Influences in any innate Keys it knows with ratings equal to its Rank, allowing it to Strengthen, Manipulate, and Control instances of those forms of death at the bare minimum, with more powerful geists being able to Create or Mass Create those phenomena as well, as per the rules for ghosts on pages 190-191.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T06:28:42-08:00","id":1471327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1471325#post1471325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Bound geist's Sin-Eater treats their effective Rank as the lower of their geist's Rank and their Synergy, which allows them to treat their touch as a bane against a ghost they outrank by at least 2 Ranks; an Unleashed geist is treated as having Influences in any innate Keys it knows with ratings equal to its Rank, allowing it to Strengthen, Manipulate, and Control instances of those forms of death at the bare minimum, with more powerful geists being able to Create or Mass Create those phenomena as well, as per the rules for ghosts on pages 190-191.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you, what are some practical instances of this form of deaths? for example, the key of burning flame would allow a geist to weaponize fire? is it similar to the werewolf gifts that deal with elements?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T07:10:39-08:00","id":1471331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1471327#post1471327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thank you, what are some practical instances of this form of deaths? for example, the key of burning flame would allow a geist to weaponize fire? is it similar to the werewolf gifts that deal with elements?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, yes; look at the concrete phenomena the Key corresponds to and filter that through the description for the Influence level being used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T07:16:03-08:00","id":1471332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1471331#post1471331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, yes; look at the concrete phenomena the Key corresponds to and filter that through the description for the Influence level being used.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I didn't expect geists to be this powerful, acting as a bane would also work on death spirits and spirits that have influence on death correct? I think I'm going to enjoy this splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 12-27-2021, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-12T09:36:35-08:00","id":1472314,"title":"","content":"I'm a little confused about the geist once unleashed, particularly when the sin eater gets the dead condition, once unleashed the geist gets corpus just like any other ghost but what happens when its health track is full of lethal or aggravated? I'm not talking about a weaponized ban, just normal damage, does the geist die for good and so does the sin eater or it just goes back to twilight and the sin eater gets resurrected at the end of the scene as usual?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-12T17:19:57-08:00","id":1472334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1472314#post1472314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little confused about the geist once unleashed, particularly when the sin eater gets the dead condition, once unleashed the geist gets corpus just like any other ghost but what happens when its health track is full of lethal or aggravated? I'm not talking about a weaponized ban, just normal damage, does the geist die for good and so does the sin eater or it just goes back to twilight and the sin eater gets resurrected at the end of the scene as usual?</div> </div> </div> </div>It explicitly says what happens when the geist's Corpus track is full of lethal or aggravated damage in the text of the Unleashed Condition, because that's the Resolution state for that Condition. Resolving the Condition instead of having it go away causes the Weakened Bond Condition (two Conditions down in the listing) to resolve at the end of the scene after the scene where the Unleashed geist is discorporated.<br /> <br /> If the geist is Unleashed because the Sin-Eater is Dead, what happens if it runs out of Corpus is likewise described in the text of the Dead Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-12T18:59:44-08:00","id":1472340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1472334#post1472334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It explicitly says what happens when the geist's Corpus track is full of lethal or aggravated damage in the text of the Unleashed Condition, because that's the Resolution state for that Condition. Resolving the Condition instead of having it go away causes the Weakened Bond Condition (two Conditions down in the listing) to resolve at the end of the scene after the scene where the Unleashed geist is discorporated.<br /> <br /> If the geist is Unleashed because the Sin-Eater is Dead, what happens if it runs out of Corpus is likewise described in the text of the Dead Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes but the dead condition says that they both die if the geist is destroyed of consumed, doesn't a geist just discorporate if its health track is full? I thought only banes and another sin eater consuming it could kill a geist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-12T19:57:01-08:00","id":1472348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1472340#post1472340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but the dead condition says that they both die if the geist is destroyed of consumed, doesn't a geist just discorporate if its health track is full?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <i>If the Sin-Eater it's Bound to isn't Dead, which specifically changes what happens when an Unleashed geist is destroyed while it is the only active part of the player character due to that Condition.</i><br /> <br /> Per the Ghost section's text on Damage on page 195, a ghost with no Essence whose rightmost Corpus box is filled with worse-than-bashing damage is destroyed. In the case of normal ghosts, that's &quot;destroyed utterly,&quot; and in the case of geists, they leave behind a deathmask \u2014 a type of memento variously described as dead objects and the product of destroying a geist; the sidebar on page 131 describes how the &quot;corpse&quot; of a destroyed geist lingers for a bit before it settles into a deathmask.<br /> <br /> Bound geists have Plasm instead of Essence in the first place, and an Unleashed geist specifically loses all the Plasm it was holding if it loses all its Corpus to lethal or aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I thought only banes and another sin eater consuming it could kill a geist. </div> </div> </div>If you're killed with your geist's Bane, in a manner that resonates with your original death, or when you're at Synergy 0, you skip straight past the Dead Condition to being irrevocably dead, as described in the section on Death on page 98.<br /> <br /> If you have the Dead Condition from dying in circumstances where none of the above three circumstances are true, then your geist is Unleashed for the rest of the scene and you die with it if its Corpus is filled with lethal or aggravated damage, per the text of that Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T03:55:51-08:00","id":1472356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1472348#post1472348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes.<br /> <br /> <i>If the Sin-Eater it's Bound to isn't Dead, which specifically changes what happens when an Unleashed geist is destroyed while it is the only active part of the player character due to that Condition.</i><br /> <br /> Per the Ghost section's text on Damage on page 195, a ghost with no Essence whose rightmost Corpus box is filled with worse-than-bashing damage is destroyed. In the case of normal ghosts, that's &quot;destroyed utterly,&quot; and in the case of geists, they leave behind a deathmask \u2014 a type of memento variously described as dead objects and the product of destroying a geist; the sidebar on page 131 describes how the &quot;corpse&quot; of a destroyed geist lingers for a bit before it settles into a deathmask.<br /> <br /> Bound geists have Plasm instead of Essence in the first place, and an Unleashed geist specifically loses all the Plasm it was holding if it loses all its Corpus to lethal or aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> If you're killed with your geist's Bane, in a manner that resonates with your original death, or when you're at Synergy 0, you skip straight past the Dead Condition to being irrevocably dead, as described in the section on Death on page 98.<br /> <br /> If you have the Dead Condition from dying in circumstances where none of the above three circumstances are true, then your geist is Unleashed for the rest of the scene and you die with it if its Corpus is filled with lethal or aggravated damage, per the text of that Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T17:17:38-08:00","id":1472394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1472348#post1472348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes.<br /> <br /> <i>If the Sin-Eater it's Bound to isn't Dead, which specifically changes what happens when an Unleashed geist is destroyed while it is the only active part of the player character due to that Condition.</i><br /> <br /> Per the Ghost section's text on Damage on page 195, a ghost with no Essence whose rightmost Corpus box is filled with worse-than-bashing damage is destroyed. In the case of normal ghosts, that's &quot;destroyed utterly,&quot; and in the case of geists, they leave behind a deathmask \u2014 a type of memento variously described as dead objects and the product of destroying a geist; the sidebar on page 131 describes how the &quot;corpse&quot; of a destroyed geist lingers for a bit before it settles into a deathmask.<br /> <br /> Bound geists have Plasm instead of Essence in the first place, and an Unleashed geist specifically loses all the Plasm it was holding if it loses all its Corpus to lethal or aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> If you're killed with your geist's Bane, in a manner that resonates with your original death, or when you're at Synergy 0, you skip straight past the Dead Condition to being irrevocably dead, as described in the section on Death on page 98.<br /> <br /> If you have the Dead Condition from dying in circumstances where none of the above three circumstances are true, then your geist is Unleashed for the rest of the scene and you die with it if its Corpus is filled with lethal or aggravated damage, per the text of that Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry to bother you again but can you point me at what page it says that a geist loses all its plasm if its Corpus is filled with lethal or aggravated? I have only read this about the sin eater when the unleashed condition is resolved while the bound is still alive, I didn't find anything that says that the geist loses all its plasm the same way when the bound is already dead, I'm sorry if I'm being insistent with this but I wanted to make a recurring geist character for my game and need to know if a geist can cut its lossess and just rematerialize like ghosts do either at their anchor or in the underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T18:07:28-08:00","id":1472396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1472394#post1472394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to bother you again but can you point me at what page it says that a geist loses all its plasm if its Corpus is filled with lethal or aggravated? I have only read this about the sin eater when the unleashed condition is resolved while the bound is still alive, I didn't find anything that says that the geist loses all its plasm the same way when the bound is already dead, I'm sorry if I'm being insistent with this but I wanted to make a recurring geist character for my game and need to know if a geist can cut its lossess and just rematerialize like ghosts do either at their anchor or in the underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Unleashed Condition ends one of two ways:<br /> 1. It ends without resolving at the end of the scene, per the main text of the Condition.<br /> 2. It ends sooner when the Condition is resolved by its Resolution criterion being met, that being a full Corpus track of lethal or aggravated damage; this gives the Sin-Eater a Synergy Beat and causes them to lose all their remaining Plasm.<br /> <br /> If a Sin-Eater loses all their remaining Plasm, their geist has also lost all their remaining Plasm, because the text of the Unleashed Condition specifies that the geist shares Plasm and Willpower pools with their Sin-Eater, and this is corroborated by the sidebar on Bound geists' &quot;missing&quot; Traits on page 76.<br /> <br /> Because they aren't merged with another person, un-Bound geists do not have this problem, and instead operate on the same rules as ghosts do, plus the adjustments presented for geists on page 197.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-14T06:30:58-08:00","id":1472428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1472396#post1472396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Unleashed Condition ends one of two ways:<br /> 1. It ends without resolving at the end of the scene, per the main text of the Condition.<br /> 2. It ends sooner when the Condition is resolved by its Resolution criterion being met, that being a full Corpus track of lethal or aggravated damage; this gives the Sin-Eater a Synergy Beat and causes them to lose all their remaining Plasm.<br /> <br /> If a Sin-Eater loses all their remaining Plasm, their geist has also lost all their remaining Plasm, because the text of the Unleashed Condition specifies that the geist shares Plasm and Willpower pools with their Sin-Eater, and this is corroborated by the sidebar on Bound geists' &quot;missing&quot; Traits on page 76.<br /> <br /> Because they aren't merged with another person, un-Bound geists do not have this problem, and instead operate on the same rules as ghosts do, plus the adjustments presented for geists on page 197.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes but the damage section at page 195 states that ghosts (it doesn't exclude geists) whose rightmost Corpus box is filled with lethal or aggravated but has 1 essence left (plasm for the geist), dissolves into plasm and reforms in hibernation to the nearest anchor in the living world (in the geist case it would be its sin eater) or on the shore of the nearest river in the underworld, since geists are still ghosts and it doesn't otherwise says that this rules don't apply to them, I figured that the only way to kill a geist (not a sin eater) other than it draining its plasm and filling it of lethal or aggravated, was to use its ban but I don't really have experience in this game so I don't know how to interpret it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-14T08:31:55-08:00","id":1472443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1472428#post1472428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes but the damage section at page 195 states that ghosts (it doesn't exclude geists) whose rightmost Corpus box is filled with lethal or aggravated but has 1 essence left (plasm for the geist), dissolves into plasm and reforms in hibernation to the nearest anchor in the living world (in the geist case it would be its sin eater) or on the shore of the nearest river in the underworld, since geists are still ghosts and it doesn't otherwise says that this rules don't apply to them, I figured that the only way to kill a geist (not a sin eater) other than it draining its plasm and filling it of lethal or aggravated, was to use its ban but I don't really have experience in this game so I don't know how to interpret it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don t think that the sin eater works as an anchor for the geist.<br /> Does the core book states it somewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-14T09:38:19-08:00","id":1472451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1472443#post1472443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don t think that the sin eater works as an anchor for the geist.<br /> Does the core book states it somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are right the book actually state that they don't have one but I think it refers to bound geists since in the condition description, it says that they don't suffer essence bleed while bound just like with anchors so I assume that the sin eater works as an anchor of sorts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-14T17:42:33-08:00","id":1472483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1472428#post1472428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but the damage section at page 195 states that ghosts (it doesn't exclude geists) whose rightmost Corpus box is filled with lethal or aggravated but has 1 essence left (plasm for the geist)</div> </div> </div> </div>Again: The contents of the Unleashed Condition specify that a full track of severe Corpus damage makes the pair of you lose all your Plasm. This is the tradeoff of being Bound: the geist is largely invulnerable to harm until it is Unleashed, at which point it is Materialized and therefore susceptible to harm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> dissolves into plasm and reforms in hibernation to the nearest anchor in the living world (in the geist case it would be its sin eater) </div> </div> </div>In the geist's case they don't have Anchors and are bound to their Sin-Eater until the Sin-Eater dies for good, per the Bound Geist Condition given to the geist by the Bargain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or on the shore of the nearest river in the underworld, since geists are still ghosts and it doesn't otherwise says that this rules don't apply to them, </div> </div> </div>A Bound geist functionally does not exist as an accessible actor unless it is Unleashed. Avoiding the entire Manifestation system and the economy it entails is half the point of the Bargain \u2014 it doesn't have Corpus while it's not Unleashed, and running out of Corpus while it's Unleashed causes it to lose all its Plasm in a way that it wouldn't lose all its Essence while unbound, and the tradeoff is that if you kill its host and then kill it, <i>it is dead</i>, which is a fantastic incentive for it to either keep its host alive or get along very poorly indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I figured that the only way to kill a geist (not a sin eater) other than it draining its plasm and filling it of lethal or aggravated, was to use its ban but I don't really have experience in this game so I don't know how to interpret it. </div> </div> </div>As a Materialized ghost, an Unleashed geist takes aggravated damage from its bane and suffer only bashing damage from anything else that doesn't specifically do worse damage to ghosts (such as unarmed attacks enhanced by the Rage). The extra layer of necessary steps to force a bound geist to be accessible to violence takes the place of the ability to reform with a single point of Essence while it lasts, because not needing to worry about maintaining that safety margin to be safe from permanent destruction is, again, half the point of the Bargain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1472451#post1472451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are right the book actually state that they don't have one but I think it refers to bound geists since in the condition description, it says that they don't suffer essence bleed while bound just like with anchors so I assume that the sin eater works as an anchor of sorts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Outside of specific circumstances, a bound geist is not a tangible thing in the world. It doesn't have or need Anchors, because it is linked to its Sin-Eater at the heart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-14T18:00:18-08:00","id":1472485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1472483#post1472483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again: The contents of the Unleashed Condition specify that a full track of severe Corpus damage makes the pair of you lose all your Plasm. This is the tradeoff of being Bound: the geist is largely invulnerable to harm until it is Unleashed, at which point it is Materialized and therefore susceptible to harm.<br /> <br /> In the geist's case they don't have Anchors and are bound to their Sin-Eater until the Sin-Eater dies for good, per the Bound Geist Condition given to the geist by the Bargain.<br /> <br /> A Bound geist functionally does not exist as an accessible actor unless it is Unleashed. Avoiding the entire Manifestation system and the economy it entails is half the point of the Bargain \u2014 it doesn't have Corpus while it's not Unleashed, and running out of Corpus while it's Unleashed causes it to lose all its Plasm in a way that it wouldn't lose all its Essence while unbound, and the tradeoff is that if you kill its host and then kill it, <i>it is dead</i>, which is a fantastic incentive for it to either keep its host alive or get along very poorly indeed.<br /> <br /> As a Materialized ghost, an Unleashed geist takes aggravated damage from its bane and suffer only bashing damage from anything else that doesn't specifically do worse damage to ghosts (such as unarmed attacks enhanced by the Rage). The extra layer of necessary steps to force a bound geist to be accessible to violence takes the place of the ability to reform with a single point of Essence while it lasts, because not needing to worry about maintaining that safety margin to be safe from permanent destruction is, again, half the point of the Bargain.<br /> <br /> Outside of specific circumstances, a bound geist is not a tangible thing in the world. It doesn't have or need Anchors, because it is linked to its Sin-Eater at the heart.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks again for the answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T05:21:32-08:00","id":1473567,"title":"","content":"I have some questions regarding plasmic healing, the book says that plasm degrades aggravated to lethal and lethal to bashing, does it also mean that it can downgrade bashing damage to heal it completely? also regarding tilts, the book says that any tilt caused by physical damage can be removed so something like arm whack can be eliminated altogether but what about poison and diseases? how much plasm would it take to remove the poisoned or the sick tilt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T05:25:13-08:00","id":1473568,"title":"","content":"I have some questions regarding plasmic healing, the book says that plasm downgrades aggravated to lethal and lethal to bashing, does it also means that it can downgrade bashing thus healing an healtbox completely? also regarding tilts, the book says that plasm can also remove any tilt caused by physical damage but what about tilts like poisoned and sick? how much plasm is needed to heal poisons and diseases like cold or cancer?<br /> <br /> Edit: sorry for the double post, the site was slow and didn't post the first time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 01-30-2022, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T07:46:02-08:00","id":1473577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1473567#post1473567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some questions regarding plasmic healing, the book says that plasm degrades aggravated to lethal and lethal to bashing, does it also mean that it can downgrade bashing damage to heal it completely? also regarding tilts, the book says that any tilt caused by physical damage can be removed so something like arm whack can be eliminated altogether but what about poison and diseases? how much plasm would it take to remove the poisoned or the sick tilt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Plasmic Healing is 2e's equivalent of 1e's Ectoplasmic Flesh mechanic, which worked by negating damage as it happened (marking the absorbed damage in the process) and then converting it to bashing damage at the end of the scene, so between that, the Bound immunity to being knocked unconscious or bleeding out, and the fact that Plasmic Healing is only harder after the fact (instead of impossible, as with Ectoplasmic Flesh), I would say this is a mechanic where &quot;downgrade&quot; doesn't extend to &quot;fully heal instantly.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Tilts caused by physical damage&quot; refers to any of the Tilts whose &quot;Ending the Tilt&quot; criteria includes something to the effect of &quot;this Tilt ends when the damage that caused it has healed,&quot; i.e. Tilts you can inflict with a targeted attack, as detailed in the chart on page 157 (plus Deafened, which works the same way but isn't listed on that chart).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T08:07:03-08:00","id":1473578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1473577#post1473577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plasmic Healing is 2e's equivalent of 1e's Ectoplasmic Flesh mechanic, which worked by negating damage as it happened (marking the absorbed damage in the process) and then converting it to bashing damage at the end of the scene, so between that, the Bound immunity to being knocked unconscious or bleeding out, and the fact that Plasmic Healing is only harder after the fact (instead of impossible, as with Ectoplasmic Flesh), I would say this is a mechanic where &quot;downgrade&quot; doesn't extend to &quot;fully heal instantly.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Tilts caused by physical damage&quot; refers to any of the Tilts whose &quot;Ending the Tilt&quot; criteria includes something to the effect of &quot;this Tilt ends when the damage that caused it has healed,&quot; i.e. Tilts you can inflict with a targeted attack, as detailed in the chart on page 157 (plus Deafened, which works the same way but isn't listed on that chart).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you again for the answers, so this means that a bound can be killed (although he would revive again as usual) by mundane things like poison, drug overdose and other ilnesses, without being able to heal them, is that correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T08:24:17-08:00","id":1473579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1473578#post1473578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you again for the answers, so this means that a bound can be killed (although he would revive again as usual) by mundane things like poison, drug overdose and other ilnesses, without being able to heal them, is that correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, albeit the Key of Disease is resonant with some of those things, diseases need to be grave sicknesses to cause damage, the Caul can be used to substitute your geist's Resistance for your Stamina and/or Resolve, the damage from the Poisoned Tilt can be resisted turn-by-turn with successful Stamina + Resolve rolls, and damage from both poisons and diseases can likewise be resisted at each interval of their infliction outside of action scenes.<br /> <br /> In 1e your Psyche rating added flatly to rolls to resist poisons and diseases, but in 2e that's most readily represented by taking the Hardy Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T09:19:51-08:00","id":1473580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1473579#post1473579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct, albeit the Key of Disease is resonant with some of those things, diseases need to be grave sicknesses to cause damage, the Caul can be used to substitute your geist's Resistance for your Stamina and/or Resolve, the damage from the Poisoned Tilt can be resisted turn-by-turn with successful Stamina + Resolve rolls, and damage from both poisons and diseases can likewise be resisted at each interval of their infliction outside of action scenes.<br /> <br /> In 1e your Psyche rating added flatly to rolls to resist poisons and diseases, but in 2e that's most readily represented by taking the Hardy Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T13:30:51-08:00","id":1473856,"title":"","content":"It's time for a silly question!<br /> <br /> Ghosts can hide themselves from the Bounds' sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T16:07:43-08:00","id":1473873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1473856#post1473856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's time for a silly question!<br /> <br /> Ghosts can hide themselves from the Bounds' sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure! As long as they succeed on a stealth check, they should be able to hide no problem, and I think there is a numen that makes it even more easier to go by unnoticed<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25516-pinkhaunt","name":"PinkHaunt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T04:40:25-08:00","id":1473893,"title":"","content":"But they can become invisible or just hide somwhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T05:14:24-08:00","id":1473894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1473893#post1473893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they can become invisible or just hide somwhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>They would have to hide somewhere, since they're as visible as normal people to the Bound and their default state of being is invisible to everyone who can't see ghosts. The Innocuous Numen subtracts two dice from rolls to notice the ghost who has it, which can help, but without a form of invisibility that doesn't rely on the state of Twilight they'll need to get out of sight like a human person would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T09:23:41-08:00","id":1473978,"title":"","content":"Ok this might be a dumb question but how do enhancements to haunts actually work? you have to spend each time the plasma required to activate the effect or you just spend it once and get to use the effect for as many times as you have charges, for example, the 4th level of the boneyard haunt lets you spend 3 plasm to create an enviromental tilt, do you need to spend 3 plasm everytime you want to create such an effect or you only need to spend it once and then use the standard charges from the haunt to activate it?<br /> <br /> Regarding haunts that don't give charges like the rage, would all the effect like inflicting tilts and aggravated damage require spending plasm each time or only once?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T15:23:35-08:00","id":1474000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1473978#post1473978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok this might be a dumb question but how do enhancements to haunts actually work? you have to spend each time the plasma required to activate the effect or you just spend it once and get to use the effect for as many times as you have charges, for example, the 4th level of the boneyard haunt lets you spend 3 plasm to create an enviromental tilt, do you need to spend 3 plasm everytime you want to create such an effect or you only need to spend it once and then use the standard charges from the haunt to activate it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Boneyard doesn't have charges to spend at all \u2014 you spend 3 Plasm and create one Environmental Tilt, and you do this as many times as you wish to spend 3 Plasm on creating Environmental Tilts in an active Boneyard you control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regarding haunts that don't give charges like the rage, would all the effect like inflicting tilts and aggravated damage require spending plasm each time or only once? </div> </div> </div>The Rage's Enhancements all specify that they affect &quot;the next&quot; attack, instance of damage, or breaking point, except for Breaking the World, which specifies that it creates one Tilt for the expenditure. You spend the Plasm and the effect happens once and then you have to spend the Plasm again to do it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T16:03:59-08:00","id":1474007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1474000#post1474000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Boneyard doesn't have charges to spend at all \u2014 you spend 3 Plasm and create one Environmental Tilt, and you do this as many times as you wish to spend 3 Plasm on creating Environmental Tilts in an active Boneyard you control.<br /> <br /> The Rage's Enhancements all specify that they affect &quot;the next&quot; attack, instance of damage, or breaking point, except for Breaking the World, which specifies that it creates one Tilt for the expenditure. You spend the Plasm and the effect happens once and then you have to spend the Plasm again to do it again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank, regarding the haunts that have charges instead like the Caul? do you need to spend plasma every single time you wish to apply the effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T17:08:44-08:00","id":1474012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1474007#post1474007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank, regarding the haunts that have charges instead like the Caul? do you need to spend plasma every single time you wish to apply the effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at the Haunts whose Conditions have charges\u2026<br /> <br /> The Caul's Cold Flesh Enhancement lasts for the length of the Haunt and doesn't interact with the charge mechanic. Its Vitiate Enhancements either work like the two-dot Enhancement or specify that they apply to the Sin-Eater's next attack and can be applied more than once. Disarticulation specifies that it can be applies more than once and says nothing about how long the homunculi last (and can therefore be assumed to last as long as the Haunt persists). The Hungry Dead has a use prerequisite and adds options to the Caul Condition, which means it lasts as long as the Haunt lasts.<br /> <br /> The Curse's Gremlin Enhancement specifies that each expenditure of Plasm adds one of its items to the options you can spend charges from the Curse Condition on, and it specifies you can apply the Enhancement more than once because there's more than one option; since these options are added to the list of options by the Enhancement, it lasts as long as the Haunt does. Same goes for Malady, Exhaustion, and Forgotten.<br /> <br /> The Memoria has no Enhancements that interact with the charge mechanic besides Memory in a Bottle giving you more charges. D\u00e9nouement does one thing for the duration of the Haunt. Memory in a Bottle ends the Haunt with the chance to resume it later. Mystery Play builds off of D\u00e9nouement and so does Break the Cycle.<br /> <br /> The Oracle's Wandering Shade and Spirit Reading Enhancements have you pay 1 and 2 Plasm respectively to add their entire set of questions to the list of questions you can spend charges from the Oracle Condition for the duration of the Haunt. Descent doesn't interact with the charge system but can be applied multiple times, such that each question about the Underworld costs 3 Plasm. Nekyia doesn't interact with the charge system and cannot be applied multiple times, so you spend 4 plasm and get one question about future events before you'll need to use the Haunt a separate time.<br /> <br /> The Shroud's Vision of Mist Enhancements last for the length of the Haunt and don't interact with the charge mechanic. Ditto for Haunting Presence aside from the Free effect permanently adjusting one of the options on the list of things you can spend charges on. Harrow and Descent add options to the list for the Shroud Condition and thus last for the length of the Haunt.<br /> <br /> There is nothing to indicate that any Enhancement that doesn't specify otherwise has a duration different than what the general rules for Haunts on page 101 say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T18:20:44-08:00","id":1474016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1474012#post1474012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the Haunts whose Conditions have charges\u2026<br /> <br /> The Caul's Cold Flesh Enhancement lasts for the length of the Haunt and doesn't interact with the charge mechanic. Its Vitiate Enhancements either work like the two-dot Enhancement or specify that they apply to the Sin-Eater's next attack and can be applied more than once. Disarticulation specifies that it can be applies more than once and says nothing about how long the homunculi last (and can therefore be assumed to last as long as the Haunt persists). The Hungry Dead has a use prerequisite and adds options to the Caul Condition, which means it lasts as long as the Haunt lasts.<br /> <br /> The Curse's Gremlin Enhancement specifies that each expenditure of Plasm adds one of its items to the options you can spend charges from the Curse Condition on, and it specifies you can apply the Enhancement more than once because there's more than one option; since these options are added to the list of options by the Enhancement, it lasts as long as the Haunt does. Same goes for Malady, Exhaustion, and Forgotten.<br /> <br /> The Memoria has no Enhancements that interact with the charge mechanic besides Memory in a Bottle giving you more charges. D\u00e9nouement does one thing for the duration of the Haunt. Memory in a Bottle ends the Haunt with the chance to resume it later. Mystery Play builds off of D\u00e9nouement and so does Break the Cycle.<br /> <br /> The Oracle's Wandering Shade and Spirit Reading Enhancements have you pay 1 and 2 Plasm respectively to add their entire set of questions to the list of questions you can spend charges from the Oracle Condition for the duration of the Haunt. Descent doesn't interact with the charge system but can be applied multiple times, such that each question about the Underworld costs 3 Plasm. Nekyia doesn't interact with the charge system and cannot be applied multiple times, so you spend 4 plasm and get one question about future events before you'll need to use the Haunt a separate time.<br /> <br /> The Shroud's Vision of Mist Enhancements last for the length of the Haunt and don't interact with the charge mechanic. Ditto for Haunting Presence aside from the Free effect permanently adjusting one of the options on the list of things you can spend charges on. Harrow and Descent add options to the list for the Shroud Condition and thus last for the length of the Haunt.<br /> <br /> There is nothing to indicate that any Enhancement that doesn't specify otherwise has a duration different than what the general rules for Haunts on page 101 say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T14:18:55-08:00","id":1475359,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm blind, but I can't seem to find how many dots of Haunts a starter Bound has? Or Touchstones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T15:06:19-08:00","id":1475365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1475359#post1475359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm blind, but I can't seem to find how many dots of Haunts a starter Bound has? Or Touchstones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 74, &quot;Sin-Eater Template&quot; has the lot; the information on Touchstone Basics on page 83 and the Synergy chart on page 91 should make it clear how many Touchstones you should have as a starting character, depending on how many starting Merit dots you've spent on Synergy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-26T05:57:53-08:00","id":1475487,"title":"","content":"Happy week end to everyone!<br /> <br /> This is one of my strage questions: do you think a geist can learn skills from his human partner? I mean, if a geist make a bound with a martial artist, then the little god of death can learn how to fight with the kung-fu style?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-26T06:21:22-08:00","id":1475488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1475487#post1475487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of my strage questions: do you think a geist can learn skills from his human partner? I mean, if a geist make a bound with a martial artist, then the little god of death can learn how to fight with the kung-fu style?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can flavor the way your geist uses its Attributes however you like, but if your geist is Unleashed it's using the stats it has as described in the Geist Creation section and the modifications described in the Unleashed Condition.<br /> <br /> You're playing one of the Bound, not their geist nor one of the Absent. Your geist doesn't &quot;learn&quot; in any sense that allows it to pick up Skill dots or Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T09:00:34-08:00","id":1475840,"title":"","content":"Would an Avernian Gate be a valid target for the Skeleton Key Ceremony ? The intent is to allow the krewe to have a preferred and quick access point to the Underworld","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 03-05-2022, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T09:17:26-08:00","id":1475841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1475840#post1475840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would an Avernian Gate be a valid target for the Skeleton Key Ceremony ? Such thay the krewe would have a preferred and quick access point to the Underworld</div> </div> </div> </div>Avernian Gates aren't closed by locks, so no. A better method would be to get Inspired or Informed when Picking the Lock to try and get an easier Exceptional Success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-10T18:17:19-08:00","id":1476183,"title":"","content":"Anyone know what the Theophany Condition is for? Is it something that was meant to be cut, or is it called something else and the name wasn't changed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-10T18:57:17-08:00","id":1476184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1476183#post1476183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone know what the Theophany Condition is for? Is it something that was meant to be cut, or is it called something else and the name wasn't changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the distinct feeling it was supposed to be for something leading up to Catabasis, but I'm pretty sure it's been a weird development fossil since the KS manuscripts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T06:52:31-07:00","id":1476323,"title":"","content":"RP question, how much can Geists communicate with their Sin-Eaters? Can they talk and exchange dialogues? Or is it limited to the Geist doing signs or mimics? Or does it vary on the Geist? That always was a source of confusion for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T08:44:52-07:00","id":1476324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1476323#post1476323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RP question, how much can Geists communicate with their Sin-Eaters? Can they talk and exchange dialogues? Or is it limited to the Geist doing signs or mimics? Or does it vary on the Geist? That always was a source of confusion for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unbound geists roll a chance die on all social rolls outside the context of frightening or intimidating (and apply the same limitation to social rolls made against them), per the Broken quality.<br /> <br /> The descriptions of the levels of Relationship seem to indicate that even at a Coercive level both halves of a Sin-Eater can understand each other's immediate desires, with higher levels of Synergy affording a stronger understanding of each other's emotions and goals.<br /> <br /> Your geist can't sit down and have a frank conversation with you, but it can be cryptic and unsettling and terrifying in helpful ways just fine, and the Tyrannous lean into that being the only language it clearly understands without being more powerfully aligned. Most of its contribution is going to be crisis points and shared gut feelings as you help solve the mystery of its Remembrance and wrap up your unfinished business.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T09:57:35-07:00","id":1476326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1476323#post1476323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RP question, how much can Geists communicate with their Sin-Eaters? Can they talk and exchange dialogues? Or is it limited to the Geist doing signs or mimics? Or does it vary on the Geist? That always was a source of confusion for me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The way I imagine geists is not that they can't talk, they are not mindless monsters, its just that they have been so detached from their humanity that they forgot how normal human beings interact, I can imagine a geist singing an old lullaby, although she wouldn't know where she learned it, a geist could insult and demean his bound akin to a drill sergeant but if asked, he wouldn't even remember ever serving in the military, other geists might be able to carry semi coherent conversations but chose not to because they don't see the point of it anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T15:50:38-07:00","id":1476342,"title":"","content":"okay thanks, i'll try to work with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T10:55:29-07:00","id":1479718,"title":"","content":"Do Ceremonies that affect ghosts work on geists as well?<br /> <br /> Also, while scanning over the list of Ceremonies to make sure my question made sense, another arose: If a casting of Forge Anchor is contested by the subject, does the celebrant still subtract the ghost's Rank from their dice pool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T15:41:37-07:00","id":1479755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1479718#post1479718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Ceremonies that affect ghosts work on geists as well?<br /> <br /> Also, while scanning over the list of Ceremonies to make sure my question made sense, another arose: If a casting of Forge Anchor is contested by the subject, does the celebrant still subtract the ghost's Rank from their dice pool?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect most Ceremonies work on geists just fine\u2026 when they aren\u2019t Bound in a Bargain at the moment.<br /> <br /> For the latter, my knee-jerk response is that the contest doesn\u2019t happen for willing targets, Ceremony or not. My kneecaps could be rusty tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T16:27:13-07:00","id":1479759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1479718#post1479718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Ceremonies that affect ghosts work on geists as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're specifically ghosts, so yes, with the possible exception of Forge Anchor for reasons of verisimilitude.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, while scanning over the list of Ceremonies to make sure my question made sense, another arose: If a casting of Forge Anchor is contested by the subject, does the celebrant still subtract the ghost's Rank from their dice pool? </div> </div> </div>It's outside of the parenthetical for unwilling targets and is the kind of thing that makes sense to be harder to manage on more powerful ghosts whether they cooperate or not, so yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T08:47:07-07:00","id":1480835,"title":"","content":"Do you think it s possible to use The Caul power The hungry dead on a ghost without commicting ectophagia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T12:05:51-07:00","id":1480848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1480835#post1480835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think it s possible to use The Caul power The hungry dead on a ghost without commicting ectophagia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the specific wording of the text (&quot;If the Sin-Eater consumed the target via ectophagia, this Enhancement costs no Plasm.&quot;), the answer is most likely yes.<br /> <br /> Can geists regain Essence for being remembered like other ghosts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T14:27:56-07:00","id":1480862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1480848#post1480848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can geists regain Essence for being remembered like other ghosts?</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory, but Iconic and Broken and the nature of how most geists are made make that slim pickings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T13:44:01-07:00","id":1481259,"title":"","content":"Am I mistaken or there are no Night Horrors books for Geist?<br /> I can't remember or find any, neither 1e nor 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T13:49:44-07:00","id":1481260,"title":"","content":"To my knowledge, geist 2e only had Memento mori as a supplement, don't remember any night horror for 1st ed either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T14:51:10-07:00","id":1481264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1481259#post1481259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I mistaken or there are no Night Horrors books for Geist?<br /> I can't remember or find any, neither 1e nor 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geist 1e had one and a half books in total (Book of the Dead was, technically, a bluebook in the same mold as Book of Spirits), not counting the large handful of SAS modules.<br /> <br /> For a good long while, Grim Fears was an outlier in being a non-Big Three Night Horrors book, and for the moment, Geist 2e shares the &quot;no Night Horrors&quot; distinction with Mummy, Hunter, and Deviant; notably, those are the four most recently-published corebooks in the edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T09:21:09-07:00","id":1482377,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone, I'm about to run my first geist game and, against my better judgement, I have allowed one of the players to play a moros mage, what I would like to know is if there is some way to introduce an old law or another narrative expedient so that I can &quot;contain&quot; the mage player and not let him derail the chronicle, kerberoi are rank 6 entities so that is already something I can use but I'm wondering if there are other canon &quot;tools&quot; shall we say (even from 1st ed) that could help keeping things from spiraling off control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T10:02:46-07:00","id":1482380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1482377#post1482377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone, I'm about to run my first geist game and, against my better judgement, I have allowed one of the players to play a moros mage, what I would like to know is if there is some way to introduce an old law or another narrative expedient so that I can &quot;contain&quot; the mage player and not let him derail the chronicle, kerberoi are rank 6 entities so that is already something I can use but I'm wondering if there are other canon &quot;tools&quot; shall we say (even from 1st ed) that could help keeping things from spiraling off control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lines and Veils, albeit for a less intense purpose than that tool is usually thought of as serving.<br /> <br /> Get the group together and set expectations and boundaries re: what the mage's player wants to be able to do and what everyone else doesn't want to deal with versus what they'd be okay with handling (and how often). Why does this player want to play a Moros and what convinced you to let them?<br /> <br /> More mechanically speaking, the fact that mages need to make a breakthrough for every new dot of Gnosis (and Gnosis limits their Arcana) should help to manage the pacing for how much the character can do compared to the rest of the krewe, as may the answer to whether the character belongs to a Sect or is simply a solitary or a member of a Nameless Order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-30-2022, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T10:33:02-07:00","id":1482385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1482380#post1482380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lines and Veils, albeit for a less intense purpose than that tool is usually thought of as serving.<br /> <br /> Get the group together and set expectations and boundaries re: what the mage's player wants to be able to do and what everyone else doesn't want to deal with versus what they'd be okay with handling (and how often). Why does this player want to play a Moros and what convinced you to let them?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, he is an old friend with whom I have been playing for a long time and a mage fan since ascension, it was also his birthday to boot so I just told him yes but he is exactly the kind of mage player that make storytellers ban mages at their tables. The group all played together for quite a while and are all friends so I don't expect problems between the players, what I do expect is him finding a way to royally screw the chronicle with some outlandishly stupid plan like trying to take over a dominion by himself or bring a dominion into the living world in an effort to depower a kerberoi. We already had the talk where I told him that I would be summoning ghostzilla to eat him if he tried anything like this and he said he didn't have a problem with it (most of the mage games I have seen him in ended with his characters dying due to some stupid idea) but I would prefer a more elegant solution that might tap into the lore so that I could use it both as a containment measure and as an hook to expand the story. The geist core book is ambiguos enough about the kerberoi that I could just use them and say that a particular spell they had in mind (like trying to unmake a kerberoi) simply doesn't work but I'm open to anything that I could use that wouldn't come as a blatant attempt to keep him in check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T11:36:34-07:00","id":1482389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1482385#post1482385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, he is an old friend with whom I have been playing for a long time and a mage fan since ascension, it was also his birthday to boot so I just told him yes but he is exactly the kind of mage player that make storytellers ban mages at their tables. The group all played together for quite a while and are all friends so I don't expect problems between the players, what I do expect is him finding a way to royally screw the chronicle with some outlandishly stupid plan like trying to take over a dominion by himself or bring a dominion into the living world in an effort to depower a kerberoi. We already had the talk where I told him that I would be summoning ghostzilla to eat him if he tried anything like this and he said he didn't have a problem with it (most of the mage games I have seen him in ended with his characters dying due to some stupid idea) but I would prefer a more elegant solution that might tap into the lore so that I could use it both as a containment measure and as an hook to expand the story. The geist core book is ambiguos enough about the kerberoi that I could just use them and say that a particular spell they had in mind (like trying to unmake a kerberoi) simply doesn't work but I'm open to anything that I could use that wouldn't come as a blatant attempt to keep him in check.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you're asking for a tool that's based in a kind of adversarial ST/player interaction for a game where the main way of accomplishing Big Things <i>always works</i> as long as the characters do the legwork (and the roll just determines how badly it fucks them up), specifically for dealing with a character from a game where the power systems are designed to give PCs just enough rope to hang themselves with, and the main game specifically has Self Versus Service as a listed theme representing personal goals conflicting with group goals.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if you don't foresee intra-party conflict arising, the most elegant solution is still to make sure everyone's on the same page about what you all want out of this game and are prepared to deal with. Starting everyone from ground-level and making sure the PCs relate to each other well enough to help each other and/or weigh the impact of their actions on their fellow celebrants will go a long way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T11:56:11-07:00","id":1482391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1482389#post1482389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you're asking for a tool that's based in a kind of adversarial ST/player interaction for a game where the main way of accomplishing Big Things <i>always works</i> as long as the characters do the legwork (and the roll just determines how badly it fucks them up), specifically for dealing with a character from a game where the power systems are designed to give PCs just enough rope to hang themselves with, and the main game specifically has Self Versus Service as a listed theme representing personal goals conflicting with group goals.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if you don't foresee intra-party conflict arising, the most elegant solution is still to make sure everyone's on the same page about what you all want out of this game and are prepared to deal with. Starting everyone from ground-level and making sure the PCs relate to each other well enough to help each other and/or weigh the impact of their actions on their fellow celebrants will go a long way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not trying to be adversarial to my player, my problem is that I'm not skilled enough as an ST to be able to run a mage game and any game where there is even a single mage is automatically one, I am very good at improvising but I have played mage games and I quite frankly couldn't think of a possible follow up to say, the mage teleporting into the dominion of the highly hostile kerberoi, snatching the legendary memento right under its nose and then coming back, that triviliaze what would be a 3 or 4 sessions of a normal geist game.<br /> <br /> Anyway that is my burden as an ST I guess, I will think of something and hopefully manage to run a good game for all the players, thanks for the answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T12:25:13-07:00","id":1482393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1482391#post1482391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am very good at improvising but I have played mage games and I quite frankly couldn't think of a possible follow up to say, the mage teleporting into the dominion of the highly hostile kerberoi, snatching the legendary memento right under its nose and then coming back, that triviliaze what would be a 3 or 4 sessions of a normal geist game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowing the limits of Awakened magic goes a long way \u2014 to use your example, sympathetic magic is spell-intensive and requires specific resources, and teleportation is not a simple trick to manage even at the lower level of &quot;these two places are spatially connected,&quot; to say nothing of how most Moros will need to have personal practice with the relevant spells for them to not burn through their Mana in one sitting, and ghosts who stick around in the Underworld can communicate and trade. The Long-Term Nimbus of a Moros attracts the sort of phenomena for which &quot;Reapers attempt to Descend the mage's Sanctum&quot; is not without precedent.<br /> <br /> Having the character start at Gnosis 1 and not benefit from the resources of a Sect will help substantially with limiting the pace at which they gain abilities that can derail the story, although, again, communicating that you would prefer the player not derail the story in particular ways would be more effective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-30-2022, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T12:49:46-07:00","id":1482396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1482393#post1482393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Knowing the limits of Awakened magic goes a long way \u2014 to use your example, sympathetic magic is spell-intensive and requires specific resources, and teleportation is not a simple trick to manage even at the lower level of &quot;these two places are spatially connected,&quot; to say nothing of how most Moros will need to have personal practice with the relevant spells for them to not burn through their Mana in one sitting, and ghosts who stick around in the Underworld can communicate and trade. The Long-Term Nimbus of a Moros attracts the sort of phenomena for which &quot;Reapers attempt to Descend the mage's Sanctum&quot; is not without precedent.<br /> <br /> Having the character start at Gnosis 1 and not benefit from the resources of a Sect will help substantially with limiting the pace at which they gain abilities that can derail the story, although, again, communicating that you would prefer the player not derail the story in particular ways would be more effective.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the answer again, I spoke with my player and he decided to go with an obrimos instead of a moros, he started to make a basic concept for his character who will be a solitary mage with no sect affiliation in search of his dead brother's ghost, he will ask the krewe for their help in the endevour since he will know next to nothing about the underworld, this will help immensely since I will not have to worry about him stealing the spotlight from the other players (he is not the kind of guy to do it voluntarily but let's face it, it would have been inevitable with a moros).<br /> <br /> I will have to brush up on my mage lore but It appears much more feasible now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T10:26:00-07:00","id":1482789,"title":"","content":"The Dumb Supper Ceremony has a listed duration of five days, but the success text states that ghosts who partake of its effects do not need to spend Essence for three days. Should the duration entry be taken as a typo, or is it that the phantasmal feast created by the Ceremony lasts for five days until consumed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T10:47:11-07:00","id":1483231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1482789#post1482789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dumb Supper Ceremony has a listed duration of five days, but the success text states that ghosts who partake of its effects do not need to spend Essence for three days. Should the duration entry be taken as a typo, or is it that the phantasmal feast created by the Ceremony lasts for five days until consumed?</div> </div> </div> </div>To me it seems that all of the 13 or less partecipants must be present while you perform the ceremony, and the feast must be consumed shortly after.<br /> Probably the 5 days duration is a typo, but it s hard to say","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T10:49:52-07:00","id":1483232,"title":"","content":"Do you think that the bottled memories created by The Memoria could be used multiple times (each sip from the bottle gives the condition with the original amount of charges)?<br /> If not, do you think it s possible to use again Recall the memoria after a bottled memory is resolved?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 06-06-2022, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T12:45:09-07:00","id":1484438,"title":"","content":"Can Sin-Eaters turn off their physical medium trait? If they got mobbed by a crowd of ghosts, could they walk through them to get away? If there's a ghost building on an empty lot, could they choose to walk through it or would they have to go around? Assuming they can interact with Castoffs, would flying a Castoff plane or sailing a ghost ship just look like them zooming around unsupported to a regular person?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T14:48:32-07:00","id":1484443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1484438#post1484438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Sin-Eaters turn off their physical medium trait?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;She cannot help but see and hear ghosts, putting her in a liminal state between medium and necromancer.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A Sin-Eater sees the dead constantly.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The geist holds you in place, but it does not hide you from Twilight or Twilight from you.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they got mobbed by a crowd of ghosts, could they walk through them to get away? </div> </div> </div>In the same sense that they could walk through a crowd of people to get away, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If there's a ghost building on an empty lot, could they choose to walk through it or would they have to go around? </div> </div> </div>The latter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Assuming they can interact with Castoffs, would flying a Castoff plane or sailing a ghost ship just look like them zooming around unsupported to a regular person? </div> </div> </div>Yup. Unless it Manifests in a visible fashion, using a Castoff is going to look as weird as walking into a dead end where an Avernian Gate stands opened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T21:58:25-07:00","id":1484475,"title":"","content":"If you dropped a cage of ghostly Essence around a Sin-Eater, they would have to explain, very embarrassed, that they can't go anywhere and need some help, could you get some of the ghost from down the block to help them out.<br /> <br /> Unless they had Caul, but that has to do with Size alteration and not &quot;all that is dead is mine to [touch].&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T01:33:24-07:00","id":1484487,"title":"","content":"The absolute nightmare for a Bound is a city that has been torn down by fire or war, and then rebuilt. The ghost buildings will make navigating some areas impossible as doors and walls won't line up.<br /> <br /> But especially bad are buildings that have been razed just for a street to be laid on that ground. A frontal collision is bad enough when (the front of) the car is between you and the wall to soften the blow. When the car doesn't interact with the wall, you're basically strapped to the tip of a rocket aimed right at that wall.<br /> <br /> The latter example is probably more common, because individual houses are more easily remembered by their previous occupants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T08:59:09-07:00","id":1484779,"title":"","content":"Do you think that a bound Geist has its own set of senses or he perceives the world only with its bound senses?<br /> One of my player wants to use his Geist as a sentinel while he sleeps and i don t know if it is possible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T21:48:11-07:00","id":1485011,"title":"","content":"Thanks folks, it was bothering me that it wasn't spelled out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1484779#post1484779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think that a bound Geist has its own set of senses or he perceives the world only with its bound senses?<br /> One of my player wants to use his Geist as a sentinel while he sleeps and i don t know if it is possible</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't find a reference to ghosts or Geists sleeping, and I remember references to Geists wandering around on their own, from time to time, and at least acting like they have their own senses and perspectives. I don't think there's any problem with using a Geist as a sentinel, assuming it's willing to do that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T06:58:23-07:00","id":1485030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1484779#post1484779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think that a bound Geist has its own set of senses or he perceives the world only with its bound senses?<br /> One of my player wants to use his Geist as a sentinel while he sleeps and i don t know if it is possible</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter. The geist functionally does not exist in the world while it's not Unleashed or powering a Haunt; its ability to project an image doesn't give you the ability to get information you couldn't get or infer yourself (Remembrance Traits notwithstanding).<br /> <br /> You can play a little bit fast and loose with unconscious shared awareness of your surroundings, but if you're dead to the world for the usual eightish hours a night your geist is not going to be able to help you notice threats in any way more concrete than the equivalent of your being a light sleeper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T10:31:43-07:00","id":1487490,"title":"","content":"If I use a Key to unlock an Haunt, I can use the same Key to unlock another Haunt (in another round) or the key are blocked until the end of the Haunt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9092-nesky","name":"Nesky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T13:28:39-07:00","id":1487505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nesky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1487490#post1487490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I use a Key to unlock an Haunt, I can use the same Key to unlock another Haunt (in another round) or the key are blocked until the end of the Haunt?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't use a given Key again until you resolve its associated Doom Condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T23:13:04-07:00","id":1487549,"title":"","content":"Ok, so you confirm me that the Doom Condition is the only situation that interfere to the use of given key?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9092-nesky","name":"Nesky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T23:56:48-07:00","id":1487553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nesky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1487549#post1487549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so you confirm me that the Doom Condition is the only situation that interfere to the use of given key?</div> </div> </div> </div>Outside extraordinary circumstances, yes, that is correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T22:48:58-07:00","id":1487697,"title":"","content":"How do Undertaker krewes handle ghosts in general? From their write up, I get that they want to change the metaphysical makeup of the Underworld through changing humanities perspective in death through mythic storytelling, but I have no idea how they deal with ghosts. The Burden write ups seem to imply they make them go through their anchors and such, but I thought that was a pilgrim thing in terms of focus?<br /> <br /> I really like the archetype conceptually, as them dealing with the living and trying to change their views on death in order to simply stop ghosts from forming is awesome, but I just have so much of a struggle visualizing one for a player campaign. They seem more like an NPC krewe at times","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T00:01:40-07:00","id":1487700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1487697#post1487697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do Undertaker krewes handle ghosts in general? From their write up, I get that they want to change the metaphysical makeup of the Underworld through changing humanities perspective in death through mythic storytelling, but I have no idea how they deal with ghosts. The Burden write ups seem to imply they make them go through their anchors and such, but I thought that was a pilgrim thing in terms of focus?<br /> <br /> I really like the archetype conceptually, as them dealing with the living and trying to change their views on death in order to simply stop ghosts from forming is awesome, but I just have so much of a struggle visualizing one for a player campaign. They seem more like an NPC krewe at times</div> </div> </div> </div>They handle ghosts the way Sin-Eaters handle ghosts. Their social role in emerging Sin-Eater society is the flipside of the Necropolitans \u2014 their big-picture focus includes running damage control on public manifestations of ghostly trouble and the impact the resulting stories might have on the Underworld, which means making sure that ghosts exploding out of the walls of a haunted house is not at the forefront of people's minds re: what comes after death, which in turn means taking steps to ensure ghosts are not likely to do that (most reliably by preventing ghosts from being formed, but finding new ghosts early is the second best thing).<br /> <br /> Furies can handle ghosts that aren't specifically victims of injustice and Mourners can tackle ghosts that don't have secrets and traditions to pass down, and Pilgrims don't have a monopoly on persuading the restless dead to let go. You handle ghosts by handling ghosts, regardless of what your krewe's archetype is. Undertakers are liable to be a little more conscious of how the process will be remembered, but otherwise they have the same tools as everybody else does.<br /> <br /> Undertakers handle ghosts as a group of people whose interactions with the living and the Bound shape the Underworld through the themes reflected by the narrative they tell the world about Death. Look to the material on Uncanny Tableaux on page 208-209 for the sort of things Undertakers might be specifically aiming for when they help a ghost move on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T08:54:35-07:00","id":1487735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1487700#post1487700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They handle ghosts the way Sin-Eaters handle ghosts. Their social role in emerging Sin-Eater society is the flipside of the Necropolitans \u2014 their big-picture focus includes running damage control on public manifestations of ghostly trouble and the impact the resulting stories might have on the Underworld, which means making sure that ghosts exploding out of the walls of a haunted house is not at the forefront of people's minds re: what comes after death, which in turn means taking steps to ensure ghosts are not likely to do that (most reliably by preventing ghosts from being formed, but finding new ghosts early is the second best thing).<br /> <br /> Furies can handle ghosts that aren't specifically victims of injustice and Mourners can tackle ghosts that don't have secrets and traditions to pass down, and Pilgrims don't have a monopoly on persuading the restless dead to let go. You handle ghosts by handling ghosts, regardless of what your krewe's archetype is. Undertakers are liable to be a little more conscious of how the process will be remembered, but otherwise they have the same tools as everybody else does.<br /> <br /> Undertakers handle ghosts as a group of people whose interactions with the living and the Bound shape the Underworld through the themes reflected by the narrative they tell the world about Death. Look to the material on Uncanny Tableaux on page 208-209 for the sort of things Undertakers might be specifically aiming for when they help a ghost move on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do always seem to forget that these kinda things aren't so narrow minded.<br /> <br /> So Undertakers, when dealing with the dead directly instead of indirectly through living, use a method helping ghosts by showing/making a better way for them to interact with the living. That way they can influence not only the passing of that ghost, but also have an effect on the underpinnings of the Underworld, especially through dead dominions and tableauxs? I think I'm understanding it better, and I do mean this in an Archtypal way, I am going to keep in better mind that Archetype does not mean &quot;intensely narrow focus&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T03:48:12-07:00","id":1488001,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I read the beats criteria and in: Chronicle of darkness, Werewolf, Demon, Changeling, Promethean take a beat If your character takes lethal damage in one of her rightmost Health boxes. In Vampire is the same but \u201cdo not gain Beats from bashing damage\u201d. In Geist and Mage no, there\u2019s a reason?</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9092-nesky","name":"Nesky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T04:16:40-07:00","id":1488002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nesky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1488001#post1488001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I read the beats criteria and in: Chronicle of darkness, Werewolf, Demon, Changeling, Promethean take a beat If your character takes lethal damage in one of her rightmost Health boxes. In Vampire is the same but \u201cdo not gain Beats from bashing damage\u201d. In Geist and Mage no, there\u2019s a reason?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Most likely balance, sin eaters and mages have a lot more ways to gain beats compared to the other splats, geists using their keys gain doom conditions that can be resolved and regained multiple times in a session, they also have synergy and krewe beats that help with developing faster, mages can similarly give themself conditions to farm beats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T09:16:35-07:00","id":1488035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nesky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1488001#post1488001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read the beats criteria and in: Chronicle of darkness, Werewolf, Demon, Changeling, Promethean take a beat If your character takes lethal damage in one of her rightmost Health boxes. In Vampire is the same but \u201cdo not gain Beats from bashing damage\u201d. In Geist and Mage no, there\u2019s a reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking damage in one of your rightmost three Health boxes is already a crisis point trigger, which, as long as you don't exceptionally succeed on the intercession roll, gives you or your geist a Condition that can provide you with Synergy Beats. It would be redundant.<br /> <br /> Also, just to correct, it's any damage for changelings or demons (as well as Beasts and hunters), not just lethal. Vampires, werewolves, Prometheans, and mummies all have a template-level relation to damage that makes &quot;take bashing damage to the point a normal person would experience wound penalties&quot; a comparatively trivial non-issue \u2014 vampires, Prometheans, and mummies can't fall unconscious from bashing damage; werewolves and mummies regenerate bashing damage rapidly; Prometheans don't suffer wound penalties; and vampires and mummies only take bashing damage from most sources of lethal damage.<br /> <br /> Deviants similarly don't mention taking severe damage in their core list of Beat criteria, and that splat is 1) highly modular as well as 2) built around having a bunch of powers with drawbacks that give you Beats when they cause complications (including more than one option whose mechanical effects include &quot;wound penalties are more trouble for you&quot;). The option's there if you need it, but it's not necessarily an assumed part of the splat that a dramatic story about transformed people involves their getting beaten or shot half to death.<br /> <br /> On the other end of things, mages don't have taking damage on their list, but instead have an entire secondary experience type that can be spent solely on developing their powers, which themselves can be (and are explicitly suggested to be) used to give themselves Conditions, and the archetype of &quot;wizard&quot; isn't one for which being severely wounded is really encouraged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-26-2022, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T16:24:46-07:00","id":1492462,"title":"","content":"If a man angers acanthus mage, then is struck by a lightning (created by karmic miracle).<br /> The man gets a bargain.<br /> As a sin-eater, is his key a key of chance or key of blood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27564-visitingdm","name":"VisitingDM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T16:59:15-07:00","id":1492466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VisitingDM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1492462#post1492462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a man angers acanthus mage, then is struck by a lightning (created by karmic miracle).<br /> The man gets a bargain.<br /> As a sin-eater, is his key a key of chance or key of blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>Table's discretion as to what makes sense for their individual game. See the &quot;The Door Has Many Keys&quot; sidebar on page 121.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-25T21:11:22-07:00","id":1493703,"title":"","content":"Quick question, haven't found anything in the books, but can the Bound see Anchors for what they are?<br /> <br /> Example: Andrew died in the 1800s, shot by a farmer in a trainstation, after the farmer intercepted a letter asking his daughter to elope. In death Andrew has two Anchors remaining. The letter, which found its way to the Krewe's hands, and the bullets, still lodged on the rotting wooden beams of the train station where he relives his last moments, waiting for his beloved that never came.<br /> <br /> Would the Krewe be able to instantly recognize the letter to be one of Andrew's Anchors when they saw him? Would the lodged bullets immediately jump to sight as an Anchor as well (some kind of deathly aura?), or would the Krewe actively need to search for them?<br /> <br /> The rules for Physical Medium should, in my opinion, mention that, but they don't. There are rules for resolving Rememberances, but shouldn't there be something about Anchors as well?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-25T22:22:10-07:00","id":1493705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HTaiji</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1493703#post1493703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question, haven't found anything in the books, but can the Bound see Anchors for what they are?<br /> <br /> Example: Andrew died in the 1800s, shot by a farmer in a trainstation, after the farmer intercepted a letter asking his daughter to elope. In death Andrew has two Anchors remaining. The letter, which found its way to the Krewe's hands, and the bullets, still lodged on the rotting wooden beams of the train station where he relives his last moments, waiting for his beloved that never came.<br /> <br /> Would the Krewe be able to instantly recognize the letter to be one of Andrew's Anchors when they saw him? Would the lodged bullets immediately jump to sight as an Anchor as well (some kind of deathly aura?), or would the Krewe actively need to search for them?<br /> <br /> The rules for Physical Medium should, in my opinion, mention that, but they don't. There are rules for resolving Rememberances, but shouldn't there be something about Anchors as well?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that The Oracle level 3 power can identify Anchors, but i don t know if they are recognizable on sight","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T05:30:45-07:00","id":1493715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HTaiji</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1493703#post1493703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question, haven't found anything in the books, but can the Bound see Anchors for what they are?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not innately, though the geographic constraints of most ghosts, the rarity of there being more than three to a ghost, and the commonality of the remains or resting place as one of them means you'll seldom need to figure out more than one extra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T15:45:43-07:00","id":1493997,"title":"","content":"Quick question, part 2:<br /> <br /> Sugestions for Merits for the the Furies Archetype mentions Council of Faith, as does the Pilgrims. Was it scrapped? Am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T20:07:13-07:00","id":1494011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HTaiji</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1493997#post1493997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question, part 2:<br /> <br /> Sugestions for Merits for the the Furies Archetype mentions Council of Faith, as does the Pilgrims. Was it scrapped? Am I missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same Merit is named in the suggestions for Pilgrims, so probably an artifact of an earlier draft, yes. I don't recall it being in the KS previews, so it's probably an editing fossil like the Theophany Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T12:55:00-07:00","id":1494748,"title":"","content":"I feel like I've overlooked something obvious, but where does a Geist typically get their name/title from?<br /> Do they pick one for themselves based on what little they remember of their life and death? Does their Sin-Eater try to come up with something appropriate after they've made the Bargain? Does emerging from their transformation into a little god of death just make them so iconic that anyone looking can tell that he's The Play-Pretend Private and she's The Prom-Queen-In-Exile from the vibes alone?<br /> Just trying to figure out how much I should factor in a Bound's personality or naming habits when coming up with their partner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26730-tomdick-harry","user":"TomDick&amp;Harry","date":". 10-10-2022, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26730-tomdick-harry","name":"TomDick&Harry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T14:53:16-07:00","id":1494752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TomDick&amp;amp;Harry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1494748#post1494748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like I've overlooked something obvious, but where does a Geist typically get their name/title from?<br /> Do they pick one for themselves based on what little they remember of their life and death? Does their Sin-Eater try to come up with something appropriate after they've made the Bargain? Does emerging from their transformation into a little god of death just make them so iconic that anyone looking can tell that he's The Play-Pretend Private and she's The Prom-Queen-In-Exile from the vibes alone?<br /> Just trying to figure out how much I should factor in a Bound's personality or naming habits when coming up with their partner.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d say it\u2019s a little bit of all, since Geists and Sin-Eaters are all highly individualistic beings and every pair has a different chemistry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T16:21:00-07:00","id":1494756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TomDick&amp;amp;Harry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1494748#post1494748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like I've overlooked something obvious, but where does a Geist typically get their name/title from?</div> </div> </div> </div>Urban legends about them, descriptive monikers, et cetera. The important thing to remember is that the geist existed in the world before the Bargain and is Iconic and Broken enough to generally get a ghost story going about them. The Absent are normal ghosts and manage to maintain aliases, and a geist is a ghost unfettered by the geographical constraints of Anchors and often incentivized to be near graveyards, where conversational ghosts congregate, at least some of the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-10T11:50:39-08:00","id":1496723,"title":"","content":"Several questions at once:<ul><li>How would Underworld of wild location, without much of human presence, look like?</li> <li>Is Irkalla's Gate the only way to enter a Dead Dominion?</li> <li>Is it possible to trick or threaten Irkalla's Gate Guardian into opening one without paying the cost?</li> <li>Could Persistent Condition or Tilt representing the price be removed, by mundane or supernatural means?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","user":"Dark Archon","date":". 11-10-2022, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-11T10:01:26-08:00","id":1496823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1496723#post1496723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Several questions at once:<ul><li>How would Underworld of wild location, without much of human presence, look like?</li> <li>Is Irkalla's Gate the only way to enter a Dead Dominion?</li> <li>Is it possible to trick or threaten Irkalla's Gate Guardian into opening one without paying the cost?</li> <li>Could Persistent Condition or Tilt representing the price be removed, by mundane or supernatural means?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>1. No clue. In my games, however, such a thing would appear as a jagged wound in the earth, heading <i>down</i>.<br /> 2. Yes.<br /> 3. Yes. If you get caught, though...<br /> 4. No clue. Possibly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-18T19:37:19-08:00","id":1497503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1496723#post1496723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would Underworld of wild location, without much of human presence, look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand the question. It looks like underground caverns or tunnels, which can exist without human presence. There probably won't be much in the way of Castoff architecture, but &quot;First-time travelers [\u2026] wonder if the [Avernian Gate] hasn't just spit them back out somewhere else&quot; is a pretty clear indication that the Underworld close enough to the surface to be described as the Underworld &quot;of&quot; a place is largely indistinguishable from underground parts of the living world it was entered from.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is Irkalla's Gate the only way to enter a Dead Dominion? </div> </div> </div>I should imagine the fact that they're described as rare and that some of them lead nowhere would indicate the answer to this one is &quot;No.&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it possible to trick or threaten Irkalla's Gate Guardian into opening one without paying the cost? </div> </div> </div>They can explicitly be tricked, though as Rank 3+ ghosts, mechanically this will be difficult.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could Persistent Condition or Tilt representing the price be removed, by mundane or supernatural means? </div> </div> </div>It's a Condition or Tilt, so yes. Not necessarily easily, but a Resolution criterion or means of Ending the Tilt must necessarily exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T15:20:36-08:00","id":1499912,"title":"","content":"I was big on Geist back in the day and even kept thinking about a homebrew 2e version back when it was unsure that would happen, but I remember looking through the kickstarter preview and... are Keystones really gone? They were one of my favourite parts of Geist. I loved that there was this physical thing that served as both a way to fight with ghosts and also a manifestation of your connection to your Geist. With the Keystone being so deeply personal and important to characters, it would be hard for me to translate my 1e Sin-eaters to 2e since they no longer have their personal quirky weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T16:10:38-08:00","id":1499914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1499912#post1499912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was big on Geist back in the day and even kept thinking about a homebrew 2e version back when it was unsure that would happen, but I remember looking through the kickstarter preview and... are Keystones really gone? They were one of my favourite parts of Geist. I loved that there was this physical thing that served as both a way to fight with ghosts and also a manifestation of your connection to your Geist. With the Keystone being so deeply personal and important to characters, it would be hard for me to translate my 1e Sin-eaters to 2e since they no longer have their personal quirky weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Keystone Memento is no longer a thing, with some of its functions now served by your Remembrance Traits. Physical Medium and the fact that every Memento has Durability of at least 5 means a Sin-Eater is likely to be pretty well-armed and/or armored even without the Rage or specifically designated weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T16:17:22-08:00","id":1499916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1499912#post1499912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was big on Geist back in the day and even kept thinking about a homebrew 2e version back when it was unsure that would happen, but I remember looking through the kickstarter preview and... are Keystones really gone? They were one of my favourite parts of Geist. I loved that there was this physical thing that served as both a way to fight with ghosts and also a manifestation of your connection to your Geist. With the Keystone being so deeply personal and important to characters, it would be hard for me to translate my 1e Sin-eaters to 2e since they no longer have their personal quirky weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless specifically homebrewing Keystones back in, you could give the characters a weaponizable Memento at character creation, saying that it\u2019s made from the residual energies of the characters\u2019 own deaths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T11:50:18-08:00","id":1501554,"title":"","content":"How do Tyrants and Tyranny work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Proud creator of <b><a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/420206/Curiouser-and-Curiouser-Bargains\" target=\"_blank\">Curiouser and Curiouser Bargains</a></b>, a collection of 30+ Homebrew Contracts and 10+ Entitlements on the STV!<br /> My <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GFE19F9st7dhGh9zv_hEQyOSm80Xp7dQwmvFg2SAXJY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules</a></b> for Changeling!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17SsOsKpfdANVZscFHSO_afTx-gD3h0iX3p5q07V4u50/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Vampire!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kR6ASTLjaEDwl3zgANnkRrbk0-s2bvw40uXwS-q15O0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Geist!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27667-super-vlad","name":"Super Vlad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27667_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T00:45:13-08:00","id":1501591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Super Vlad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1501554#post1501554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do Tyrants and Tyranny work?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the Bound who hit Synergy 3 at some point previously knows their geist's Touchstone, hits Synergy 0, and ritualistically destroys their geist's Touchstone to resolve the Flatlining Condition instead of resolving a Remembrance scene or dying for good. After that, the character has a dot of Tyranny, which is only mechanically different in that they always roll Tyranny + Intimidation to intercede in crisis points.<br /> <br /> Given that becoming Tyrannous makes you a Storyteller character, the implication that the same things that provide Synergy Beats allow these Bound to raise their Tyranny rating is sort of a moot point, but it's interesting to consider how this shift in dynamic reorients the Relationship levels for the purposes of intercession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T02:31:26-08:00","id":1501677,"title":"","content":"In the character creation, it says that each burden has a unique haunt. Is it possible to take that haunt as a non affinity haunt? The book doesn\u2019t say you can\u2019t.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10150-bob275","name":"bob275","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T04:47:27-08:00","id":1501690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bob275</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1501677#post1501677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the character creation, it says that each burden has a unique haunt. Is it possible to take that haunt as a non affinity haunt? The book doesn\u2019t say you can\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that character creation says you must assign at least two of your three starting dots to Haunts your Burden has an affinity for, and the fact that the unique Haunts of each Burden are not mechanically distinguished in how they're learned aside from only being in-affinity for one Burden instead of two, collectively imply that yes, you can spend up to one of your starting Haunt dots on the signature Haunt of a different Burden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-20T12:57:38-07:00","id":1505924,"title":"","content":"I'm working on a Sin Eater to try and learn this system better. I was wondering, if a Geist was a former Wolf Blooded, would that character's pack totem, if deceased, be an acceptable Geist? Assuming, of course, that the pack totem has lost a significant part of itself and only functions according to the Geist rules.<br /> <br /> Looking over the beats part and I'm a little confused. It says all beats go to the common pool (except special beats, but let's ignore those) and when the common pool has 5 beats every play gets an experience. Does that mean if I have 5 players, and each player achieves 2 of their aspirations, they each gain 2 full experience for that? That's a dramatic increase in XP from Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":".  Adding a question 03-20-2023, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-20T18:07:37-07:00","id":1505987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1505924#post1505924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm working on a Sin Eater to try and learn this system better. I was wondering, if a Geist was a former Wolf Blooded, would that character's pack totem, if deceased, be an acceptable Geist? Assuming, of course, that the pack totem has lost a significant part of itself and only functions according to the Geist rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, sure, weird stuff happens, but a geist is a ghost and spirits don't generally leave ghosts on account of how they don't default to dying when killed and don't tend to get enough human recognition to evoke the grieving response that sustains the dead in the land of the living.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Looking over the beats part and I'm a little confused. It says all beats go to the common pool (except special beats, but let's ignore those) and when the common pool has 5 beats every play gets an experience. Does that mean if I have 5 players, and each player achieves 2 of their aspirations, they each gain 2 full experience for that? That's a dramatic increase in XP from Werewolf. </div> </div> </div>The number of Beats in the common pool is five times the number of players, not five. That means once the pool has enough Beats in it that you could divide them up five per player, every player gets the Experience they'd get in a non-Group Beats game for earning five Beats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T05:24:23-07:00","id":1506034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1505924#post1505924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm working on a Sin Eater to try and learn this system better. I was wondering, if a Geist was a former Wolf Blooded, would that character's pack totem, if deceased, be an acceptable Geist? Assuming, of course, that the pack totem has lost a significant part of itself and only functions according to the Geist rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most things that can function as pack totems won't leave ghosts when they die, and even if they did, they'd still have to become a Geist. On top of that, part of the game focuses on solving the mystery of the Geist's identity and having a Geist you used to know could seriously change that aspect of the game. It could still be plenty enjoyable, though.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the totem could already be a Geist. That way, you'd know (part of) their history as a Geist but not necessarily anything about who they were before, and they'd already have gone through the process of dying and then becoming a Geist.<br /> The only thing you'd need to explain is why the Geist stopped being a pack totem. Perhaps the entire pack got wiped out in a catastrophic event, and the Geist decided to save at least one of their pack mates the only way it knew how?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T10:13:13-07:00","id":1506048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1506034#post1506034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the entire pack got wiped out in a catastrophic event, and the Geist decided to save at least one of their pack mates the only way it knew how?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was going to be the back story, only with the totem dying to become a geist instead of being a geist to begin with. Your idea works better though, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T22:06:22-07:00","id":1506120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1506034#post1506034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing you'd need to explain is why the Geist stopped being a pack totem. Perhaps the entire pack got wiped out in a catastrophic event, and the Geist decided to save at least one of their pack mates the only way it knew how?</div> </div> </div> </div>This does sound pretty awesome, but it would be pretty funny if the pack is still around and the player has to deal with a bunch of wolf-men trying to get their totem back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T10:34:09-07:00","id":1506153,"title":"","content":"I figured I'd add a question just to keep things going.<br /> <br /> Suppose you use the Caul to substitute your Geist's Resistance for your Composure right before you use the Stillness key (with the Unlock Attribute of Composure) to unlock the Boneyard. Then you roll Synergy + Boneyard + Composure to mess with things within the Boneyard. By default, this uses your Sin-Eater's and not your Geist's Composure, but you can spend a charge from Caul to use your Geist's Composure, right?<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T09:08:03-07:00","id":1506488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jsnider3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1506153#post1506153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figured I'd add a question just to keep things going.<br /> <br /> Suppose you use the Caul to substitute your Geist's Resistance for your Composure right before you use the Stillness key (with the Unlock Attribute of Composure) to unlock the Boneyard. Then you roll Synergy + Boneyard + Composure to mess with things within the Boneyard. By default, this uses your Sin-Eater's and not your Geist's Composure, but you can spend a charge from Caul to use your Geist's Composure, right?<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading seems to say that would be technically correct by the wording; you would be substituting an attribute for one action. My assumption is, however, that this isn't an intended function of the Caul. It also begs the question of whether you get the other benefits (e.g. the bonus plasm) or just the dice bonus, but that would be something to ask your ST.<br /> <br /> If you are the ST, then I suggest telling your players either 1) no i won't allow that (can be a bit of a &quot;feels bad&quot; for any player without the Caul to miss out on that ability) or 2) yes, but only the dice-pool will change (and, in the case of things like the Marionette where you roll the Haunt pool again to do other things, it goes back to your regular Synergy + Haunt + appropriate Attribute unless you spend another Caul charge, given it is a per-action effect)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T17:13:24-07:00","id":1506549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lorekeeper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1506488#post1506488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My reading seems to say that would be technically correct by the wording; you would be substituting an attribute for one action. My assumption is, however, that this isn't an intended function of the Caul. It also begs the question of whether you get the other benefits (e.g. the bonus plasm) or just the dice bonus, but that would be something to ask your ST.<br /> <br /> If you are the ST, then I suggest telling your players either 1) no i won't allow that (can be a bit of a &quot;feels bad&quot; for any player without the Caul to miss out on that ability) or 2) yes, but only the dice-pool will change (and, in the case of things like the Marionette where you roll the Haunt pool again to do other things, it goes back to your regular Synergy + Haunt + appropriate Attribute unless you spend another Caul charge, given it is a per-action effect)</div> </div> </div> </div>This was just idle speculation on the rules, not part of a game I'm currently in. If I was STing this, I would either say that you can't use the Caul to use your Geist's attributes to unlock a key or I'd say that you get the full benefits (including plasm) of your Geist's attributes if you do. I'm not so sure that second option would be all that unbalanced, since extruding the Caul 1) takes a turn, 2) blatantly reveals the user as a supernatural creature, and 3) either costs them plasm or risks giving them a Doom. In exchange, they get four or so extra plasm and dice. Plasm isn't exactly limitless, but neither are time and subtlety. Plus, the idea of turning into a monster in order to be slightly better at spellcasting sounds cool and cool things should be encouraged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T20:43:43-07:00","id":1506600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jsnider3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1506549#post1506549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was just idle speculation on the rules, not part of a game I'm currently in. If I was STing this, I would either say that you can't use the Caul to use your Geist's attributes to unlock a key or I'd say that you get the full benefits (including plasm) of your Geist's attributes if you do. I'm not so sure that second option would be all that unbalanced, since extruding the Caul 1) takes a turn, 2) blatantly reveals the user as a supernatural creature, and 3) either costs them plasm or risks giving them a Doom. In exchange, they get four or so extra plasm and dice. Plasm isn't exactly limitless, but neither are time and subtlety. Plus, the idea of turning into a monster in order to be slightly better at spellcasting sounds cool and cool things should be encouraged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counterpoints:<br /> <br /> 1. Haunts are not spells and the Caul is not you turning into a monster in any way that would meaningfully change things about that.<br /> 2. Your geist does not have extra facility with the Haunts shared between the two of you in a way that corresponds to Unlock Attributes \u2014 it has a set dicepool that doesn't correspond to the Attribute it would use for more than half the Keys in the book.<br /> 3. The Caul is one of three Haunts that merges you with the geist in some way, and it does that through bodily plasticity and shared knowledge/sensation, not by giving you ghostly qualities like the Shroud or the violent middle road of the Rage.<br /> 4. This feels like the sort of you'd-be-stupid-not-to-take-it combo shenanigan that 1e's &quot;you can add your Boneyard activation successes to the activation roll for any Manifestation you activate with the same Key in addition to targeting them against anyone within range of the Boneyard&quot; allowed, and I note that the way Keys and the Boneyard work in 2e means that one's off the table.<br /> 5. Unlike the aforementioned Boneyard synergy, this effect works with any Key from any Caul (even an unKeyed one), which doesn't feel terribly strongly thematic regardless of how spooky it is for someone to unleash potent supernatural powers after displaying visible monstrosity.<br /> 6. Using Keys is already a power-up for unlocking Haunts and adding even more dice risks diluting the thematic purpose of using them with Attributes you're strong in and/or in resonant situations, because your geist's stats have no guaranteed overlap with your own and your geist's facility with its Key(s) is represented by it having them as powerful Influences.<br /> <br /> Cool things should be encouraged, but this is a game about being a weird type of ghost, and, just like <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-1-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf doesn't do Facets that are basically magic spells to throw at a target</a>, Geist should not proceed along the logical disjunction from &quot;ghosts look like people when they're not being viewed through the lens of trauma&quot; to &quot;the powers of a pseudo-living ghost bonded with a traumatically-empowered super-ghost become more powerful when merged with that super-ghost in a specific way, despite that way not being the one of three different ways of merging with that super-ghost that gives them the qualities of a ghost.&quot; Something being cool doesn't make it appropriate in every context or mechanical representation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T16:55:19-07:00","id":1507795,"title":"","content":"What does the merit that makes your Geist rank 4 actually do? Does it increase the Geist's stats? Stat maximums? Influences?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T17:34:58-07:00","id":1507803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1507795#post1507795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does the merit that makes your Geist rank 4 actually do? Does it increase the Geist's stats? Stat maximums? Influences?</div> </div> </div> </div>It increases their Rank for the purposes of Bound mechanics that reference the Geist's Rank, i.e. calculating honorary Rank between it and Synergy, limiting dots gained in Remembrance Traits, and being used in the geist's dicepools for Haunts and for determining Influence dots in innate Keys while Unleashed.<br /> <br /> It doesn't give them extra Attribute dots or change their ban or bane (the Geist Creation rules set those totals at 12 dots and appropriate to a Rank 3 entity, respectively), but anything that directly calls the geist's numerical Rank as a variable quality uses 4 instead of 3 for those calculations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T21:48:34-07:00","id":1509555,"title":"","content":"Could a Kindly Bound come back for a reason that legitimately wasn't their fault? For example, could a doctor become a Kindly Bound if they saved someone who later on went on to commit a horrible crime? Another example would be a Kindly who is a martial arts master who believes that it is their fault that a one of their students used their skills to bully people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T00:59:15-07:00","id":1509564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1509555#post1509555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a Kindly Bound come back for a reason that legitimately wasn't their fault? For example, could a doctor become a Kindly Bound if they saved someone who later on went on to commit a horrible crime? Another example would be a Kindly who is a martial arts master who believes that it is their fault that a one of their students used their skills to bully people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, ghosts aren't rational creatures and can get hung up on all sorts of shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T22:29:36-07:00","id":1513913,"title":"","content":"Okay, odd question.<br /> <br /> Are there any rules for the kind of situation that can create a ghost? I'm looking things that aren't ST fiat. <br /> Stuff like &quot;the higher the Integrity of a person, the less likely they are to leave a ghost&quot;. <br /> I have no idea if this stuff even exists...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T23:09:02-07:00","id":1513915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1513913#post1513913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, odd question.<br /> <br /> Are there any rules for the kind of situation that can create a ghost? I'm looking things that aren't ST fiat.<br /> Stuff like &quot;the higher the Integrity of a person, the less likely they are to leave a ghost&quot;.<br /> I have no idea if this stuff even exists...</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the very first page of the section on ghosts on page 185, anything destroyed leaves <i>a</i> ghost (Dave Brookshaw's <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1511880-tome-of-the-pentacle-on-dtrpg?p=1513362#post1513362\">recent post</a> about what the Psychopomp's Crown Attainment was slated to be suggests Integrity 10 humans are a hard exception, as inferred by the Starting Rank bit on page 188 only mentioning Integrity up to 9), though the vast majority of these ghosts are swept into the Underworld in short order without sustained feelings of loss from the living to shore up their forms.<br /> <br /> For sapient ghosts it's down to death and life-changing trauma, as described in the same section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T23:13:17-07:00","id":1513916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1513915#post1513915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per the very first page of the section on ghosts on page 185, anything destroyed leaves <i>a</i> ghost (Dave Brookshaw's <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1511880-tome-of-the-pentacle-on-dtrpg?p=1513362#post1513362\">recent post</a> about what the Psychopomp's Crown Attainment was slated to be suggests Integrity 10 humans are a hard exception, as inferred by the Starting Rank bit on page 188 only mentioning Integrity up to 9), though the vast majority of these ghosts are swept into the Underworld in short order without sustained feelings of loss from the living to shore up their forms.<br /> <br /> For sapient ghosts it's down to death and life-changing trauma, as described in the same section.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! That post by Dave is what prompted me wanting to check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T12:33:16-07:00","id":1515468,"title":"","content":"As I recall, being remembered by the living gives a Ghost essence. Doppelgangers are the Ghosts of the still living. How do those concepts interact?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T14:15:05-07:00","id":1515477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1515468#post1515468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I recall, being remembered by the living gives a Ghost essence. Doppelgangers are the Ghosts of the still living. How do those concepts interact?</div> </div> </div> </div>The criterion is &quot;be remembered as the living person you once were, by a living person.&quot; Doppelgangers are ghosts of people who are still alive, formed through life-altering trauma. Logically, then, Doppelgangers regain Essence from the living remembering how the living person whose trauma created them once was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T14:34:16-07:00","id":1515479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1515477#post1515477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The criterion is &quot;be remembered as the living person you once were, by a living person.&quot; Doppelgangers are ghosts of people who are still alive, formed through life-altering trauma. Logically, then, Doppelgangers regain Essence from the living remembering how the living person whose trauma created them once was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would that not imply, since said person is still alive and presumably doing thing that make people remember them, that the typical Doppelganger is probably quite abundant with essence then? At least until said person dies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T14:40:02-07:00","id":1515480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1515479#post1515479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would that not imply, since said person is still alive and presumably doing thing that make people remember them, that the typical Doppelganger is probably quite abundant with essence then? At least until said person dies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Typically, since Chronicles' universe functions on rules of narrative, events that're traumatic enough to cause the creation of doppelgangers tend to also cause the living survivor to somehow change from that experience - which, in turn, creates a conflict where a survivor of a near-death experience (whether due to the experience itself <i>or</i> by natural consequence on a long-term period of time) gradually changes enough from their past self that it results in a significant enough divergence. Mage's temporal sympathy with past selves plays into this idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T15:24:02-07:00","id":1515486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1515479#post1515479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would that not imply, since said person is still alive and presumably doing thing that make people remember them, that the typical Doppelganger is probably quite abundant with essence then? At least until said person dies?</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as people remember the person who almost died as they were during their near-death event. As that person changes and peoples' perceptions of that person changes, less and less Essence would be provided.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T15:30:23-07:00","id":1515487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1515479#post1515479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would that not imply, since said person is still alive and presumably doing thing that make people remember them, that the typical Doppelganger is probably quite abundant with essence then? At least until said person dies?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Once was.&quot; As in the person they are now is a different person than they once were, whether from a near-death experience or losing a limb or being confronted with the reality of having lived for a year under the control of a vampire.<br /> <br /> As a lovely little comic by the name of <i>Home Sick Pilots</i> succinctly put it, ghosts <i>are</i> trauma. In Geist they are fed by people expecting something to be there but knowing it won't be, and moving on requires that manifestation of trauma to be willing to let go of the things keeping it stuck in the world, ideally before the rest of the world has moved on enough to stop needing reminders of what used to be. For ghosts formed by traumas other than their living basis's own physical death, that means making peace with the fact that the living person they once were (who they no longer reflect as an actor in the present) is gone.<br /> <br /> People with Doppelganger phantom limbs don't need to worry about feeding their ghost eyes Essence because the sensation of having a sensory organ that isn't there is generally a solid reminder of the loss, but the ghost of who you were before you almost drowned at the beach will generally be taking pains to remind you that you used to be more outgoing if the friends and family who see how the accident changed you don't sustain it above the drip-feed of Essence it gets from being Anchored to you; if you and they stop thinking about how you used to be different, it loses its safety buffer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T23:17:02-07:00","id":1517685,"title":"","content":"How long does the Echoes Condition last? It doesn't seem like it should be around forever (what, would it stack every scene you use it?)<br /> <br /> And what counts as an action using the Trait? I've got a Geist that gives Taste of Fear [a ghoul merit] as a Remembrance Trait. Is Intimidation in general penalized, or only when using the power? What about things that don't have actions? Sticking with Ghoul merits, Taste of Gold just gives a Vice. The write up implies Resources as a Remembrance Trait. Fixer simply decreases Availability. I have one Geist that grants Safe Place (it's a house). <br /> <br /> How do I handle all this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T23:53:33-07:00","id":1517686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1517685#post1517685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long does the Echoes Condition last? It doesn't seem like it should be around forever (what, would it stack every scene you use it?)<br /> <br /> And what counts as an action using the Trait? I've got a Geist that gives Taste of Fear [a ghoul merit] as a Remembrance Trait. Is Intimidation in general penalized, or only when using the power? What about things that don't have actions? Sticking with Ghoul merits, Taste of Gold just gives a Vice. The write up implies Resources as a Remembrance Trait. Fixer simply decreases Availability. I have one Geist that grants Safe Place (it's a house).<br /> <br /> How do I handle all this?</div> </div> </div> </div>What you're asking about seems niche enough that it requires some hand-waving and house-ruling.<br /> <br /> Mine would be:<br /> <br /> Echoes: I believe there's an unspoken assumption that STs and players should just waive away the Condition if it ceases to be meaningful/dramatic.<br /> <br /> Taste of Fear: Only when using the Merit itself.<br /> <br /> Taste of Gold: The Echoes kick in when the Bound gets her Willpower fill once, and imposes its -1 on any roll trying to beat someone in a competition.<br /> <br /> Fixer: The Echoes kick in when the Bound benefits from the Availability discount once, and imposes its -1 on any roll trying to hire someone's service.<br /> <br /> Safe Place: The Echoes kick in when the Bound benefits from the Initiative bonus once, and imposes its -1 on any roll trying to maneuver around or defend yourself within the safe house.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T03:45:39-07:00","id":1519329,"title":"","content":"Ok, i haven't finished reading this thread or the 2e book, but I have it in my head that a Geist and a rank 3 ghost are different things.<br /> <br /> A Geist was a ghost who drinks from one of the rivers of the Underworld and becomes more Death-like, infused with some of the power of the Underworld (and if killed that power remains in their deathmask which is what empowers Reapers, and also makes them more Death-aligned).<br /> <br /> A ghost who absorbs a doppleganger of themselves to reach rank 3 is absorbing power of themself, not the Underworld, so presumably doesn't lose their sense of self, infact a doppleganger going from rank 1 to 2 in this way gains a sense of self.<br /> <br /> Is this correct? Are there other rules (like a more powerful Geist 'coming back from the Underworld' getsmore generic anchors) which you would use to differentiate between the more person-like ghosts vs the more Underworld/death-like geists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T04:27:07-07:00","id":1519331,"title":"","content":"There doesn't really need to be anything to differentiate them, they do the same thing it's just different ways of getting there. <br /> <br /> And you're partially right about Geists, Geists are (at least) rank 3 ghosts but not all rank 3 ghosts are Geists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T05:27:25-07:00","id":1519334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1519329#post1519329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, i haven't finished reading this thread or the 2e book, but I have it in my head that a Geist and a rank 3 ghost are different things.<br /> <br /> A Geist was a ghost who drinks from one of the rivers of the Underworld and becomes more Death-like, infused with some of the power of the Underworld (and if killed that power remains in their deathmask which is what empowers Reapers, and also makes them more Death-aligned).<br /> <br /> A ghost who absorbs a doppleganger of themselves to reach rank 3 is absorbing power of themself, not the Underworld, so presumably doesn't lose their sense of self, infact a doppleganger going from rank 1 to 2 in this way gains a sense of self.<br /> <br /> Is this correct? Are there other rules (like a more powerful Geist 'coming back from the Underworld' getsmore generic anchors) which you would use to differentiate between the more person-like ghosts vs the more Underworld/death-like geists?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, a ghost can be Rank 3+ without being a geist, which is differentiated by not using the geist (or Reaper) additional mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T06:24:57-07:00","id":1519339,"title":"","content":"Has that changed somewhere down the line? 'Cause the Geist 2e core book is quite explicit that Rank 3-5 ghosts are always Geister. Something which I always disliked since there's several ways of increasing Rank outside the Underworld, and increasing from Rank 1 to 2 wouldn't make you a Geist even if you're doing it the &quot;proper&quot; way of drinking from a River.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T08:38:00-07:00","id":1519345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1519339#post1519339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has that changed somewhere down the line? 'Cause the Geist 2e core book is quite explicit that Rank 3-5 ghosts are always Geister. Something which I always disliked since there's several ways of increasing Rank outside the Underworld, and increasing from Rank 1 to 2 wouldn't make you a Geist even if you're doing it the &quot;proper&quot; way of drinking from a River.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know the answer to your question, but i would be fine with a rank 2 Geist who was trapped in the Underworld until they reached rank 3 by drinking... But it seems unlikely that a rank 0-1 ghost/castoff/barghest can drink from one of the river of their own volition...<br /> <br /> That said, i only know of two other ways for ghosts to gain rank (excluding the drinking). A Mage spell and the two ghosts from the same source (dopplegangers, or a doppleganger and the actual ghost of the person the doppleganger copied...). What other ways are there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T10:02:38-07:00","id":1519348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1519339#post1519339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has that changed somewhere down the line? 'Cause the Geist 2e core book is quite explicit that Rank 3-5 ghosts are always Geister.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not recall the core rulebook being explicit about that, at all. It's explicit the other direction, all Geists are at least rank 3 ghosts, but never says all rank 3 ghosts are Geists. Do you have a citation?<br /> <br /> ETA: Kerberoi have among their number rank 5 ghosts and they are specifically not Geists. Pg. 197<br /> <br /> ETA 2: Also, isn't the first person to be buried in any graveyard automatically a rank 3 ghost bound to the graveyard as the protector of that gate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":". 08-01-2023, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T15:00:28-07:00","id":1519368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1519348#post1519348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ETA 2: Also, isn't the first person to be buried in any graveyard automatically a rank 3 ghost bound to the graveyard as the protector of that gate?</div> </div> </div> </div>The core talks about it at pag 200, and states that those rank 3 ghosts are Geists (aka Guardian Geists)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T15:53:27-07:00","id":1519375,"title":"","content":"I think what\u2019s happening here is that there are so few Rank 3-4 ghosts that aren\u2019t Geists, to the point that, <i>in-universe, </i>most people just shrug and say that Rank 3-4 and Geist-hood might as well be the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T18:23:10-07:00","id":1519389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1519348#post1519348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not recall the core rulebook being explicit about that, at all. It's explicit the other direction, all Geists are at least rank 3 ghosts, but never says all rank 3 ghosts are Geists. Do you have a citation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tessie has historically overread the fact that the breakdown of ghostly Ranks on page 187 says that the Bound call Rank 3-5 ghosts geists to mean that any Rank 3-5 ghost is necessarily a geist. The matter of doppelgangers consuming their duplicate selves to potentially reach Rank 3 has been a recurring topic in this vein.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T19:19:57-07:00","id":1519391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1519339#post1519339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has that changed somewhere down the line? 'Cause the Geist 2e core book is quite explicit that Rank 3-5 ghosts are always Geister. Something which I always disliked since there's several ways of increasing Rank outside the Underworld, and increasing from Rank 1 to 2 wouldn't make you a Geist even if you're doing it the &quot;proper&quot; way of drinking from a River.</div> </div> </div> </div>All geists are rank 3 or higher, not all rank 3 or higher ghosts* are geists. This has been explained to you several times.<br /> <br /> *or other underworld entities<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T09:16:54-07:00","id":1519444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1519391#post1519391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All geists are rank 3 or higher, not all rank 3 or higher ghosts* are geists. This has been explained to you several times.<br /> <br /> *or other underworld entities</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, cool, the fits well with my understanding of the metaphysics.<br /> <br /> But for rules purposes, what I am asking is<br /> <br /> A rank 3 Geist gets<ul><li>does not have anchors, does not suffer essence bleed, and is not dragged into the Underworld for having no Anchor</li> <li>Replaced their influences with a their inate key</li> <li>Barely recognisable as the person they were</li> <li>Their humanity is buried beneath the corrupting influence of the Underworld</li> <li>And they get a remembrance.</li> </ul>My assumption is that a rank 3 ghost has anchors\u2020, keeps their influences, appears more like the person they were/better memories (though absorbing a doppleganger might reinforce memories before the ghost was created, and if using the rules for the Absent then Memory becomes a seperate thing).<br /> <br /> Their humanity is not buried as they haven't drunk from an Underworld river.<br /> <br /> And no remembrance.<br /> <br /> PS: there is the Empower Ghost Numen. Which i will be assuming doesn't stack with the Quicken ghost spell from Mage as bothonly allow one rank to be gained and neither are lasting.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2020unless the resolve all their anchors and no longer suffers essence bleed either.<br /> <br /> <br /> PPS: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ghosts created at Rank 3-5 are the result of mystical convergences, occult rituals, and similar effects. </div> </div> </div>So the above would apply to a ghost which was created this way too. But for such a rare creation it would be down to ST Fiat, which for me still requires getting my metaphysics clear.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T11:00:45-07:00","id":1519477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1519444#post1519444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, cool, the fits well with my understanding of the metaphysics.<br /> <br /> But for rules purposes, what I am asking is<br /> <br /> A rank 3 Geist gets<ul><li>does not have anchors, does not suffer essence bleed, and is not dragged into the Underworld for having no Anchor</li> <li>Replaced their influences with a their inate key</li> <li>Barely recognisable as the person they were</li> <li>Their humanity is buried beneath the corrupting influence of the Underworld</li> <li>And they get a remembrance.</li> </ul>My assumption is that a rank 3 ghost has anchors\u2020, keeps their influences, appears more like the person they were/better memories (though absorbing a doppleganger might reinforce memories before the ghost was created, and if using the rules for the Absent then Memory becomes a seperate thing).<br /> <br /> Their humanity is not buried as they haven't drunk from an Underworld river.<br /> <br /> And no remembrance.<br /> <br /> PS: there is the Empower Ghost Numen. Which i will be assuming doesn't stack with the Quicken ghost spell from Mage as bothonly allow one rank to be gained and neither are lasting.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2020unless the resolve all their anchors and no longer suffers essence bleed either.<br /> <br /> <br /> PPS:<br /> <br /> So the above would apply to a ghost which was created this way too. But for such a rare creation it would be down to ST Fiat, which for me still requires getting my metaphysics clear.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Second Edition Corebook gets contradictory about Geists having no anchors or not, with one section noting they don't, because having no anchors is a pretty big indicator of why you are in the Underworld which is why the geistification is tempting, and another section stating that they have anchors with anything loosely resonant with their death/Starting Key, and a Rank 3 Ghost can still lose their Anchors without closure and be sucked into the Underworld*, but otherwise, yeah.<br /> <br /> Rank 3 and higher ghosts who are just <i>ghosts</i> are the result of aberrant conditions, like the Doppelganger of a exceptionally unlucky person or the result of Awakened/Arisen/Unchained tampering, but as a result of that, there's no application of the Geist or Reaper sub-type applied to them or anything of the like. They operate like unusually powerful but otherwise normal ghosts.<br /> <br /> THis is something of a weird place to be in, going into the social consequences of such aberrations. On the one hand, they're more powerful entities in the world of death, and the relative normalcy they have in contrast to Geists and Reapers as the nearest adjacent human-esque actors in the world of death makes them desireable within the communities of the dead as leaders, guardians, and otherwise people who can put in more work to make things happen, which can both be either socially empowering or disabling (depending on the disposition of the ghost), and if they actually do it, makes the Essence economy that much more dire. If a Rank 3+ ghost can manage some alone time, they might do pretty all right for themselves, getting an appreciable buffer between them and the void and an increased ability to interact with the living within their means.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Geists and Reapers natural role as psychopomp by virtue of metaphysical mobility is their main virtue (well, that and their Essence security doing a lot to take them out of the Essence economy to a more substantial degree), and the fact that a powerful ghost is still effectively landlocked to their part in life. THe fact they are, in some ways, more likely to survive** drinking a River, just means that any high ranking ghost who lands in the Underworld is probably going to have more pressure, from their own expectations or others, to give being a Geist a try. Demands for psychopompery in the ghostly Twilight will depend on how comfortably a high rank ghost gets Essence, but there can be an expectation for them to try and fill in the same roles, and while they might fair better, they're not equipped for it-a problem that can emerge when that power gets mistaken for similiarity.<br /> <br /> But otherwise, yeah-a Ghost who is Rank 3 by virtue unrelated to drinking from a river or by claiming a Deathmask is not a geist or a Reaper. THe Rank statement in the corebook that trips people up comes from the fact that a Rank 3+ ghost is usually an aberration to the usual operations of the world of the dead that relies on actors outside of the ecosystem.<br /> <br /> *We should mention your example is usually resolved with &quot;and they get to pass on,&quot; so there's that.<br /> **I suppose I should say are more apparently likely, since nothing about the increase of Rank does nothing for the actual drinking of the rivers, but you try telling your River City that-hell, you try telling ghosts who don't have the corebook that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T14:08:47-07:00","id":1519511,"title":"","content":"Thanks for that, i think I get most of that entirely. So I will only reply to the bit that I want to comment on, take this as my nodding in agreement with anything i have snippets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1519477#post1519477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*We should mention your example is usually resolved with &quot;and they get to pass on,&quot; so there's that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and they get to pass on. That is entirely understood. And it is likely that if they had anything which they really wanted to hang around for, maybe it could be argued that that should be an anchor.<br /> <br /> But (ignoring the need for a passing on ceremony) i would argue that a Rank 3+ ghost has more of a reason to hope for being able to do thing in this (twilight) world. Or is more likely to choose to delay passing on. Maybe their last anchor was a blood relative who died peacefully and they let them go. But they still have grandchildren who they aren't anchored to.<br /> <br /> Maybe they have a community of lower ranked ghosts to take care of or a Krewe of Sin-eaters, and are overflowing with essence (because of being the lead of a religious community who remembers them).<br /> <br /> Thinking of ancestor spirit stuff here. Could be an interesting PC/NPC. Maybe this is not likely, or maybe they could develop numina which would allow them travel to the Astral Realm of Death (their afterlife). And possibly even increase their rank further by some even stranger means.<br /> <br /> Lots of potential for a guardian ghost who would really struggle against the reapers and potentially geists. Or far beyond that for a PC to evolve in their own direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Second Edition Corebook gets contradictory about Geists having no anchors or not, with one section noting they don't, &lt;snip&gt; and another section stating that they have anchors with anything loosely resonant with their death/Starting Key </div> </div> </div> This seems easily resolved by saying that Geists have no anchors but can treat anything loosely resonant like it has the open/anchor condition. Which is a sligthly different statement.<br /> <br /> But i don't know if that means they can influence it only, or if they also regain essence being around it (would that be the norm with spirit in an open condition?).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and a Rank 3 Ghost can still lose their Anchors without closure and be sucked into the Underworld*, but otherwise, yeah. </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> THis is something of a weird place to be in, going into the social consequences of such aberrations. On the one hand, they're more powerful entities in the world of death, and the relative normalcy they have in contrast to Geists and Reapers as the nearest adjacent human-esque actors in the world of death makes them desireable within the communities of the dead as leaders, guardians, and otherwise people who can put in more work to make things happen, which can both be either socially empowering or disabling (depending on the disposition of the ghost), and if they actually do it, makes the Essence economy that much more dire. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that is exactly where I think there could be interesting story telling.<br /> <br /> Not sure how the essence economy works on that. Do they soak up all the essence that other ghosts need, or could they be a fount of essence because of their greater inherent powers? Possibly leading ceremonies to feed lower ranked ghosts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> THe fact they are, in some ways, more likely to survive** drinking a River, just means that any high ranking ghost who lands in the Underworld is probably going to have more pressure, from their own expectations or others, to give being a Geist a try. </div> </div> </div>I suspect that is correct, but depending on their attitude (i am assuming they would have accumulated more power, memories, and greater influence - leading to more essence from using that influence on living mortals) they might also dislike geists and try to grow their power despite being in the Underworld surrounded by other higher rank entities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> **I suppose I should say are more apparently likely, since nothing about the increase of Rank does nothing for the actual drinking of the rivers, but you try telling your River City that-hell, you try telling ghosts who don't have the corebook that. </div> </div> </div>Are they not sitting at a higher resistance trait (Min) and possible have far more health levels to survive?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 08-02-2023, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T19:00:39-07:00","id":1519542,"title":"","content":"Can Sin Eaters only be human or could something else made of flesh become a Sin Eater if it had the intelligence to make a pact and had a willing Geist? (Not talking about template stacking, thinking more like a genetically modified animal.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T19:08:51-07:00","id":1519545,"title":"","content":"Sounds more like a Deviant.<br /> <br /> In practical terms, CofD is very human-centric. As such, I'd not allow it by default, but if it would make for an interesting story I don't see a reason to deny it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T19:18:12-07:00","id":1519549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1519542#post1519542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Sin Eaters only be human or could something else made of flesh become a Sin Eater if it had the intelligence to make a pact and had a willing Geist? (Not talking about template stacking, thinking more like a genetically modified animal.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bargain is a Manifestation used by a geist, and the geist uses it by touching a dying mortal and the dying mortal accepting the offer. &quot;Mortal&quot; as a noun is pretty consistently used to refer to humans, and the Bargain replaces the new Bound's soul, which things that aren't humans don't usually have in the way the franchise typically means when it uses the word &quot;soul.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T19:27:26-07:00","id":1519551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1519542#post1519542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Sin Eaters only be human or could something else made of flesh become a Sin Eater if it had the intelligence to make a pact and had a willing Geist? (Not talking about template stacking, thinking more like a genetically modified animal.)</div> </div> </div> </div>For the most part, the game has never once approached the idea that Bargains are made with anything other than humans, largely because most non-human things don't interact with the deathly metaphysics, and the few exceptions you might hope to find in that neck of the woods are exceptions on top of exceptions-the purview of story seeds and not the setting as needs to be established.<br /> <br /> Like, it's possible for a human-level intellect dog to die and then enter into a Bargain, but Geist has bigger things to answer before it even gets to answering this.<br /> <br /> As a one-time writer opinion though, I wouldn't say no to it, but you'd have to persuade me to take it seriously if you wanted to start building a whole branching set of questions and worldbuilding off of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T07:43:43-07:00","id":1519630,"title":"","content":"I know surviving in the underworld isn't always easy but do we have any examples of Geists that are very old, like several hundred or even thousands of years old, before they create a Sin Eater?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T19:52:11-07:00","id":1519702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1519630#post1519630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know surviving in the underworld isn't always easy but do we have any examples of Geists that are very old, like several hundred or even thousands of years old, before they create a Sin Eater?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's theoretically possible, but generally speaking geists don't really have much of a way out of the Bargain that doesn't end their existence short of extreme breach of contract, and if they were inclined to make the offer it would probably happen sooner rather than later, especially with 2e's Underworld having undergone notable changes over time.<br /> <br /> There's nothing on the books in 2e yet on account of how the normal books in that category are the core and Memento Mori, but this is an edition of the game that came out while Dark Eras was being released, with sample settings to match. It's not hard to take any geist character from a historical context and transplant them to modern day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T05:23:41-07:00","id":1519850,"title":"","content":"I was reading up on the differences between Wraith and Geist yesterday, and what kept coming up was that the Underworld in CofD was much harsher, the ghosts tend to end up either trapped in the walls, losing their memories/identity, or forced to suffer the Old Laws of a Deep Dominion.<br /> <br /> As such it seems unlikely that there are many ghost even 500 years old... Nevermind multiple thousands.<br /> <br /> Becoming a reaper or Geist make sense in that context. I don't know if 2e changed anything or 1e introduced any ancient ghosts/geists. Or even ghosts who became kerberori.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Which begs the question, how would a ghost gain essence? Afaik there are three/four ways in the Underworld, dreging the rivers for essence containing objects, ectophagia, being remembered by the living, and following the rules of a deep dominion.<br /> <br /> It seems the first two are basically the same, gaining essence from other ghost/barghests/castoffs/(? mementos).<br /> <br /> Which raises a question for me, would a castoff of a famous building gain every time the living think of it? And come to think of it, will castoffs get absorbed into the Underworld (if they run out of essence) and retain their shape/become part of the background?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  correcting grammar 08-05-2023, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T07:34:51-07:00","id":1519858,"title":"","content":"That's my problem with my scenario as well, unless youre a Kerberoi surviving in the underworld long term is a difficult prospect. <br /> <br /> I'm not certain castoffs really gain essence, though I suppose they can since some seem capable of performing actions. I would say yes, they would gain essence from being remembered. <br /> <br /> Remember most cast offs are going into the underworld by default, a broken toy or discarded murder weapon are going to lack anchors allowing them to remain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T08:17:04-07:00","id":1519863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1519850#post1519850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which raises a question for me, would a castoff of a famous building gain every time the living think of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The operative words for gaining Essence from memory are grief and loss \u2014 the book is pretty explicit that it's the combined expectation of something to be there and the knowledge it won't be that shores up a ghost's self-image, and the sidebar on dead celebrities gives the distinctively not-tremendous rate of gain of one point of Essence per dot of Fame per week when Fame only goes to three dots and the ghost tends to lose a dot of Fame per posthumous decade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And come to think of it, will castoffs get absorbed into the Underworld (if they run out of essence) and retain their shape/become part of the background? </div> </div> </div>It was my impression that this was one of the reasons reasons navigating by architecture in the Upper Reaches is easier, though things smaller than buildings are more likely to drift down the rivers until they dissolve or are fished out and consumed (or turned into Mementos through whatever Underworld process causes that to happen).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T13:12:41-07:00","id":1519895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1519858#post1519858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's my problem with my scenario as well, unless youre a Kerberoi surviving in the underworld long term is a difficult prospect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't expect it to be that hard to survive long-term in a dead dominion. People overestimate how hostile they are to characters that aren't actively poking things with sticks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T14:05:40-07:00","id":1519899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1519863#post1519863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The operative words for gaining Essence from memory are grief and loss \u2014 the book is pretty explicit that it's the combined expectation of something to be there and the knowledge it won't be that shores up a ghost's self-image, and the sidebar on dead celebrities gives the distinctively not-tremendous rate of gain of one point of Essence per dot of Fame per week when Fame only goes to three dots and the ghost tends to lose a dot of Fame per posthumous decade.<br /> <br /> It was my impression that this was one of the reasons reasons navigating by architecture in the Upper Reaches is easier, though things smaller than buildings are more likely to drift down the rivers until they dissolve or are fished out and consumed (or turned into Mementos through whatever Underworld process causes that to happen).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so yes, that makes sense, many castoff buildings being out of essence and absorbed into the Underworld make the architecture there appear like the local architecture of the Upper Reaches (which is what is meant by Authchthonous Depths).<br /> <br /> That doesn't speak to what happens if they are getting essence from the living.<br /> <br /> 3 essence per week isn't going to prevent them being absorbed into the walls. When thinking about it, my prime example would always be the World Trade Centre Towers.<br /> <br /> From a mechanical point of view, they would definitely have left castoffs (as their destruction would have resulted in a number of breaking points, and integrity lost, so they would begin at rank 2). Further i suspect they would have anchors - even though that is unusual for castoffs. Lastly the question of how much essence they would gain, and i suspect the grief and loss associated with their destruction would result in more than enough essence for them to have kept filled to the brim.<br /> <br /> But given that this is an exceptional case (and i don't even think they would be in the Underworld - assuming my exception of them having anchors is valid), i think the amount of essence generated would not be reflective of the majority of castoffs, and infact there could well be narrative reasons to change any of these details if you were planning to include the Twin Towers in your campaign - i presume this is a topic which the Geist authors avoided making any canonical statements about - i am just trying to think through the consequences of the rules as written; even if my conclusion is that the rules allow for exceptions in exceptional cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  fixing typos 08-05-2023, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T14:33:13-07:00","id":1519902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1519899#post1519899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But given that this is an exceptional case (and i don't even think they would be in the Underworld - assuming my exception of them having anchors is valid), i think the amount of essence generated would not be reflective of the majority of castoffs, and infact there could well be narrative reasons to change any of these details if you we're planning to include the Twin Towers in your campaign - i presume this is a topic which the Geist auther avoided making any canonical statements about - i am just trying to think through the consequences of the rules as written; even if my conclusion is that the rules allow for exceptions in exceptional cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that NYC was the signature city for Geist 1e and considering the infamy of the WTC's destruction and the attendant death and trauma surrounding them, it seems self-evident that if one were to model the Twin Towers as one or more Castoffs they would be exceptional specimens unless one went out of the way to contrive a reason for them not to be.<br /> <br /> The operative fact is that the mechanical and narrative information presented about ghostly Essence makes it pretty clear that &quot;being remembered by the living&quot; is distinct from &quot;being thought about by the living at all.&quot; People who have only known about the basis of a ghost as a thing that is no longer present will not generate Essence just by thinking about it, because that's not feeling a loss; one could make a thematic case for ritualized mourning and memorializing fulfilling the same function as surviving kin missing their dead friend/neighbor/family member, but casual awareness that your grandmother used to have a beloved motorcycle will not reinforce the persisting image of that motorcycle in the manner of a person who rode it or saw it maintained momentarily forgetting (or wanting to forget) that it's gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T11:59:11-07:00","id":1521994,"title":"","content":"So you become a Sin-Eater when you die. And your Geist is a ghost.<br /> <br /> Say a parent dies from the supernatural, then like 10 or so years later, their kid\u2019s about to die from the supernatural (maybe the same thing?). Would it be \u201callowed\u201d for the kid to become a Sin-Eater (possibly mid-campaign) and/or for the parent to become their kid\u2019s Geist?<br /> <br /> Or would that create complications?<br /> <br /> Idea: Pre-fallen Demon kills the parent in front of the child. Fast forward, child is about to do a self-sacrifice thing. Parents spirit be like \u201cnope, not your time\u201d and the child then wakes up either where they fell or in a body bag (or, more humorously, their casket right before the service starts).<br /> <br /> I know the rules about swapping merits and any supernatural merits would be void. I\u2019m more so wondering \u201ccould this happen in a game, or would the parent-child dynamics mess something up\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T12:20:02-07:00","id":1521996,"title":"","content":"It could happen, but there are problems with it. To become a Geist a ghost has to drink from the rivers of the underworld. Drinking from those rivers pretty much erased a large amount of the Geist's identity. That's part of playing Geist: Sin Eaters, unlocking your Geist's past and lost memories. <br /> <br /> What I would do is have the Geist be a more generic &quot;The Mother&quot; and maybe later part of uncovering her memories involves seeking out her child and protecting him or her from the demon that killed her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T12:57:28-07:00","id":1522002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>firestar001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1521994#post1521994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say a parent dies from the supernatural, then like 10 or so years later, their kid\u2019s about to die from the supernatural (maybe the same thing?). Would it be \u201callowed\u201d for the kid to become a Sin-Eater (possibly mid-campaign) and/or for the parent to become their kid\u2019s Geist?<br /> <br /> Or would that create complications?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being Broken and having a Remembrance instead of Anchors means a geist is going to have a very difficult time with communication both coming and going, as well as being recognized as the person they used to be, but nothing strictly prevents &quot;my geist is secretly my parent who died all those years ago&quot; as a story beat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T14:34:45-07:00","id":1522011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1521996#post1521996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could happen, but there are problems with it. To become a Geist a ghost has to drink from the rivers of the underworld. Drinking from those rivers pretty much erased a large amount of the Geist's identity. That's part of playing Geist: Sin Eaters, unlocking your Geist's past and lost memories.<br /> <br /> What I would do is have the Geist be a more generic &quot;The Mother&quot; and maybe later part of uncovering her memories involves seeking out her child and protecting him or her from the demon that killed her.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you said \u2018The Mother\u2019 I\u2019ve immediately thought of this obscure but interesting game called \u201cOthercide\u201d. It\u2019s a BIT Geist-ish in dealing with memories and lovecraftian enemies. <br /> <br /> <br /> But thanks, I\u2019ll need to reread the Geist book again. Didn\u2019t think it would be as easy as I\u2019d hoped, but I\u2019m glad the idea has some interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-17T19:07:33-07:00","id":1532790,"title":"","content":"On my Forgotten English Calendar; the word of the day is, &quot;Sin-Eater&quot;, Welsh, someone that would come to the house of the dead and eat food, thereby cleansing their sins. -1930","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T04:51:16-07:00","id":1536152,"title":"","content":"Is there any conversion guide for Geist 1st edition to 2ed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T07:02:03-07:00","id":1536982,"title":"","content":"2 questions:<br /> <br /> First, would it be possible to have a geist that's a:<br /> <br /> A: Non-Homo Sapiens Human<br /> <br /> B: Baby<br /> <br /> C: Conjoined Twins<br /> <br /> Second, what would he appropriate rememberance traits for a baby geist, if it's possible to make one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T19:28:11-07:00","id":1537051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1536982#post1536982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 questions:<br /> <br /> First, would it be possible to have a geist that's a:<br /> <br /> A: Non-Homo Sapiens Human<br /> <br /> B: Baby<br /> <br /> C: Conjoined Twins<br /> <br /> Second, what would he appropriate rememberance traits for a baby geist, if it's possible to make one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything is possible if your storyteller agrees. Discuss it with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T11:53:30-07:00","id":1537094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1536982#post1536982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 questions:<br /> <br /> First, would it be possible to have a geist that's a:<br /> <br /> A: Non-Homo Sapiens Human<br /> <br /> B: Baby<br /> <br /> C: Conjoined Twins<br /> <br /> Second, what would he appropriate rememberance traits for a baby geist, if it's possible to make one?</div> </div> </div> </div>A: As long as it has the intelligence needed to offer the bargain sure, but a ghost so ancient would have a very difficult to resolve Remembrance i think<br /> <br /> B: I would say at least a 6 year old baby, younger ones simply lack the degree of self awareness needed to survive the underworld and offer a bargain<br /> <br /> C: It would be very interesting.<br /> Both surely has to be died togheter, but it is unlikely that they both could drink from the river at the same time.<br /> The still rank 2 ghost could act as a parasite, or mesh grotesquely with the Geist","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T07:45:06-07:00","id":1538479,"title":"","content":"Can Bound have babies? I know that the child wouldn't be another Bound, but could a Bound still reproduce?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T09:24:20-07:00","id":1538481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1538479#post1538479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Bound have babies? I know that the child wouldn't be another Bound, but could a Bound still reproduce?</div> </div> </div> </div>They've got functioning biology and there hasn't been any statement in the books that they no longer have the ability to reproduce, so it would be a reasonable assumption that they can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T11:55:53-07:00","id":1538484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1536982#post1536982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">B: Baby<br /> <br /> C: Conjoined Twins</div> </div> </div> </div>The ghost of a baby isn't going to have the intelligence to offer the Bargain, or honestly to survive the Underworld very long to become a geist in the first place.<br /> Conjoined twins are two people. They're going to leave two ghosts, not one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1538479#post1538479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Bound have babies? I know that the child wouldn't be another Bound, but could a Bound still reproduce?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, the Bound can have children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T10:33:03-07:00","id":1539426,"title":"","content":"A question that I don't think has been addressed - maybe everyone else just knows the answer.<br /> <br /> A Krewe has two- and three-dot free Ceremonies per archetype - but it starts at Esotery 1, which caps Mystery Cult Initiation at 1, which means celebrants can't actually access those Ceremonies until the Krewe's Esotery rises. Also Bestow Regalia, but an Esotery 1 Krewe doesn't actually have any Regalia to bestow. Is that right? Are the free Ceremonies sitting there, doing nothing, waiting for you to raise Esotery?<br /> <br /> And following from that...<br /> <br /> Should characters who personally learn &quot;latent&quot; free Ceremonies get their Experiences back when they get those Ceremonies through Esotery and Initiation? Should the same apply to bought Krewe Ceremonies replacing bought personal Ceremonies as Esotery rises? Do bought personal Ceremonies just <i>become </i>Krewe Ceremonies when Esotery gets high enough? Should there be a partial Experience refund if more than one member of the Krewe had the Ceremony as a personal Ceremony?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-23T03:39:15-07:00","id":1540934,"title":"","content":"How many people do actually leave a ghost behind? Is there a rule, or a quote, stating at least some kind of proportion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-23T04:55:50-07:00","id":1540937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1540934#post1540934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many people do actually leave a ghost behind? Is there a rule, or a quote, stating at least some kind of proportion?</div> </div> </div> </div>The ghost section is pretty unambiguously stated as &quot;whenever something is destroyed,&quot; with notes that &quot;something&quot; includes people and that most ghostly objects only last a few seconds before they're swept into the Underworld, and with the implicit caveat that if a person has Integrity 10 they won't leave a ghost (the Rank of a typical ghost created from a person's death being 1 if they had Integrity 1-6 or 2 if they had Integrity 7-9).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-23T08:11:47-07:00","id":1540939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1540934#post1540934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many people do actually leave a ghost behind? Is there a rule, or a quote, stating at least some kind of proportion?</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems ghosts are one of the most common supernatural phenomena. In part because doppelgangers (ghosts that exist while the original lives) can be generated from near death experiences. Anyone who dies in a particularly traumatizing way, or with many attachments or unresolved issues will likely generate a ghost from how strongly those emotions imprint unto Death attuned ephemera. One thing from that stuck out to me was that the first person buried in a graveyard will inevitably rise as a Rank 3 ghost (core book page 200), as the guardian of the area and potential partner in the Bargain, which makes it feel that its so common that the supernatural ecosystem already accounts for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T16:16:49-07:00","id":1541037,"title":"","content":"Can Sin-Eaters see in the dark? Do they have an ability to see in the dark either by their ability to see into Twilight or some Haunt I missed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25650-jacook03","name":"Jacook03","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25650_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T19:23:38-07:00","id":1541049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacook03</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1541037#post1541037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Sin-Eaters see in the dark? Do they have an ability to see in the dark either by their ability to see into Twilight or some Haunt I missed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Closest thing is the Boneyard's awareness and anti-stealth effects. Sin-Eaters perceive ghosts in Twilight the same as they would ordinary people, but that doesn't make it any harder for ghosts to physically hide from them (they aren't lit from within or anything like that, and obvious mutilation is a function of trauma and/or occult curiosities like geisthood or Iconography Merits).<br /> <br /> The Caul's ability to substitute your geist's Attributes can help offset penalties from darkness, and you might interpret the Shroud rendering you unable to be blinded or deafened by non-supernatural means as allowing you to ignore penalties from mundane darkness, but there is no power on the books that just outright says &quot;Sin-Eaters can see in the dark.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T08:14:07-07:00","id":1541062,"title":"","content":"Fun question, talking with a player about the Boneyard Haunt, and since objects are &quot;infused with a small amount of the Sin-Eater's awareness&quot; could a Sin-Eater use a radio, or television, or etch-a-sketch, or fridge magnets, etc., to communicate with someone else in the Boneyard? Follow up, if they had Shroud and were in Twilight, can you use Boneyard to perform that communication without being seen?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25650-jacook03","name":"Jacook03","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25650_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T08:55:46-07:00","id":1541064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacook03</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1541062#post1541062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun question, talking with a player about the Boneyard Haunt, and since objects are &quot;infused with a small amount of the Sin-Eater's awareness&quot; could a Sin-Eater use a radio, or television, or etch-a-sketch, or fridge magnets, etc., to communicate with someone else in the Boneyard?</div> </div> </div> </div>With the caveat that the poltergeist activity afforded by the Boneyard Tilt seems to be limited to mechanical effects and thus you wouldn't be able to do something as non-spooky as a normal audio/video call mediated through a radio or television, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Follow up, if they had Shroud and were in Twilight, can you use Boneyard to perform that communication without being seen? </div> </div> </div>The Shroud Condition specifically ends if you use another Haunt or draw attention to yourself","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T10:27:56-07:00","id":1541594,"title":"","content":"I know it states it somewhere in the book, but I can't seem to find it. How long does the plasm last after a ghost materializes? I believe it is a chapter, but I could be wrong. I'm pretty sure that I read a when a ghost materializes it leaves an amount of Plasm equal to the essence spent to materialize, but I can't seem to find where it states how long is lasts, lol much less how the Sin-Eater collects it ... like scooping it up to put in his pocket and slap on his sandwich later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25650-jacook03","name":"Jacook03","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25650_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T12:13:54-07:00","id":1541597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacook03</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1541594#post1541594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it states it somewhere in the book, but I can't seem to find it. How long does the plasm last after a ghost materializes? I believe it is a chapter, but I could be wrong. I'm pretty sure that I read a when a ghost materializes it leaves an amount of Plasm equal to the essence spent to materialize, but I can't seem to find where it states how long is lasts, lol much less how the Sin-Eater collects it ... like scooping it up to put in his pocket and slap on his sandwich later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the notes on Using Plasm (p96), coating something in Plasm makes it Open to all ghosts until the end of the chapter or until it's washed off, and per the &quot;Plasm Creation&quot; note in the Manifestations section on page 191 Plasm created by the manifestation of a ghost also lasts until the end of the chapter. Plasm left behind in the trails of chthonians (p198) likewise evaporates at the end of the chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T12:52:43-07:00","id":1541598,"title":"","content":"As always, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25650-jacook03","name":"Jacook03","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25650_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-21T01:43:10-08:00","id":1548658,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have any idea who the Hermit on the beach is?<br /> <br /> I was reading the 2e core book and at the Ocean of Fragments, there's mention of a hermit who lives on the shore. I was struck by the similarity of concept to the Other who lives on the shore of the Abyss in <i>Astral Realms</i>, and I was curious if that was a deliberate parallel or not. (Keep in mind that the Other is itself a reference, at least in description, to Voormas from <i>Ascension</i>.)<br /> <br /> So I decided to look up <i>Book of the Dead</i> to see if there's more information, and yeah, with more detail they're more clearly distinguished characters. But, there's a new mystery:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He claims he used to be king of something, and that vast armies of powerful monsters served him. But how would he know? </div> </div> </div>It could be nothing, it's very vague, but that sounds like a reference. Does anyone remember any of the writers mentioning it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-07T00:34:51-08:00","id":1549043,"title":"","content":"Does a Sin eater honorary rank count versus other sin eater as a Bane (for Haunts or for damage)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-07T06:47:13-08:00","id":1549048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1549043#post1549043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a Sin eater honorary rank count versus other sin eater as a Bane (for Haunts or for damage)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honorary Rank never counts against things that aren't the ephemeral being it's an honorary Rank of. Much as powerful spirits aren't the Bane of werewolves, a Sin-Eater with e.g. Synergy 1 does not take aggravated damage from the unmodified unarmed attacks of a Synergy 3+ Sin-Eater.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T10:10:31-07:00","id":1549408,"title":"","content":"Ghosts who drink from the rivers of a Underworld gain 1 rank.<br /> <br /> Imbibing: Drinking from a River inflicts 1 aggravated wound per turn for (10 - Integrity) turns, but also increases a ghost\u2019s Rank by 1.<br /> <br /> What prevents them from drinking (always after healing) until they gain the maximum rank?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T11:29:25-07:00","id":1549409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1549408#post1549408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts who drink from the rivers of a Underworld gain 1 rank.<br /> <br /> Imbibing: Drinking from a River inflicts 1 aggravated wound per turn for (10 - Integrity) turns, but also increases a ghost\u2019s Rank by 1.<br /> <br /> What prevents them from drinking (always after healing) until they gain the maximum rank?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Taking aggravated damage also saps their Essence and in the Underworld that's at a premium, particularly given that drinking from a River is a breaking point that can lower a ghost's Integrity; higher Integrity equating to higher starting Rank likewise doesn't undo the fact that most Rank 2 ghosts who end up in the Underworld will have undergone at least two breaking points by the time they get to a River.<br /> <br /> Also, while there's no mechanical representation of this beyond Broken and Iconic and the Remembrance, becoming a geist tends to scramble the memory a little bit. There's a reason Cabeiros requires a Bound to <i>force</i> their geist to drink more.<br /> <br /> Finally, the fact that all the powers you get with Rank cost Essence to use and the Underworld is not a great place to maintain Essence above subsistence-level means most intelligent ghosts are going to view &quot;turn myself inside-out for magical powers&quot; as a last resort after failing to hack it in the River Cities or sifting the Upper Reaches, possibly after having had to resort to less savory forms of ectophagia.<br /> <br /> By the time you're in a frame of mind for it to start looking like a good idea you're sidling up to a body of water that quickly knocks out any ghost that falls in and deposits them on the shores <s>to be left unconscious unless force-fed Plasm or other ghostly Corpus (or given Essence some other way)</s>, with the specific goal of doing something that will likely consume at least a third of the Essence you can hold in the process of scouring at least half of your Health away (which will take the better part of a month to heal with rest).<br /> <br /> Like, yes, the river is full of free mutagen. Most sane people will still not want to drink it more than once if they can help it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  No dormancy in the Underworld. 06-06-2026, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T11:31:55-07:00","id":1549410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1549408#post1549408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts who drink from the rivers of a Underworld gain 1 rank.<br /> <br /> Imbibing: Drinking from a River inflicts 1 aggravated wound per turn for (10 - Integrity) turns, but also increases a ghost\u2019s Rank by 1.<br /> <br /> What prevents them from drinking (always after healing) until they gain the maximum rank?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts still have to buy with exp first the Attribute levels minimum for a new rank AND then also buy the rank while drinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T12:36:38-07:00","id":1549412,"title":"","content":"Perfect, thank you for the answers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-18T05:25:07-07:00","id":1550237,"title":"","content":"I ve problems understanding the Labyrinth Dominion (memento mori book)<br /> -what does the third law actually means?<br /> -what kind of things are laws trasgressors allowed to write to make amend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-18T08:51:43-07:00","id":1550240,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Neos01</a> I take it the third law is referring to the instructions written on the walls: &quot;...the order to travel deeper...&quot;<br /> <br /> As for what they can write: instructions for getting out. The caveat is that firstly the Bull sends you to a random part of the labyrinth, so you don't actually know the way out. Secondly, law 1 includes disfiguring the walls, so presumably writing anything that the Bull doesn't approve of counts as an additional violation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T19:28:25-07:00","id":1550927,"title":"","content":"Is there something akin to personal Archetypes, or just Krewe ones? Also, is there anything similar to Vampire Bloodlines, Mage Legacy or Changeling Entitlement for Geists? Any edition would do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-11T03:05:31-07:00","id":1550934,"title":"","content":"The 1st edition of Geist had something called a Channel. It involved the Krewe triggering their Geists' transformation into a conceptually deeper form. However, the details of that process rubbed many people the wrong way. Here is a link to an argument over that fact:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/133915-sin-eater-history-and-background-expansion-fluff-houserules\">LINK</a><br /> <br /> The 2nd edition seemed to go the opposite direction, where the &quot;natural&quot; progress of a Sin-Eater's Geist is to regain its humanity, rather than drifting away from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-11T06:42:45-07:00","id":1550939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1550927#post1550927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there something akin to personal Archetypes, or just Krewe ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically, your Root and Bloom (and, to a lesser degree, your krewe's Virtue and Creed) fill the role that Archetype did in 1e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, is there anything similar to Vampire Bloodlines, Mage Legacy or Changeling Entitlement for Geists? Any edition would do. </div> </div> </div>Structurally, your krewe Archetype is your characters' shared Y-splat and developing the krewe further is used for that type of character refinement; individually, your character's Remembrance provides the kind of accumulative semi-personalized bonuses a bloodline, Legacy, or entitlement would provide, with Krewe Regalia filling in the gaps somewhat; simply raising your Synergy won't make your crisis point trigger narrower or give you access to Plasm-powered Skills and Merits, nor will it allow you to temporarily boost your Rank, enhance Skill rolls, or gain new Keys.<br /> <br /> Similar to how in Promethean 2e Athanors were changed from a Z-splat to material keys to the Azothic Memory that facilitate Promethean characters going through the Pilgrimage with less of a direct line of tutelage required (and the effects of the New Dawn are more mechanically defined), and similar to how in Demon the Cipher is an optional method of diving deeper into mystical secrets for a splat with an incentive to stay under the radar and an inclination to think in terms of purpose, and similar to how the core Deviant template is incredibly bare-bones in no small part because it's sharing bookspace with the most mechanically involved version of the organization mechanics, Geist 2e takes the tack that when you are playing a character whose specific driving goals are to resolve at least one of two personal quests so there's nothing making you especially regret dying before your time, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1235166-2e-hack-archetypes-as-y-splats-not-krewe?p=1277499#post1277499\">a specific separate character development axis with a fully separate purpose from your Burden, Remembrance, and krewe Doctrine is kind of beyond the scope of need for a typical PC.</a><br /> <br /> In 1e, as Teatime notes, expanding your krewe's channel allows it to double as a Z-splat as well as a player group, built out like one would a Hunter conspiracy with a side of weird syncretic mythology, and expand it as one would expect for a death cult powered in part by initiated headcount.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-11-2025, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-04T07:24:21-07:00","id":1552056,"title":"","content":"Ghosts are solid in the Underworld by default (rather than in Twilight form) so what happens to a Geist when the Sin-eater it is no is bound to enters the Underworld?<br /> <br /> Wait, do Geists typically hoover around in twilight otherwise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-04T10:30:48-07:00","id":1552058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1552056#post1552056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts are solid in the Underworld by default (rather than in Twilight form) so what happens to a Geist when the Sin-eater it is no is bound to enters the Underworld?<br /> <br /> Wait, do Geists typically hoover around in twilight otherwise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, in pages 58 and 76 it states they hover in Twilight by default. The main difference is that a Sin-Eater makes the area around them feel more real, more clear, more alive for the dead (see <i>Liminal Aura</i> is page 99), so I imagine that even with the minor god of death hanging around them, a Sin-Eater's presence is distinctive in the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-04T11:06:02-07:00","id":1552059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1552056#post1552056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts are solid in the Underworld by default (rather than in Twilight form) so what happens to a Geist when the Sin-eater it is no is bound to enters the Underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>It remains intangible but may be visible, per the &quot;On the Leash&quot; sidebar on Page 100.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-05T12:44:17-07:00","id":1552077,"title":"","content":"Ok, so unless unleashed they remain in place (where the soul usually is) and aren't tangible in twilight only a projection, so not like a ghost to being with.<br /> <br /> That means Unleashing them in the Underworld must be uncomfortable...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-05T15:07:41-07:00","id":1552080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1552077#post1552077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That means Unleashing them in the Underworld must be uncomfortable...</div> </div> </div> </div>Unleashing means the geist is Materialized regardless, so not substantially more uncomfortable than normal for hitting a crisis point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-06T01:33:58-07:00","id":1552095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1552080#post1552080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unleashing means the geist is Materialized regardless, so not substantially more uncomfortable than normal for hitting a crisis point.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I mean when it is materializing, if it isn't the projection into twilight but actually within the Bound's soul-hole (whatever you call the slot a soul usually goes in) then being material while unleashing seems painful. Not while unleashed, that would be normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-06T05:56:59-07:00","id":1552099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1552095#post1552095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I mean when it is materializing, if it isn't the projection into twilight but actually within the Bound's soul-hole (whatever you call the slot a soul usually goes in) then being material while unleashing seems painful. Not while unleashed, that would be normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always figured unleashing as the Sin eater extruding Plasm that coalesce in the Geist form, so i think that no matter where you are the sensation is the same","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-06T06:43:36-07:00","id":1552101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1552095#post1552095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I mean when it is materializing, if it isn't the projection into twilight but actually within the Bound's soul-hole (whatever you call the slot a soul usually goes in) then being material while unleashing seems painful. Not while unleashed, that would be normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>The geist only Materializes when Unleashed. The sidebar I mentioned specifies that the normal projection is immaterial even in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Unleashing forms a body for the geist out of Plasm, which is ostensibly no more uncomfortable than extruding Plasm normally save that Unleashing without a crisis trigger deprives you of your ability to spend Plasm for the scene (or two scenes if the geist is discorporated).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-11T07:12:53-07:00","id":1553061,"title":"","content":"What is the relationship, if any, between The Other, Aeon of Paradox in the Astral; and The Hermit of the Black Beach in the Underworld?<br /> <br /> The thematic associations are strong: friendly, old man of indistinct ethnicity, in the shore of a large endless waterbody of dissolution (Ocean of Oroboros, Ocean of Fragments).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-11T11:00:53-07:00","id":1553067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1553061#post1553061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the relationship, if any, between The Other, Aeon of Paradox in the Astral; and The Hermit of the Black Beach in the Underworld?<br /> <br /> The thematic associations are strong: friendly, old man of indistinct ethnicity, in the shore of a large endless waterbody of dissolution (Ocean of Oroboros, Ocean of Fragments).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not specified in any way. It's a thematic overlap with no elaboration made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T18:54:59-08:00","id":1556686,"title":"","content":"In my Mage campaign, we are dealing with ghouls and revenants. Revenants not being the Vampire kind but the kind that are people who don't die and basically possess their own bodies. Do Geists/Bound deal with these things and how functionally different are they from each other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27121-hyuse","name":"Hyuse","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T19:35:00-08:00","id":1556692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyuse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1556686#post1556686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my Mage campaign, we are dealing with ghouls and revenants. Revenants not being the Vampire kind but the kind that are people who don't die and basically possess their own bodies. Do Geists/Bound deal with these things and how functionally different are they from each other?</div> </div> </div> </div>Geist assumes that every ghost who has not descended to the Underworld has their body or their gravesite as one of their Anchors and provides a Merit for Absent characters (ghosts who trade for Memories to supplement their more conventional means of gaining Essence and serve as the gameline's secondary playable character type much as ghouls in Vampire or wolf-blooded in Werewolf) that models being bound to one's own dead body in a more enduring fashion than the scene at a time that the Possession Manifestation allows, which gives the character Health instead of Corpus and requires the consumption of a substantial amount of raw meat (or a smaller amount of raw human meat) per week for upkeep and healing, as well as requiring the character spend Willpower to interact with other people socially.<br /> <br /> Outside of those contexts, there's the well-known capacity for ghosts to simply Possess a dead body (whether their own or, if they're a geist, a body whose means of death matches their innate Key) on a limited basis and any stranger phenomena that don't have consistent mechanics to model them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T19:43:10-08:00","id":1556740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyuse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1556686#post1556686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Geists/Bound deal with these things and how functionally different are they from each other?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1556692#post1556692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside of those contexts, there's the well-known capacity for ghosts to simply Possess a dead body (whether their own or, if they're a geist, a body whose means of death matches their innate Key) on a limited basis and <b><u>any stranger phenomena that don't have consistent mechanics to model them</u></b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bold by me, this, a lot of attention to this.<br /> <br /> There's a number of distinct ways to have &quot;Revenants&quot; in the setting already covered, and a heavy implication that this isn't a particularly uncommon result for weird phenomena.<br /> <br /> Which means, for the second question, that it isn't straightforward to state how they functionally differ. Each Revenant may follow rules with significant distinctions in any aspect. A commonality that you'll find is a lack of natural healing and some form of decay over time, but even those can't be guaranteed. Revenants <i><b>usually</b></i> don't have many powers beyond their physical bodies and whatever they do to heal and/or come back, but then again, no consistent, general rules.<br /> <br /> For the first question, yes, though what &quot;deal&quot; means depends. But yes, since those are usually ghosts possessing bodies, they're within the purview of the Bound, and if if one isn't the Bound won't know without a proper investigation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-23T06:08:45-07:00","id":1558972,"title":"","content":"Are listed somewhere examples of ghosts passing on without the Ceremony?<br /> I need to know if it s &quot;natural&quot; enough to be replicated by a Mage Death 1 spell","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-23T07:34:12-07:00","id":1558974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1558972#post1558972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are listed somewhere examples of ghosts passing on without the Ceremony?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are not, and the mechanics of resolving all your Anchors is just that you become a valid target for the Ceremony, but despite its rating Pass On is comparatively common.<br /> <br /> Presumably Fallen Worlds would have helped bridge the gap between Mage and Geist for this in addition to porting the correlation between ghostly Rank and Integrity-at-time-of-death, but for the time being it's probably safest to assume something that requires magic to properly happen (or, in the case of a geist, fulfillment of both a Remembrance and a Burden) would be the domain of a Ruling spell at minimum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-25T15:58:45-07:00","id":1559625,"title":"","content":"So, question: As Vampires have their Masquerade, Werewolves have their Lunacy and Changelings have the Keepers and Huntsmen to worry about, it makes sense that those factions would try their best to stay hidden from the &quot;mundane&quot; world.<br /> <br /> But, as far as I can tell, there really isn't anything of that nature stopping the Bound from advertising who they are and their services? Like, obviously if they put an ad in the yellow pages about being a medium, most people would just assume they were quacks. But what I'm asking is, <u><b>is there any in-universe reason why the Bound would try to cover up their actions, existence or powers?</b></u>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-25T17:18:55-07:00","id":1559626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1559625#post1559625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, question: As Vampires have their Masquerade, Werewolves have their Lunacy and Changelings have the Keepers and Huntsmen to worry about, it makes sense that those factions would try their best to stay hidden from the &quot;mundane&quot; world.<br /> <br /> But, as far as I can tell, there really isn't anything of that nature stopping the Bound from advertising who they are and their services? Like, obviously if they put an ad in the yellow pages about being a medium, most people would just assume they were quacks. But what I'm asking is, <u><b>is there any in-universe reason why the Bound would try to cover up their actions, existence or powers?</b></u></div> </div> </div> </div>The Underworld is shaped by ghosts, ghosts contain human memory of death and trauma more generally, and the ghosts that are most likely to become part of the foundations of the Underworld are the less functional ones created by the deaths of people who experienced traumatic events, of which exposure to the supernatural is a significant example.<br /> <br /> This is a major part of why the Undertakers exist as an Archetype opposite to Necropolitans: by dint of basic entropy, the unquiet dead having greater exposure in human culture worsens the signal-to-noise ratio of the tides of life and death in ways that passively and actively confound efforts to make things better, not least by introducing more chaos for Reapers to exploit. Even if you aren't part of a krewe of Sin-Eaters with ambitions of turning the Underworld into something more benign, working openly as a supernatural entity means more people can get a somewhat accurate impression of what you can do and have opinions about it that they can act on.<br /> <br /> Ghosts have the ability to steal Memories now, which adds a vector for cleanup that didn't consistently exist in 1e's presentation, but &quot;throwing big rocks into dark waters risks capsizing your boat&quot; is a general operational principle that guides most supernatural societies with staying power in Chronicles regardless of what type of monster populates them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-25T06:26:14-07:00","id":1562141,"title":"","content":"Question about Remembrance Traits:<br /> <br /> Say a Sin-Eater has Synergy 1, their Geist is Rank 3, and has Sympathetic (\u2022\u2022) as their Remembrance Trait.<br /> <br /> Given that \u201cSin-Eaters have an effective ghost Rank (p. 187) equal to the lower of Synergy or her geist\u2019s Rank\u201d (97),<br /> <br /> and \u201cPlasm Cost: Spend Plasm to gain dots in the Trait, up to the Sin-Eater\u2019s effective Rank\u201d,<br /> <br /> \u201dAll or Nothing: For Merits with a fixed dot cost, you must spend enough Plasm to gain all the Merit\u2019s dots in order to benefit from it\u201d (100),<br /> <br /> is it correct that this Sin-Eater could not use their Geist\u2019s Remembrance Trait until they raised their Synergy to 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28872-csctnfire","user":"csctnfire","date":". 07-25-2026, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28872-csctnfire","name":"csctnfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-25T09:32:56-07:00","id":1562147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>csctnfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1562141#post1562141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about Remembrance Traits:<br /> <br /> Say a Sin-Eater has Synergy 1, their Geist is Rank 3, and has Sympathetic (\u2022\u2022) as their Remembrance Trait.<br /> <br /> Given that \u201cSin-Eaters have an effective ghost Rank (p. 187) equal to the lower of Synergy or her geist\u2019s Rank\u201d (97),<br /> <br /> and \u201cPlasm Cost: Spend Plasm to gain dots in the Trait, up to the Sin-Eater\u2019s effective Rank\u201d,<br /> <br /> \u201dAll or Nothing: For Merits with a fixed dot cost, you must spend enough Plasm to gain all the Merit\u2019s dots in order to benefit from it\u201d (100),<br /> <br /> is it correct that this Sin-Eater could not use their Geist\u2019s Remembrance Trait until they raised their Synergy to 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Most initial Remembrance Traits are Skills or scaled Social Merits for this reason, though the Eminence Krewe Regalia can temporarily increase your effective Rank by 1 without spending personal Experiences or raising Synergy, and you raise your effective Synergy by 2 while pursuing one of your Touchstones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-06-2026, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T18:48:05-07:00","id":1563482,"title":"","content":"Some general questions relating to Regalia:<br /> <br /> The Regalia Condition says to think about how a particular Regalia appears when it's first created (and rename the Condition) \u2014 are Regalia visible in the same way as Haunts are (determined by the Sin-Eater), only visible to those who can see ghosts, third thing?<br /> <br /> Can you use the &quot;innate&quot; Key provided by the Power Regalia Effect to create a Memento the same way you could more permanent innate Keys provided by other means?<br /> <br /> Does the &quot;for the duration of a scene&quot; stipulation on the Power Regalia Effect mean that the Key can only be accessed for one scene per chapter/application of the Condition? If so, does the voluntary resolution method still work if used after that scene? Does the access to the Key kick in immediately or can the character wait to cash it in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}